{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5","id":1369651,"title":"Should Kuei-Jin be in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-22T14:28:00-08:00","id":1369651,"title":"Should Kuei-Jin be in V5?","content":"This topic came up in the Ravnos thread; I considered posting there but I think it's a separate issue, even if they may be absent for a similar reason. As I mentioned somewhere before, not much has been said so far about South, East and Southeast Asia*, apart from Japan, Hecata and at least a statement about the Ministry. To me, that looks like a vast, half-the-biggest-continent spanning &quot;TBD&quot;.<br /> <br /> I like a lot about the Kuei-Jin. If they are replaced with Cainites, I still want the dharmas preserved, not necessarily as Paths, and explanation of how the Camarilla arrived in Japan (and where ever else).<br /> <br /> *I'm also curious about the Golden Courts further afield in Oceania, but that's stretching the pan-Asian splat further again (depending on how one writes the Golden Courts) and how many vampires could there be on the Pacific islands anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T14:40:45-08:00","id":1369660,"title":"","content":"I think they should be replaced with new, previously unknown, Kindred Clans.<br /> <br /> Ones that COULD be an offshoot of existing clans but are possibly not.<br /> <br /> Jiangshi could be Cappadocians for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T15:31:05-08:00","id":1369675,"title":"","content":"Should Vampires other than Kindred be in the game? Yes, if you can find a myth arc for them, having something totally other, inspired by different myths, competing to fill the same or similar predatory niche could be really interesting, could the Kuei-Jin be reworked into that? Unknown,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T15:36:26-08:00","id":1369677,"title":"","content":"With the proper reworking I would like for them to be in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T15:42:18-08:00","id":1369679,"title":"","content":"At the very least, retcon out Tou Mu as an evil spirit. We don't need to be copying off of D&amp;D's paper. Especially not when even D&amp;D seems to have realized that it was a mistake before KotE even came along (unless there was some place in 2e other than Legends and Lore where she would have shown up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-22-2020, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:00:45-08:00","id":1369683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369675#post1369675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Vampires other than Kindred be in the game? Yes, if you can find a myth arc for them, having something totally other, inspired by different myths, competing to fill the same or similar predatory niche could be really interesting, could the Kuei-Jin be reworked into that? Unknown,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest issue (which I explained in the Ravnos thread) is the fact the Kuei-Jin prevent Asian gamers from being able to enjoy V:TM in their home nations. If you want to play sexy vampires, snooty nobleman, and raged-out Anarchs--which is pretty much why anyone would play the V:TM game to begin with--the Kuei-Jin take up half of the planet and say they kill all of them and prevent them from establishing themselves.<br /> <br /> And the Kuei-Jin don't fill that role either.<br /> <br /> In a way much worse than the Assamites, Ravnos, or Setites are in racial issues because at least you can play a Camarilla court in India.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:19:11-08:00","id":1369687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369683#post1369683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the biggest issue (which I explained in the Ravnos thread) is the fact the Kuei-Jin prevent Asian gamers from being able to enjoy V:TM in their home nations. If you want to play sexy vampires, snooty nobleman, and raged-out Anarchs--which is pretty much why anyone would play the V:TM game to begin with--the Kuei-Jin take up half of the planet and say they kill all of them and prevent them from establishing themselves.<br /> <br /> And the Kuei-Jin don't fill that role either.<br /> <br /> In a way much worse than the Assamites, Ravnos, or Setites are in racial issues because at least you can play a Camarilla court in India.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and we had other people in that thread saying that they wanted the other mythical creatures, just done better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:21:27-08:00","id":1369688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369687#post1369687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and we had other people in that thread saying that they wanted the other mythical creatures, just done better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe but I think there's a fundamental disconnect because the Kuei Jin should have been their own splat.<br /> <br /> While they drink blood and are undead, they're closer to Wraith or Demon: The Fallen than Kindred.<br /> <br /> So when you deal with adapting the myth, there's no real reason for the Kuei Jin to ever interact with the Cainites anymore than the Werewolves or Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:29:29-08:00","id":1369692,"title":"","content":"I think you could have 'Kuei-Jin' (the name) in V5. Whether you could have things as depicted in KotE in V5 is another matter entirely. Given the discussions I've seen of that (and Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, for that matter) the answer is 'hell no' and you're probably better off treating them all as variations of the same creature (even if they don't have a different origin point - eg they descend from some other being than 'Caine').<br /> <br /> This would be a reversion to an earlier approach to such things (which may have had its own problems - I'm not qualified to judge that) but its not impossible, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:49:47-08:00","id":1369695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369688#post1369688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe but I think there's a fundamental disconnect because the Kuei Jin should have been their own splat.<br /> <br /> While they drink blood and are undead, they're closer to Wraith or Demon: The Fallen than Kindred.<br /> <br /> So when you deal with adapting the myth, there's no real reason for the Kuei Jin to ever interact with the Cainites anymore than the Werewolves or Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that they would be in direct competition for pray, that's the conflict right there, you can add in geopolitical rivalries etc, but it's two undead predators scrapping over the herd at its core. Making the territories less monolithic would be a very good idea mind, something the new promise could have been, but really wasn't, how you would fit in mixing those hunting ranges with established lore, well, not impossible, but tricky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:52:40-08:00","id":1369696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369695#post1369695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that they would be in direct competition for pray, that's the conflict right there, you can add in geopolitical rivalries etc, but it's two undead predators scrapping over the herd at its core. Making the territories less monolithic would be a very good idea mind, something the new promise could have been, but really wasn't, how you would fit in mixing those hunting ranges with established lore, well, not impossible, but tricky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, the Kuei Jin books are very clear about how little the Hunger matters to them. The demphasis of it from flesh and blood to Ki I felt robbed them of an interesting angle.<br /> <br /> The game is more about fighting demons I think. Which means I would think they'd regularly encounter Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:57:10-08:00","id":1369699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369696#post1369696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, the Kuei Jin books are very clear about how little the Hunger matters to them. The demphasis of it from flesh and blood to Ki I felt robbed them of an interesting angle.<br /> <br /> The game is more about fighting demons I think. Which means I would think they'd regularly encounter Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Given how overwhelming the hunger is in v5, crowding out humanity/path and politics, as it constantly gatecrashes the game.. Having vampires not being hammered into the ground by it would be a relief <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T17:02:03-08:00","id":1369701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369699#post1369699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly. Given how overwhelming the hunger is in v5, crowding out humanity/path and politics, as it constantly gatecrashes the game.. Having vampires not being hammered into the ground by it would be a relief <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could also have vampires who drink Kool-Aid but I don't think that's the better game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T17:08:54-08:00","id":1369702,"title":"","content":"Another way to look at KotE is &quot;do you want to play vampire, but without the usual baggage&quot;?<br /> <br /> V:tM is a stand alone system while KotE is a kitchen sink cross over system.<br /> V:tM is about being isolated from humanity while KotE has a strong family connection theme and other Asian community values<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V:tM is about hiding the supernatural while KotE is about managing the supernatural balance<br /> V:tM is about Caine screwing up and you being collateral damage, while KotE is about you screwing up your life and paying for it.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V:tM is about being an emo teenager for eternity while KotE is about growing up/maturing for power gain.<br /> <br /> I would say that what needs to happen with the Kuei-jin is their mechanics need a serious overhaul to remove excess bloat and crunch, then fold the heretical dharmas into the original ones, make the dharmas much less antagonistic to everyone, and finally retcon the california invasion. KotE was a good alternative flavor of vampirism, but it was used in a poor fashion in relation to the metastory of the game line.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T17:21:31-08:00","id":1369704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369683#post1369683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way much worse than the Assamites, Ravnos, or Setites are in racial issues because at least you can play a Camarilla court in India.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't experienced this personally (as I am extremely white), but more than one of my friends has told me about Masquerade LARPs insisting they play specific clans because of their skin colors. So I agree with you wholeheartedly on that.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I were in charge? I would specify that Asia has &quot;normal&quot; Kindred just like Europe and Africa and Australia and the Americas do. The Wan Kuei (which seems to be their new name?) exist alongside them, not instead of them. So you can incorporate regional mythology if you want, or you can play a classic Camarilla-versus-Anarchs-versus-Sabbat game set in Tokyo or wherever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T18:22:46-08:00","id":1369718,"title":"","content":"Wipe out the kue jin. Turn Asia into a wild West for the kindred. Asia gets exploited by a new set of kindred colonizers. A new generation of young Asian kindred amarchs rebels. You could handle a colonization theme mixed and possibly promote the rise of some new sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T18:53:03-08:00","id":1369724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369718#post1369718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wipe out the kue jin. Turn Asia into a wild West for the kindred. Asia gets exploited by a new set of kindred colonizers. A new generation of young Asian kindred amarchs rebels. You could handle a colonization theme mixed and possibly promote the rise of some new sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not just have the local Cainites revealed to have been there all along?<br /> <br /> Mind you, the Second Inquisition means there's plenty of unclaimed cities for Kindred now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T19:53:06-08:00","id":1369732,"title":"","content":"KotE is all kinds of awesome. the lore, the powers, the dharmas, the whole concept is boss. probably the best game i ever ran, five chronicles over five years.<br /> <br /> however, it's never really played well with VtM. it should come back, revised, cleaned up, tightened, for the 21st century, but it should be its own splat distinct from VtM, and thus not in V5.<br /> <br /> separate both and that will give both lots of room to grow.<br /> <br /> or hell, just give it the Mummy: the Curse treatment and drop it into CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T20:00:25-08:00","id":1369733,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d prefer the core Clans to be culturally adopted to play in Eastern countries, rather than having a bunch of new ones that don\u2019t interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T20:03:12-08:00","id":1369734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369704#post1369704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't experienced this personally (as I am extremely white), but more than one of my friends has told me about Masquerade LARPs insisting they play specific clans because of their skin colors. So I agree with you wholeheartedly on that.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I were in charge? I would specify that Asia has &quot;normal&quot; Kindred just like Europe and Africa and Australia and the Americas do. The Wan Kuei (which seems to be their new name?) exist alongside them, not instead of them. So you can incorporate regional mythology if you want, or you can play a classic Camarilla-versus-Anarchs-versus-Sabbat game set in Tokyo or wherever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun Fact: White Wolf knew &quot;Wan Kuei&quot; was a more sensible name for them all the way back in the Kindred of the East core book. They said as much in the pages of it. They just decided to use &quot;Kuei Jin&quot; - muddling Chinese and Japanese vocabulary - under the pretense of...solidarity, I guess? It was dumb logic that would never have flown in-universe. It's hard enough to get mortals from the two countries to like each other (what with the crimes Imperial Japan did before and during WWII), let alone achieving it with immortal monsters, many of whom probably remember the nights when Japan was, to the Chinese mind, an out-of-date backwater in comparison to the Middle Kingdom.<br /> <br /> Whether bad blood or simple cultural arrogance, I don't see them all identifying as a mash-up of two languages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I agree that Cainites should have a greater presence in East Asia, even if you keep the Wan Kuei around. After heavy influence by western powers in the region - through trade, colonization, and war - it would be silly to assume Kindred wouldn't have arrived and developed a foothold. Especially since Kindred can multiply far more readily than Wan Kuei. I could see Kindred landing in China alongside the British forces, and using the resulting Opium Wars to destroy loads of native vampires, before taking root in Hong Kong and other areas. I can see American vampires arriving in Japan, Korea, and Vietnam during their respective wars, exploiting the damage to population and infrastructure to dig in.<br /> <br /> Honestly, such places should be a shadow battle ground, with Wan Kuei nursing old grudges and Kindred trying to maintain their holdings in relatively young domains. Fights breaking out in the <a href=\"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2018-06-27/china-ghost-cities-show-growth-driven-by-debt/9912186\" target=\"_blank\">mostly empty ghost cities of China</a>. Intrigue in the claustraphobic corridors of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kowloon_Walled_City\" target=\"_blank\">Kowloon Walled City</a>. Tensions simmering under the surface in Tokyo, a crowded city of high technology and a ruthless desire to keep everything running smoothly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T20:05:22-08:00","id":1369735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369704#post1369704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, if I were in charge? I would specify that Asia has &quot;normal&quot; Kindred just like Europe and Africa and Australia and the Americas do. The Wan Kuei (which seems to be their new name?) exist alongside them, not instead of them. So you can incorporate regional mythology if you want, or you can play a classic Camarilla-versus-Anarchs-versus-Sabbat game set in Tokyo or wherever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Other than central mainland China, where there are other issues about being dead and walking around, thats how it has always been in OWoD. Its just a whole lot of people seemed to miss it. In terms of nomenclature I prefer Hungry Ghosts myself as an umbrella term, theres a lot more to Asia/Oceania/Melanesia etc. than just China and each region would have their own terminology, see Aswang families in the Phillipines, Leyak covens in Bali etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 02-22-2020, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T20:09:37-08:00","id":1369736,"title":"","content":"Now as to whether I'd like to see them in V5? Probably not. V5 is mostly about removing outliers and consolidating things, simplifying and fitting things into simpler groups. And they're really bad, even compared to original White Wolf, at non-Western European/American setting material so far. So best they stay away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T20:49:24-08:00","id":1369740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369734#post1369734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I agree that Cainites should have a greater presence in East Asia, even if you keep the Wan Kuei around. After heavy influence by western powers in the region - through trade, colonization, and war - it would be silly to assume Kindred wouldn't have arrived and developed a foothold. Especially since Kindred can multiply far more readily than Wan Kuei. I could see Kindred landing in China alongside the British forces, and using the resulting Opium Wars to destroy loads of native vampires, before taking root in Hong Kong and other areas. I can see American vampires arriving in Japan, Korea, and Vietnam during their respective wars, exploiting the damage to population and infrastructure to dig in.<br /> <br /> Honestly, such places should be a shadow battle ground, with Wan Kuei nursing old grudges and Kindred trying to maintain their holdings in relatively young domains. Fights breaking out in the <a href=\"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2018-06-27/china-ghost-cities-show-growth-driven-by-debt/9912186\" target=\"_blank\">mostly empty ghost cities of China</a>. Intrigue in the claustraphobic corridors of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kowloon_Walled_City\" target=\"_blank\">Kowloon Walled City</a>. Tensions simmering under the surface in Tokyo, a crowded city of high technology and a ruthless desire to keep everything running smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I remember when thinking about Cainites in China is the fact that <b><i>Cainites aren't European</i></b>. Whenever I think of Eastern Cainites, I imagine they're people who got their Cainites from the Middle East and the trade of those regions potentially ranging back to Persia.<br /> <br /> Its not like trade and interaction with the Middle East is anything new.<br /> <br /> That's not even going back to the Enoch days when there could be Children of Caine there before Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-23-2020, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T21:44:19-08:00","id":1369747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369695#post1369695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that they would be in direct competition for pray...</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if it's the Ministry vs the Face of the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:16:56-08:00","id":1369756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369747#post1369747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if it's the Ministry vs the Face of the Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you auto correct. But funny enough to keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:18:57-08:00","id":1369757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369740#post1369740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing I remember when thinking about Cainites in China is the fact that <b><i>Cainites aren't European</i></b>. Whenever I think of Eastern Cainites, I imagine they're people who got their Cainites from the Middle East and the trade of those regions potentially ranging back to Persia.<br /> <br /> Its not like trade and interaction with the Middle East is anything new.<br /> <br /> That's not even going back to the Enoch days when there could be Children of Caine there before Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are however the walking, talking confirmation of biblical myth, and having other myths be true as well would really help break that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:27:47-08:00","id":1369762,"title":"","content":"They are also walking, talking embodiments of a myth that is still less than a hundred years old in its completed form. The original vampire legends, and the legends of the vampires of asia were originally pretty similar, rooted as they were in the same misunderstandings of things like deep comas, and the weird things corpses sometimes do. <br /> <br /> The vampire/succubus/Byronic/bodice-ripper hybrid thing vampires became happened in stages, and was only completed within the living memory of quite a few people living today. There are certain things you just have to let slide to make this game work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:31:18-08:00","id":1369765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369762#post1369762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are also walking, talking embodiments of a myth that is still less than a hundred years old in its completed form. The original vampire legends, and the legends of the vampires of asia were originally pretty similar, rooted as they were in the same misunderstandings of things like deep comas, and the weird things corpses sometimes do.<br /> <br /> The vampire/succubus/Byronic/bodice-ripper hybrid thing vampires became happened in stages, and was only completed within the living memory of quite a few people living today. There are certain things you just have to let slide to make this game work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly, but of an older vintage. the case of the Order of Hermes's favored practice, the Enochian language. It's like Klingon for Christian Alchemists!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T03:29:09-08:00","id":1369805,"title":"","content":"The Wan Kuei are in the Metaplot, therefore (as in the case of the Ravnos) you can\u2019t simply wipe them out since even if you do so, historical chronicles, set before their destruction, will still need them.<br /> <br /> As they did with about everything foreign in V5 I would rule everything weird about them as just misconceptions by western Vampires. Than I would rewrite the systems. Maybe instead of hunger, their unique selling point would be balance or what ever... but I would keep it much closer to the original system. As the fate of Saulot shows, eastern and western vampires are in reality much closer than both claim. In my personal head canon, Cain was basic a Wan Kuei who possessed his corpse because of his brothers death as a Wan Kuei would do. Unfortunately, since he was the mourner him self, he can never find peace and is stuck. But other than the wan Kuei he developed the ability to spread his curse and maybe every wan Kuei could do so, if Cain or Lilith would tell him, how that works.<br /> <br /> but the major change I would make is, that I would establish that kindred and Wan Kuei aren\u2019t that good in recognizing each other and often simply miss that the other group exists in a place. That would allow kindreds to exist in Asia (as we already know, Ravnos, Lasombra, Ventrue, Gangrel, Tzimisce, Ministry, Salubri, Hecata and Nosferatu are known for being established in the East). On the other hand, it would allow the KotE to exist at places we haven\u2019t seen them jet, maybe just because they and western Kindreds haven\u2019t discovered each other. I would even try to give a reason for more western character being Wan Kuei, but at the moment I am not share how to do so other than to point out, that the original Vampire of Eastern Europe in fact is more similar to the concept of Wan Kuei, but that is just me being a smart alec...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T04:12:22-08:00","id":1369808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369805#post1369805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As they did with about everything foreign in V5 I would rule everything weird about them as just misconceptions by western Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be darkly amusing, considering the Kuei-jin were themselves a revision of the earlier Cathayans -- the Gaki and Bushi of 1st and 2nd Edition <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> were simply declared Western misconceptions of the Hungry Dead. Perhaps each generation of vampires in the West gets the East wrong in their own particular way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T06:51:27-08:00","id":1369830,"title":"","content":"Kindred of the East is a great game once you research on it and get used to the asian culture and mythos. I really hope they don't change it to something more simple.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T07:29:04-08:00","id":1369832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369830#post1369830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East is a great game once you research on it and get used to the asian culture and mythos. I really hope they don't change it to something more simple.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess part of my issue is my degree is in Asian Studies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:10:45-08:00","id":1369839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369832#post1369832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I confess part of my issue is my degree is in Asian Studies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they should bring you on board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:11:08-08:00","id":1369855,"title":"","content":"Since they have little importance in any games I might run, it don't matter to me. So I leave it to others who are more invested in the question to answer it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:14:20-08:00","id":1369858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369688#post1369688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe but I think there's a fundamental disconnect because the Kuei Jin should have been their own splat.<br /> <br /> While they drink blood and are undead, they're closer to Wraith or Demon: The Fallen than Kindred.<br /> <br /> So when you deal with adapting the myth, there's no real reason for the Kuei Jin to ever interact with the Cainites anymore than the Werewolves or Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cainite\u2019s and Kuei-Jin in the same areas would be somewhat more likely to interact as hunting grounds might be contested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:40:10-08:00","id":1369861,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but no.<br /> V5 played big and hard made big sweeping changes and ultimately couldn't get vampires done right or respectfully, you think they could tackle the controversial hungry ghosts? Fat chance. <br /> Not having a firm grip on the reality of the west, do you think they can pull off the east? I'd rather not see <i>Kue-Jin: The asian dreams of middle class white woman who uses the term 'problematic' a lot</i> thank you very much.<br /> <br /> Do <br /> Not <br /> Touch<br /> With a twenty metre pike. <br /> Thank you. <br /> <br /> (though, Y'know, the more they over-cock up, the better the chances that WoD5 will be decanonized, so they really probably should have a go)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:49:59-08:00","id":1369865,"title":"","content":"As much as I love the kue jin it's hard for me to imagine what they add to the v5 agenda. Maybe I'm just not imaginative enough but all they seem to do is restrict stories set in half the world's population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:55:30-08:00","id":1369868,"title":"","content":"I suppose that I've been treating Kindred of the East as an aspect of V:tM, rather than a another game in its own right that affects the setting of V:tM. As Werewolf: The Apocalypes does. I would expect most players of V:tM to prefer to have the option of games set in eastern Asia and it sounds like that could be enabled further in the following ways:<ul><li>Retroactively omit Kuei-Jin from the metaplot. This would suck for anyone who likes them AND V5.</li> <li>Kill them off as part of the metaplot. That's problematic for the same reason as the above and it would limit deeply established and historic kindred presences.</li> <li>Make them more like kindred, if not actual kindred. I'm leaning towards this, but they'd lose essential characteristics in the process.</li> <li>Keep them mechanically as they are, but write in more coexistence with V:tM sects and clans. I think this would appeal to most people, except for those who dislike Kuei-Jin conceptually or think that there's already enough. For better or worse, it would entail more crossover.</li> <li>Make them more like kindred, if not actual kindred AND write in more coexistence. I imagine this would be a bit like how in the 2E Requiem core book, in which Beijing and Tokyo have a mixture of their own covenants and the global Western five (even if the latter was just the Lancea et Sanctum at the time).</li> </ul><br /> And then there's also the question of where whatever Asian vampires we get appear outside Asia. This is related to something that I like about the V5 Ministry and Banu Haqim and even Giovanni and dislike about most iterations of Ravnos. The former two clans now have big niches in Anarch and Camarilla communities respectively, beyond appearing every so often to say &quot;Hey kids(sss), wanna buy [whatever sketchy shit you're already looking for]*/have someone assassinated before I return to Alamut?&quot;. Suppose Hecata are trying to play the Camarilla and the Anarchs in Seoul against each other: what niche could some devil tigers have in Birmingham?<br /> <br /> *Although I do love this take on Setites anyway (not including the semi-strawman serpentine sibilance) and Giovanni kind of still have something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 02-23-2020, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:03:10-08:00","id":1369870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369868#post1369868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey kids(sss), wanna buy [whatever sketchy shit you're already looking for]*<br /> <br /> *Although I do love this take on Setites anyway (not including the semi-strawman serpentine sibilance)</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a laugh point for that. I do love the original fucked up snake cult drug peddler Setites, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:07:15-08:00","id":1369872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369861#post1369861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(though, Y'know, the more they over-cock up, the better the chances that WoD5 will be decanonized, so they really probably should have a go)</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the most popular and famous version of the game so far?<br /> <br /> The age of Twitch and Youtube has sold V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_