ll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the most popular and famous version of the game so far?<br /> <br /> The age of Twitch and Youtube has sold V5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> sadly, then their will be no place for me in future editions either. The disgusting controller/stalker/abuser setup of Touchstones and the obsession with massive numbers of beast/hunger effects make that clear, as does the complete obliteration of what used to make the elders terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:39:44-08:00","id":1369886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369881#post1369881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sadly, then their will be no place for me in future editions either. The disgusting controller/stalker/abuser setup of Touchstones and the obsession with massive numbers of beast/hunger effects make that clear, as does the complete obliteration of what used to make the elders terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you can also do Touchstones as genuinely protecting and loving them right?<br /> <br /> The beast/hunger effect has already been discussed as wrong too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:59:36-08:00","id":1369889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369886#post1369886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know you can also do Touchstones as genuinely protecting and loving them right?<br /> <br /> The beast/hunger effect has already been discussed as wrong too.</div> </div> </div> </div>the only way to love and protect a human, for a kindred, is to sever all contact and hope like hell no one finds about about them, every other action is painting a target on them, either for your hunger, or your enemies, this is why Golconda seekers used to avoid humans, vampires are irredeemably evil monsters, no matter how they delude themselves. 'Beast I be, Lest Beast I Become' makes that utterly clear. <br /> <br /> And no, I have been told that the RAW is wrong, but until that is an official errata, everything else is a house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T13:32:47-08:00","id":1369899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369889#post1369889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the only way to love and protect a human, for a kindred, is to sever all contact and hope like hell no one finds about about them, every other action is painting a target on them, either for your hunger, or your enemies, this is why Golconda seekers used to avoid humans, vampires are irredeemably evil monsters, no matter how they delude themselves. 'Beast I be, Lest Beast I Become' makes that utterly clear.<br /> <br /> And no, I have been told that the RAW is wrong, but until that is an official errata, everything else is a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've seen otherwise in Chicago by Night with the Touchstones. But yes, a bit like Spider-Man, being a friend to mortals can expose them to danger.<br /> <br /> I recommend a really touching relationship on display in THE SACRIFICE accompanied by a terrible one by Red Moon Roleplaying. Matthew Dawkins is amazing and terrifying in that one [and not the guy with a good Touchstone].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T19:49:18-08:00","id":1369955,"title":"","content":"I did like Kindred of the East since it helped to alleviate the problems that arose from setting up Vampire as based in Christian mythology. &quot;Oh, your Native American myths or African myths were just misunderstood monsters of Christian origin because Christian mythology is right and everyone else's mythology is wrong.&quot; Having something that was part of the Vampire setting, but that was firmly unrelated to anything resembling Christian mythology was really nice.<br /> <br /> I also liked the basic concept of the Wan Kuei (people who had committed enough sins that when they died, they went to hell but then had the willpower to break out of hell, go back to the mortal world and have a second chance at redeeming themselves). It made for really cool character arcs.<br /> <br /> Really iIn a lot of respects KotE was my favorite game from White Wolf, but at this point I'd just say bag it, throw it all in the trash and call it day. They won't be able to do a good with it. People who didn't like the gameline would be unhappy with it coming back without significant changes, people who liked the old gameline would be unhappy if it did receive those significant changes.<br /> <br /> If they do decide to just get rid of the Wan Kuei and replace them with regular old run-of-the-mill vampires, I just really, really hope they don't get Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom treatment with the whole, &quot;wink wink, nudge nudge, these vampires are just regular vampires in silly hats and you can see how they can all be traces back to the Antediluvians.&quot; Introduce completely different clans with completely different weakness and completely different abilities so we're not going, &quot;Oh, I see which of the thirteen Clans this group was originally part of.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T20:16:53-08:00","id":1369958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369955#post1369955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did like Kindred of the East since it helped to alleviate the problems that arose from setting up Vampire as based in Christian mythology. &quot;Oh, your Native American myths or African myths were just misunderstood monsters of Christian origin because Christian mythology is right and everyone else's mythology is wrong.&quot; Having something that was part of the Vampire setting, but that was firmly unrelated to anything resembling Christian mythology was really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? Since it says flat out that Cainites are Children of Caine since it shows that the native Chinese, Japanese, and Korean vampires are completely different. It removes a lot of the setting ambiguity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they do decide to just get rid of the Wan Kuei and replace them with regular old run-of-the-mill vampires, I just really, really hope they don't get Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom treatment with the whole, &quot;wink wink, nudge nudge, these vampires are just regular vampires in silly hats and you can see how they can all be traces back to the Antediluvians.&quot; Introduce completely different clans with completely different weakness and completely different abilities so we're not going, &quot;Oh, I see which of the thirteen Clans this group was originally part of.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think this confuses me since African Clans would be the ones the European ones were descended from in-universe.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I'd love for the gameline to hammer HARD how young the Camarilla is and how vampires are far-far older than Europe. So much so that the ancients should outnumber the modern vampires by a significant amount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-23-2020, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T02:45:10-08:00","id":1370010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369955#post1369955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did like Kindred of the East since it helped to alleviate the problems that arose from setting up Vampire as based in Christian mythology. &quot;Oh, your Native American myths or African myths were just misunderstood monsters of Christian origin because Christian mythology is right and everyone else's mythology is wrong.&quot; Having something that was part of the Vampire setting, but that was firmly unrelated to anything resembling Christian mythology was really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a common claim in fandom that <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is based upon a Judeo-Christian foundation myth which is portrayed, in the books, as inherently true. This is not actually the case; if one reads the books carefully, the &quot;objective&quot; history of vampires only goes back to the Antediluvians. The Second City, the second generation, and the existence of Caine only exist in vampire mythology, and there is nothing published to support their factual reality. These aspects of the background may exist in the game world ... or they may be the inventions of the third generation to hide the true origin of vampires. <br /> <br /> (This is, of course, entirely separate from books about other aspects of the World of Darkness, like <i>Devil's Due</i>, which are written with the inherent assumption that the Judeo-Christian origin myths are actually true. These are not generally very good books.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369955#post1369955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do decide to just get rid of the Wan Kuei and replace them with regular old run-of-the-mill vampires, I just really, really hope they don't get Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom treatment with the whole, &quot;wink wink, nudge nudge, these vampires are just regular vampires in silly hats and you can see how they can all be traces back to the Antediluvians.&quot; Introduce completely different clans with completely different weakness and completely different abilities so we're not going, &quot;Oh, I see which of the thirteen Clans this group was originally part of.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The approach taken by <i>Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom</i> is arguably the least problematic and offensive way of dealing with African vampires. One significant real-world issue with how Africa is portrayed in popular media is the idea that the people of Africa are intrinsically different in some unspecified way from the rest of humanity. Yet, African history is tied incredibly closely to that of Europe and western Asia, with a huge amount of trade, conflict, and cultural interchange. It is important in writing about Africa and African history (and the history part is unavoidable when dealing with immortal vampires) to stress the continuity and commonalites between Africa and the surrounding world. Exoticism tends to appeal to people who like the idea of the &quot;dark continent&quot;, a place of mystery and threatening otherness, though I'm not entirely sure that it's the best way to deal with Africa. Rather like some of the criticisms of <i>Kindred of the East </i>on this thread...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T03:09:17-08:00","id":1370017,"title":"","content":"There was even a thread a ways back that speculated that the Caine origin was Antedeluvian propaganda, and invited speculated as to what the reality was.<br /> <br /> My two theories were (1)the Antes are actually Chthulhuesque beings who were never human. Only 4rth and thinner types are actually human vampires. The horrors from beyond spawned avatars in our reality, and those avatars shared some of their essence with humans, but since the blood is unnatural in this world it gets weaker the further away it is from the source.<br /> <br /> And (2) the Antes are all completely unrelated people who made deals with the Devil for immortality. They all became vampires because vampirism is just how the Devil's immortality manifests. The various clan weaknesses are because different people were better at negotiating the fine-print, but all of them got screwed to at least a degree because they were bargaining with the Devil, and no one really gets a good deal out of that. At best, they missed little things in different parts of the contract, and so got screwed in slightly different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T03:15:28-08:00","id":1370019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369679#post1369679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, retcon out Tou Mu as an evil spirit. We don't need to be copying off of D&amp;D's paper. Especially not when even D&amp;D seems to have realized that it was a mistake before KotE even came along (unless there was some place in 2e other than Legends and Lore where she would have shown up).</div> </div> </div> </div>To me I will retcon very original yama kings as a kind of special great earthbound<br /> <br /> Sorry but according to 1000 Hells I think they ARE Demons in D:tF, despite how similar Demon and spirit is. They are fallen servitor of the God, after all. But later the yama king is rather a title than specific creatures","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T04:07:02-08:00","id":1370025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369872#post1369872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the most popular and famous version of the game so far?<br /> <br /> The age of Twitch and Youtube has sold V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, an indicator of being in the right place at the right time, rather than any indicator of quality. <br /> <br /> And Is it really that popular? I doubt I would've heard of it if I wasn't already a fan. It's all relative too; I heard there are more people playing pen'n paper games now, Better sales and a bigger audience come together, no? Plus, the overwhelming majority of the fame is from controversial decisions, no? <br /> Your spin on this is weak. <br /> <br /> I don't have a degree on the subject, but my pretty good understanding of east asia, and how westerners view easy asia, really suggest that no, the people who did V5 can't do this. <br /> If they wanted to give it to asians to do, they'd pick the wrong people. <br /> And, y'know, nationalism's pretty big over there compared to europe. It's not an easy task to do things fairly, even when you grab locals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T09:21:00-08:00","id":1370071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370025#post1370025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, an indicator of being in the right place at the right time, rather than any indicator of quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it's good.<br /> <br /> Seriously, your hatred of the game is fine. It's not for you but can you ditch the idea that it's an objective quality because it insults the fans of the game as is. Also the hard work of the people who have made great books from it.<br /> <br /> Very often the same people who made V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:27:48-08:00","id":1370087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370025#post1370025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a degree on the subject, but my pretty good understanding of east asia, and how westerners view easy asia, really suggest that no, the people who did V5 can't do this.<br /> If they wanted to give it to asians to do, they'd pick the wrong people.<br /> And, y'know, nationalism's pretty big over there compared to europe. It's not an easy task to do things fairly, even when you grab locals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk, I've been quite happy with the brief mentions we've gotten of East Asia so far in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T11:22:06-08:00","id":1370104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370019#post1370019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me I will retcon very original yama kings as a kind of special great earthbound<br /> <br /> Sorry but according to 1000 Hells I think they ARE Demons in D:tF, despite how similar Demon and spirit is. They are fallen servitor of the God, after all. But later the yama king is rather a title than specific creatures</div> </div> </div> </div>D:tF has a complication that might foul up your approach, in that it ignores the existence of the Middle Umbra. That's half of the setting for the 1000 Hells ripped out right off the bat. &quot;Earthbound&quot; as a state is also very much the opposite of what the Yama Kings are in, since they ended up squatting in spiritual realms that they had welded together instead of being invested into objects after being summoned from an Abyss where they had been exiled. You can go to these realms, but the Abyss is simply just nothingness; empty of space and separated from time, effectively making it so that the &quot;inhabitants&quot; don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T18:53:09-08:00","id":1370208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370010#post1370010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a common claim in fandom that <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is based upon a Judeo-Christian foundation myth which is portrayed, in the books, as inherently true. This is not actually the case; if one reads the books carefully, the &quot;objective&quot; history of vampires only goes back to the Antediluvians. The Second City, the second generation, and the existence of Caine only exist in vampire mythology, and there is nothing published to support their factual reality. These aspects of the background may exist in the game world ... or they may be the inventions of the third generation to hide the true origin of vampires.<br /> <br /> (This is, of course, entirely separate from books about other aspects of the World of Darkness, like <i>Devil's Due</i>, which are written with the inherent assumption that the Judeo-Christian origin myths are actually true. These are not generally very good books.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there's a problem with that, it is the only origin story (save for the Setite take on it) that we got. So it is effectively the truth for us because we don't have much of anything in regards to alternate origin stories to oppose it within VtM.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that the now non-canon <i>Gehenna</i> treated the Caine story as truth in all it's scenarios.<br /> <br /> If they wanted VtM to have unclear origins for vampires they could have done so just as easily as they did in VtR. The problem is that they only ever present the Caine Myth as the origin of Cainite vampires and it has become so utterly wedded to VtM that they couldn't undo it even if they wanted to. And if they did attempt to muddy the waters by throwing in new possible origin stories, fans would either ignore them as false or get outraged that they're attempting to retcon the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T19:54:44-08:00","id":1370216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370208#post1370208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except there's a problem with that, it is the only origin story (save for the Setite take on it) that we got. So it is effectively the truth for us because we don't have much of anything in regards to alternate origin stories to oppose it within VtM.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that the now non-canon <i>Gehenna</i> treated the Caine story as truth in all it's scenarios.<br /> <br /> If they wanted VtM to have unclear origins for vampires they could have done so just as easily as they did in VtR. The problem is that they only ever present the Caine Myth as the origin of Cainite vampires and it has become so utterly wedded to VtM that they couldn't undo it even if they wanted to. And if they did attempt to muddy the waters by throwing in new possible origin stories, fans would either ignore them as false or get outraged that they're attempting to retcon the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that Caine being the origins of vampires in the world is any particularly important thing, though, as the origin of a supernatural creature when werewolves are animist, changelings are Celtic Paganism, and Wraith is Nihilist Cosmic Horror.<br /> <br /> But yes, you could have the Kuei-Jin claim to be descended from, say, A Demon Emperor or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T21:55:39-08:00","id":1370233,"title":"","content":"Duplicate post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 02-25-2020, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T21:59:30-08:00","id":1370237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370019#post1370019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me I will retcon very original yama kings as a kind of special great earthbound<br /> <br /> Sorry but according to 1000 Hells I think they ARE Demons in D:tF, despite how similar Demon and spirit is. They are fallen servitor of the God, after all. But later the yama king is rather a title than specific creatures</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Yama Kings appear to have been created after the Demons were imprisoned in the Abyss, if you're considering overlapping cosmology. The original Yama Kings are essentially very powerful spirits (probably Incarna level) that were created specifically to cleanse the souls of the dead that go to Yomi, but later they became corrupt. Yomi Wan and the Abyss from D:TF are definitely different places. The souls of the dead don't go to the Abyss, and the Fallen imprisoned in the Abyss no longer actively serve any sort of function in the universe, while souls do go to Yomi Wan and the Yama Kings technically still serve a purpose, even if they've been corrupted.<br /> <br /> You might be interested in Dragons of the East page 40. It has some interesting info if you are trying to mesh the various cosmologies, which you can do so long as you're willing to assume that not every supernatural group gets everything right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 02-25-2020, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T22:02:47-08:00","id":1370238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370216#post1370216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that Caine being the origins of vampires in the world is any particularly important thing, though, as the origin of a supernatural creature when werewolves are animist, changelings are Celtic Paganism, and Wraith is Nihilist Cosmic Horror.<br /> <br /> But yes, you could have the Kuei-Jin claim to be descended from, say, A Demon Emperor or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And have that descent supported by rules, rules that make it clear they are an utterly different type of creature. The Caine origin is an elephant in the room, as is Demon the Fallen, but that;s another conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T22:07:21-08:00","id":1370240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370238#post1370238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And have that descent supported by rules, rules that make it clear they are an utterly different type of creature. The Caine origin is an elephant in the room, as is Demon the Fallen, but that;s another conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I guess I must be the exception to the rule in that I actually really like the Caine origin myth. I like single coherent metaphysics in my WOD. It helps underlay the gothic tone. I don't want a rifts world of darkness where everything and the kitchen sink has to be somehow tied together into a single coherent tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T22:11:29-08:00","id":1370242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370238#post1370238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And have that descent supported by rules, rules that make it clear they are an utterly different type of creature. The Caine origin is an elephant in the room, as is Demon the Fallen, but that;s another conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it an elephant?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that saying that a Middle Eastern myth is true for an origin of a monster is really that big of a deal in the setting in terms of cultural appropriation.<br /> <br /> Especially since Caine's myth is generally changed from traditional Judeo-Christian myth.<br /> <br /> And how is making Werewolf true any different from Demon or Mage?<br /> <br /> I mean, unless you just don't want any Judeo-Christian elements and are averse to them like a vampire with a cross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T22:15:38-08:00","id":1370243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369881#post1369881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> sadly, then their will be no place for me in future editions either. The disgusting controller/stalker/abuser setup of Touchstones and the obsession with massive numbers of beast/hunger effects make that clear, as does the complete obliteration of what used to make the elders terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've read it, the upcoming Player's Guide should provide support and such for these sorts of things. The core book even says the rules within it are not intended to cover elders. I'm house-ruling elders until then, and will continue to house-rule them if I don't like what the Player's Guide has for them.<br /> <br /> While behind their original schedule, there's this from the Modiphius website.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;V5 Players Guide</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Summer 2019) \u2013 A guide to playing different styles of Vampire: The Masquerade to help you play the way YOU want to play, from gritty street level drama to romantic blood opera, complete with advice, new rules, and guidance on using the 5</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">th</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Edition system to play previous editions of Vampire.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T22:43:05-08:00","id":1370247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370216#post1370216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that Caine being the origins of vampires in the world is any particularly important thing, though, as the origin of a supernatural creature when werewolves are animist, changelings are Celtic Paganism, and Wraith is Nihilist Cosmic Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean in some respects it's not important, but in other respects it is important. If Caine is the origin of vampires then it basically confirms the Judeo-Christian creation myth which in turn means that Creation myths of other cultures or religions aren't correct and that their own myths are just misinterpretations or bastardizations of Christianity. The werewolves, Changelings and everything else are peripheral to VtM and their own origin stories don't matter in the context of VtM. But the Wan Kuei were an actual part of the game line in a bigger way, and managed to bring in a competing mythology that said, &quot;No, the Christian myths aren't the truth, we have different ones and they're every bit as valid,&quot; which I really liked.<br /> <br /> It would have been nice if we had seen non-Christian Vampires get to bring something similar to the table, but all we got was the Followers of Set's story, and then had stuff like KotEK which basically reconfirmed the whole Caine/Antediluvian story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T22:51:12-08:00","id":1370249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370247#post1370247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean in some respects it's not important, but in other respects it is important. If Caine is the origin of vampires then it basically confirms the Judeo-Christian creation myth which in turn means that Creation myths of other cultures or religions aren't correct and that their own myths are just misinterpretations or bastardizations of Christianity. The werewolves, Changelings and everything else are peripheral to VtM and their own origin stories don't matter in the context of VtM. But the Wan Kuei were an actual part of the game line in a bigger way, and managed to bring in a competing mythology that said, &quot;No, the Christian myths aren't the truth, we have different ones and they're every bit as valid,&quot; which I really liked.<br /> <br /> It would have been nice if we had seen non-Christian Vampires get to bring something similar to the table, but all we got was the Followers of Set's story, and then had stuff like KotEK which basically reconfirmed the whole Caine/Antediluvian story.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another reason why the Wan Kuei might not be a good addition to the game. But I do think that we should add alternative Kindred myths.<br /> <br /> Maybe also some alternative Caine interpretation.<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine is real but who cursed him and why?&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of the games I played in had him cursed by the Sun God of whatever culture it was done. I also had Osiris and Set, Romulus and Remus, and other &quot;brother murder&quot; legends with Caine just the latest adaptation of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T23:13:00-08:00","id":1370254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5#post1369651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like a lot about the Kuei-Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they are brought back in some form, but have origins utterly unconnected to Cainites. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5#post1369651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and how many vampires could there be on the Pacific islands anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I currently live in Samoa and sometimes wonder about the same thing. However, Samoa is one of the least gothic-punk-darkness places ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T23:25:16-08:00","id":1370257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370254#post1370254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I currently live in Samoa and sometimes wonder about the same thing. However, Samoa is one of the least gothic-punk-darkness places ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve been to Samoa on holiday. It is beautiful, as are the people, but I could imagine some hidden vampire enclave, only coming out to socialize on the beaches at night. I could see the locals being aware of it, but keeping the tourists unaware. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T01:50:41-08:00","id":1370270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370249#post1370249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the games I played in had him cursed by the Sun God of whatever culture it was done. I also had Osiris and Set, Romulus and Remus, and other &quot;brother murder&quot; legends with Caine just the latest adaptation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done the same with my own homebrew and in house games. But it was just nice having an official sect of vampires that had nothing to do with the Christian mythology, the Biblical Caine or his Antediluvians. The world's a big place, and I always found the way Vampire leaned too heavily into the Abrahamic religions while largely ignoring everything else was somewhat problematic (though understandable considering who the people writing the game were and who their primary audience for VtM was - when VtM was first being written it wasn't being written for audiences in China or Southeast Asia or Africa or South America).<br /> <br /> My hope is that if, in 5th edition, White Wolf does decide to get rid of the Wan Kuei and replace them with more traditional vampires, we don't just get recolored &quot;Player 2&quot; clans like we did in Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom. Instead I'd like to see vampires that don't have any obvious or even subtle ties to bloodlines that more typical vampires trace themselves back to, and have their own competing origin story which would (hopefully) would be presented as at least as accurate a story as Caine and the Antediluvians. Of course there would still be more traditional Kindred clans in Asia, but ultimately I think getting rid of the Wan Kuei and replacing them all with the regular Toreador, and Brujah and Malkavians would end up making the setting feel smaller and the less interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-25-2020, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T01:54:47-08:00","id":1370272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370270#post1370270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've done the same with my own homebrew and in house games. But it was just nice having an official sect of vampires that had nothing to do with the Christian mythology, the Biblical Caine or his Antediluvians. The world's a big place, and I always found the way Vampire leaned too heavily into the Abrahamic religions while largely ignoring everything else was somewhat problematic (though understandable considering who the people writing the game were and who their primary audience for VtM was - when VtM was first being written it wasn't being written for audiences in China or Southeast Asia or Africa or South America).<br /> <br /> My hope is that if, in 5th edition, White Wolf does decide to get rid of the Wan Kuei and replace them with more traditional vampires, we don't just get recolored &quot;Player 2&quot; clans like we did in Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom. Instead I'd like to see vampires that don't have any obvious or even subtle ties to bloodlines that more typical vampires trace themselves back to, and have their own competing origin story which would (hopefully) would be presented as at least as accurate a story as Caine and the Antediluvians. Of course there would still be more traditional Kindred clans in Asia, but ultimately I think getting rid of the Wan Kuei and replacing them all with the regular Toreador, and Brujah and Malkavians would end up making the setting feel smaller and the less interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, is the archetype something that needs to be changed? If you had the Jiangshi be a group of pale-skinned corpse-like Kindred who live in crypts and have death-related powers, is that bad that they're probably Cappadocians?<br /> <br /> Or Cappadocians are them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T02:24:09-08:00","id":1370276,"title":"","content":"Hold on for a moment<br /> Why are you all describing vampires as Judaeo-Christian? <br /> <br /> Everything's Judaic. There's nothing christian there. <br /> If you follow the words; All the Caine Myth is Old testament. God is decisively old testament (because the new testament would make him nicer). There's nothing 'new testament' and there's a few things arguably Pre-Judaism. But, forgive me if I'm wrong, I've found absolutely nothing in VTM that gives the Caine myth some Christ (Other than, y'know, the assumptions of christian vampires and players, who are further removed from the event. True faith does not indicate a correct religion) <br /> (really interesting thing I found when I was looking stuff up. Apparently ancient people believed babies were from semen, and the womb was just a nurturing place for semen. Fascinating stuff) <br /> <br /> But the main thing I wanted to say, was that you actually don't know if the Caine myth isn't made up BS. Sure, there are Gehenna situations with Caine and Lilith (contradicting scenarios I might add) but just because the people are real does not mean the stories are. When I was reading about Cagn (was that it?), the african Caine analogue, I didn't conclude 'LoL silly africans misrepresenting Jewish beliefs' because, y'know, stories spread and change and there's no evidence that the europeans got it right (The Antideluvians are mostly in Europe and West Asia? Well, that's just taking advantage of big population centres that don't have Wan-Kuei around) <br /> <br /> It's fun, thematic and convenient to have vampires<i> believe</i> they're from Caine<br /> But it's also fun, thematic and convenient for Myth to be Myth. <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires are liars. <br /> Only Set speaks the Truth<br /> (His followers don't)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T05:09:31-08:00","id":1370313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370243#post1370243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I've read it, the upcoming Player's Guide should provide support and such for these sorts of things. The core book even says the rules within it are not intended to cover elders. I'm house-ruling elders until then, and will continue to house-rule them if I don't like what the Player's Guide has for them.<br /> <br /> While behind their original schedule, there's this from the Modiphius website.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&amp;quot;V5 Players Guide</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Summer 2019) \u2013 A guide to playing different styles of Vampire: The Masquerade to help you play the way YOU want to play, from gritty street level drama to romantic blood opera, complete with advice, new rules, and guidance on using the 5</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">th</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Edition system to play previous editions of Vampire.&amp;quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The game developer said something different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1341627-helena-portia-candid-camera-or-real?p=1341802#post1341802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity, the rules for elder characters have already been released. When you consider that rolling nine or ten dice, plus your Blood Potency bonuses (such as blood surge, etc.) you're unstoppable compared to a neonate with a dice pool of three or four. There's no nerfing, it's just that some readers don't appear to be taking into account the benefits of Generation, Blood Potency, amalgam Disciplines, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T05:17:52-08:00","id":1370315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370313#post1370313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game developer said something different.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The two comments are not necessarily contradictory, although they do look that way. I\u2019m taking it to mean, in a comment that is possibly not given in context, that the rules of playing Elders will not require adding lots more rules or stats, but will merely extrapolate on the existing rules as they stand. So, there may be support for playing Elder level characters in the Player\u2019s Guide - which isn\u2019t supported in the core rules explicitly - but there won\u2019t be any massive expansion of rules in order to accommodate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T08:39:42-08:00","id":1370364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370276#post1370276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold on for a moment<br /> Why are you all describing vampires as Judaeo-Christian?<br /> <br /> Everything's Judaic. There's nothing christian there.<br /> If you follow the words; All the Caine Myth is Old testament. God is decisively old testament (because the new testament would make him nicer). There's nothing 'new testament' and there's a few things arguably Pre-Judaism. But, forgive me if I'm wrong, I've found absolutely nothing in VTM that gives the Caine myth some Christ (Other than, y'know, the assumptions of christian vampires and players, who are further removed from the event. True faith does not indicate a correct religion)<br /> (really interesting thing I found when I was looking stuff up. Apparently ancient people believed babies were from semen, and the womb was just a nurturing place for semen. Fascinating stuff)<br /> <br /> But the main thing I wanted to say, was that you actually don't know if the Caine myth isn't made up BS. Sure, there are Gehenna situations with Caine and Lilith (contradicting scenarios I might add) but just because the people are real does not mean the stories are. When I was reading about Cagn (was that it?), the african Caine analogue, I didn't conclude 'LoL silly africans misrepresenting Jewish beliefs' because, y'know, stories spread and change and there's no evidence that the europeans got it right (The Antideluvians are mostly in Europe and West Asia? Well, that's just taking advantage of big population centres that don't have Wan-Kuei around)<br /> <br /> It's fun, thematic and convenient to have vampires<i> believe</i> they're from Caine<br /> But it's also fun, thematic and convenient for Myth to be Myth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires are liars.<br /> Only Set speaks the Truth<br /> (His followers don't)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know how deep you are into religion and into which one, but most Christian confessions see the old testament still as part of the Bible and their faith. You can\u2019t really have the new testament without the old. Jesus as savior makes little sense out of the Jewish context. Most Christians today even don\u2019t deny that Jesus was a Jew, or at least grew up Jewish. That is why in the middle age the search for Jesus\u2019 foreskin was a thing, because people concluded that Jesus, grown up in a Jewish family, must have been circumcised. And other than the rest of his body this particular body part might have remained on earth as probably the most powerful relict in whole Christianity. (Excuse me for the pictures you have in mind now, people are weird, and they always were and always will be).<br /> <br /> What makes the myths more Christion as well is the whole \u201coriginal sin\u201d thing, that is kind of represented in the curse. I know, most Christion other than Catholics don\u2019t have that, but considered that Catholicism was the dominant religion in Europe for a long time, I guess that counts.<br /> <br /> And most people forget about the gnostic Christs, older groups of Christs who thought very differently about a lot of stuff. Some, for example thought there must have been two gods, the good god and the creator because the creator must have been an evil god since the world is\u2026 well just look around and decide if the world looks like something, a benevolent god would create for his children\u2026<br /> <br /> Gnosticism is btw, what the Church of Cain is based on.<br /> <br /> But, eventually, I agree, we don\u2019t know what really happened back then, we can only conclude that there probably was (at least) one first vampire. The rest is clouded in the mist of ages\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.: You could also use the term \u201cAbrahamic\u201d which includes other religions that are connected to the same source as Islam or Druze. That would even make more sense since Judeo-Christion exclude those while they have the same \u201corigin story\u201d as jews and christian and therefore have Cain or at least a Cain like figure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T08:48:37-08:00","id":1370366,"title":"","content":"I currently read through the V5 rules for blood again and I came to the conclusion, that the humors are kind of what KotE did with Yin, Yang, Hun and Po. I think, with this in mind, it is even much easier to recreate the Wan Kuei. They basically would get a different blood Potency system, that would include chi-consumption at some level and maybe some new disciplines or discipline powers. Everything else is more or less fluff and could be rewritten by someone with a better knowledge of Asian culture and myths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:42:59-08:00","id":1370380,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370276#post1370276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fun, thematic and convenient to have vampires<i> believe</i> they're from Caine<br /> But it's also fun, thematic and convenient for Myth to be Myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much! I go one step further and have a lot of other different myths running around apart from the Caine one, just because the world's a big place.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370276#post1370276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are liars.<br /> Only Set speaks the Truth</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen!<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370276#post1370276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(His followers don't)</div> </div> </div> </div>Slander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:50:56-08:00","id":1370385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370313#post1370313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game developer said something different.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought the The Gentleman Gamer wasn't actually working on the Players Guide, but rather knew a person who was, and was receiving limited information from them. I watched a video where The Gentleman Gamer talked a bit about what he'd heard from others working on the project, but said he didn't know all that much.<br /> <br /> Regardless, the V5 core book flat out says multiple times that the rules contained within aren't for elders, so the rules for elders have not been released. The things he mentioned for elders simply don't hold up against multiple neonates or ancillae, and there should be a significant power difference between elders, young methuselahs, and ancient methuselahs.<br /> <br /> A more recent News post from Modiphius says this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Coming on its heels is the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Vampire: The Masquerade 5</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">th</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Edition Players Guide</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. An essential guide containing additional information on Clans, Disciplines, new tools plus some excellent playing advice and alternative ways to play. And finally, an overview of all 13 Kindred clans in one place! Find out everything you needed to know to play your best V5 game yet.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 02-25-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:55:03-08:00","id":1370387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370242#post1370242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it an elephant?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that saying that a Middle Eastern myth is true for an origin of a monster is really that big of a deal in the setting in terms of cultural appropriation.<br /> <br /> Especially since Caine's myth is generally changed from traditional Judeo-Christian myth.<br /> <br /> And how is making Werewolf true any different from Demon or Mage?<br /> <br /> I mean, unless you just don't want any Judeo-Christian elements and are averse to them like a vampire with a cross.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I want doubt and ambiguity, to be expressed at a rules level. I want different supernaturals to have different origins, backed by being actually different, even if they","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:55:42-08:00","id":1370388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370242#post1370242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it an elephant?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that saying that a Middle Eastern myth is true for an origin of a monster is really that big of a deal in the setting in terms of cultural appropriation.<br /> <br /> Especially since Caine's myth is generally changed from traditional Judeo-Christian myth.<br /> <br /> And how is making Werewolf true any different from Demon or Mage?<br /> <br /> I mean, unless you just don't want any Judeo-Christian elements and are averse to them like a vampire with a cross.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I want doubt and ambiguity, to be expressed at a rules level. I want different supernaturals to have different origins, backed by being actually different, even if they fill similar niches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:57:50-08:00","id":1370389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370388#post1370388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want doubt and ambiguity, to be expressed at a rules level. I want different supernaturals to have different origins, backed by being actually different, even if they fill similar niches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough but if they're different supernaturals I wouldn't want Kuei-Jin at elysium, fighting Kindred in Los Angeles, or even encountering them save in a one-shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:03:27-08:00","id":1370392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370389#post1370389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough but if they're different supernaturals I wouldn't want Kuei-Jin at elysium, fighting Kindred in Los Angeles, or even encountering them save in a one-shot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Elysium ofc not, but they are aiming for the same targets and influence, just by different means, they should clash, like hyenas and lions clash, over territory, over prey, over power, but it should be so they have a messy patchwork conflict going on, not as monolithic splats,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 02-25-2020, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:11:37-08:00","id":1370393,"title":"","content":"I believe the Ravnos have an alternate creation myth. Zapathasura, the man most wronged by the fallen Wan Xian, was blessed by the gods to fight them and keep them in line. Some of the gods, fearing he might abuse his power and become like the Wan Xian, also cursed him. There's also a few other creation myths from various continents, such as Cagn, and the Canarl, though most are variations of the Caine myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:38:56-08:00","id":1370398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370393#post1370393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Ravnos have an alternate creation myth. Zapathasura, the man most wronged by the fallen Wan Xian, was blessed by the gods to fight them and keep them in line. Some of the gods, fearing he might abuse his power and become like the Wan Xian, also cursed him. There's also a few other creation myths from various continents, such as Cagn, and the Canarl, though most are variations of the Caine myth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The differences aren't backed by rules, so, aren't supported. I may be to simulationist, but if you tell me something is different, show me how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T10:45:13-08:00","id":1370401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370398#post1370398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The differences aren't backed by rules, so, aren't supported. I may be to simulationist, but if you tell me something is different, show me how.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that the differences aren't backed by the rules. I suspect those alternative creation myths were added to support Storytellers that want to change things up. Though they don't currently have rules supporting their differences, there's a lot of potential with the Drowned Legacies for other species of vampire, though I'm not sure that will ever be explored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T13:28:48-08:00","id":1370433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370385#post1370385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought the The Gentleman Gamer wasn't actually working on the Players Guide, but rather knew a person who was, and was receiving limited information from them. I watched a video where The Gentleman Gamer talked a bit about what he'd heard from others working on the project, but said he didn't know all that much.<br /> <br /> Regardless, the V5 core book flat out says multiple times that the rules contained within aren't for elders, so the rules for elders have not been released. The things he mentioned for elders simply don't hold up against multiple neonates or ancillae, and there should be a significant power difference between elders, young methuselahs, and ancient methuselahs.<br /> <br /> A more recent News post from Modiphius says this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Coming on its heels is the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Vampire: The Masquerade 5</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">th</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> Edition Players Guide</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. An essential guide containing additional information on Clans, Disciplines, new tools plus some excellent playing advice and alternative ways to play. And finally, an overview of all 13 Kindred clans in one place! Find out everything you needed to know to play your best V5 game yet.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Outdated information. C.T.Pipes said he heard from a podcast there will be only 12 clans because Ravnos gotta nukes for good on and off. Actually, maybe only 11, cauz the new writers are clueless about how to do monstruous vampires tzimisce with the rules from core pushing to the oppposite side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T14:38:52-08:00","id":1370448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370398#post1370398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The differences aren't backed by rules, so, aren't supported. I may be to simulationist, but if you tell me something is different, show me how.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, they're not unsupported either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T15:35:32-08:00","id":1370458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370433#post1370433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Outdated information. C.T.Pipes said he heard from a podcast there will be only 12 clans because Ravnos gotta nukes for good on and off. Actually, maybe only 11, cauz the new writers are clueless about how to do monstruous vampires tzimisce with the rules from core pushing to the oppposite side.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I heard about that. Still, there's the part that says &quot;...new tools plus some excellent playing advice and alternative ways to play.&quot; I'm completely comfortable houseruling elders, clans, and Disciplines, though I'll always appreciate having to do less work. I've already written up Ravnos, Chimerstry (called Maya in my games), Salubri Warriors, Valeren, and have begun work on the Baali, Daimonion, the Kiasyd, Maeghar, and Mytherceria (Mytherceria will need some hefty changes) for V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T17:37:25-08:00","id":1370475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370458#post1370458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I heard about that. Still, there's the part that says &quot;...new tools plus some excellent playing advice and alternative ways to play.&quot; I'm completely comfortable houseruling elders, clans, and Disciplines, though I'll always appreciate having to do less work. I've already written up Ravnos, Chimerstry (called Maya in my games), Salubri Warriors, Valeren, and have begun work on the Baali, Daimonion, the Kiasyd, Maeghar, and Mytherceria (Mytherceria will need some hefty changes) for V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what alternative way to play theyre talking about. In truth, I genuinely didn't understood what they mean with it.<br /> I want out of universe explanation instead of the in universe commentary like anarch and camarilla guides.<br /> I will not be interested if this supplement just say to me to homebrew, but this is unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T19:45:52-08:00","id":1370490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370448#post1370448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, they're not unsupported either.</div> </div> </div> </div>If something supposedly has a different origin, but uses the same system, has generation, disciplines, embraces the same way etc , the rules are showing you that the claims aren't true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T21:41:26-08:00","id":1370503,"title":"","content":"If they want to remove the whol KotE thing, they may have problem when dealing with Hunter 5E (if it's still possible... well...) at least. For ancestors of kuei-jin, wan xian, are also the hunter's. (the Apocrypha even hints wan xian) I want to see how will they deal with this.<br /> <br /> *Maybe the wan xian are not the old imbueds accurately, but has been very, very close (the heroes hail from the mortals, but the xian are much more powerful)<br /> <br /> **Another tip, DA: Inquisitor are not another kind of imbueds ,it is just a spiritual <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">prequel</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 02-26-2020, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T12:53:29-08:00","id":1370629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370503#post1370503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they want to remove the whol KotE thing, they may have problem when dealing with Hunter 5E (if it's still possible... well...) at least. For ancestors of kuei-jin, wan xian, are also the hunter's. (the Apocrypha even hints wan xian) I want to see how will they deal with this.<br /> <br /> *Maybe the wan xian are not the old imbueds accurately, but has been very, very close (the heroes hail from the mortals, but the xian are much more powerful)<br /> <br /> **Another tip, DA: Inquisitor are not another kind of imbueds ,it is just a spiritual <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">prequel</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly has there actually been any word on them doing any of the other splats? Outside of video games, I haven't heard anything since Paradox first purchased WW about the other game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T13:12:50-08:00","id":1370632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370490#post1370490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If something supposedly has a different origin, but uses the same system, has generation, disciplines, embraces the same way etc , the rules are showing you that the claims aren't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure? All that means is that the Caine origin has no claim to be true because someone has equal evidence of being true since it has the same powers but believes the opposite.<br /> <br /> It's like if you asked, &quot;Is the Caine Myth true?&quot; of Mithras and he said, &quot;No.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:17:00-08:00","id":1370645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370632#post1370632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you figure? All that means is that the Caine origin has no claim to be true because someone has equal evidence of being true since it has the same powers but believes the opposite.<br /> <br /> It's like if you asked, &amp;quot;Is the Caine Myth true?&amp;quot; of Mithras and he said, &amp;quot;No.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras has no way of knowing for sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (but do what he says anyway, especially when he gets proper stats) <br /> <br /> Why ? Because WW did to good a job of building the Caine myth arc, really, and I dislike the cop out of 'these things are completely different ignore that they use exactly the same rules' that turns up in gaming frequently, also the way my mind works wants categories to put things in, so WW made the. 'cainite' category, so cainites go in that box, the shape changing breeds category, so werecritters live there, etc etc (yes this does make for disappointing days irl). <br /> <br /> That need to have categories and subcategories to make sense of things leads on to wanting hungry dead from different myths to be different, they aren't different if they fit in the cainites box (plus Gehenna made it clear that it was true, as did DtF, which is a game I really enjoyed, for all its many faults). I want other myths to have at least a little of that level of care and world building, rather than be a cainite respray. <br /> <br /> You once asked me what had to change about Anarchs for me to like them, I hope my response makes more sense now, their is nothing they could do, for I don't like what makes them Anarch, they could be the best written version of what they are, and I wouldn't like them because I fundamentally don't get them, I have read about real world Anarchist militia, armies and free states....and the Anarchs really, really aren't them, they don't fit in the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:48:29-08:00","id":1370674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370645#post1370645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mithras has no way of knowing for sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (but do what he says anyway, especially when he gets proper stats)<br /> <br /> Why ? Because WW did to good a job of building the Caine myth arc, really, and I dislike the cop out of 'these things are completely different ignore that they use exactly the same rules' that turns up in gaming frequently, also the way my mind works wants categories to put things in, so WW made the. 'cainite' category, so cainites go in that box, the shape changing breeds category, so werecritters live there, etc etc (yes this does make for disappointing days irl).<br /> <br /> That need to have categories and subcategories to make sense of things leads on to wanting hungry dead from different myths to be different, they aren't different if they fit in the cainites box (plus Gehenna made it clear that it was true, as did DtF, which is a game I really enjoyed, for all its many faults). I want other myths to have at least a little of that level of care and world building, rather than be a cainite respray.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying that if you can create a wonderful and detailed mythology that has the progenitor of the vampire and subsequent generations be someone other than Caine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You once asked me what had to change about Anarchs for me to like them, I hope my response makes more sense now, their is nothing they could do, for I don't like what makes them Anarch, they could be the best written version of what they are, and I wouldn't like them because I fundamentally don't get them, I have read about real world Anarchist militia, armies and free states....and the Anarchs really, really aren't them, they don't fit in the box. </div> </div> </div>Okay, what don't you get I'm curious about? I am actually very interested in this as a student of real life X and Y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T21:17:18-08:00","id":1370696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370674#post1370674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)<br /> I'm just saying that if you can create a wonderful and detailed mythology that has the progenitor of the vampire and subsequent generations be someone other than Caine.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2)<br /> Okay, what don't you get I'm curious about? I am actually very interested in this as a student of real life X and Y.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) you could, but WW chose Caine, linked that myth with the rules, so those rules are 'how vampires descending from Caine work', at least in my mind, that is kinda how I think about most things, which makes me really good at vanishing into the weeds to build characters (absurdly fast to quote a previous ST, who by the end was getting me to stay 'generic' NPC's for him), and really bad at unchaining story (not calling it fluff, had a Dev on a different game object to that term, he told us why, and it made enough sense to make any time I use it since a slip) from rules, when I previously said 'rules are the scaffolding of story' I meant it.<br /> <br /> 2) why a faction of gangsters and failed theorists, that keeps forming circular firing squads and degenerating into squabbles over territory gets given so much success, why what looks like jocks with fangs is lauded in story so much, why a movement that disorganized gets called Anarchs (seriously read about actual Anarchists, disorganized they are not, at all, Homage to Catalonia is a great place to start, for characters that deserve to have been embraced read up about Makhno of the Revolutionary Insurectioary Army of Ukraine, dude was walking talking crazy awesome) the Anarchs (or rather the Devs) need to make up their mind what the Anarchs actually are, catch all for street gangs and local political clubs, a genuine Anarchist inspired by (or movement that inspired) the mortal Anarchist movements, insult for neonate and ancilla the cam don't like....what is it, and why, exactly, would two full clans want to join it, were is its unity and structure, where is its International(anarchism currently has 3 internationals, so Anarchs could also have rival ones jockeying for power). What has it done to earn and embody the title Anarch , currently? <br /> <br /> Because, even in V5, which apparently is using them as it's default sect, they don't look like an organisation, and without that structure to have strength, they look like they should get rolled by the first properly mobilised force that hits them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T21:42:38-08:00","id":1370700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370629#post1370629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly has there actually been any word on them doing any of the other splats? Outside of video games, I haven't heard anything since Paradox first purchased WW about the other game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat it as a wishful thinking. AFAIK Paradox haven't any plan about other gamelines, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T22:12:29-08:00","id":1370701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370700#post1370700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Treat it as a wishful thinking. AFAIK Paradox haven't any plan about other gamelines, whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apocalypse 5e is coming in 2021, at least, and the trademark on &quot;Orpheus&quot; was recently renewed. I'm not sure which other ones are in the pipeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T22:29:03-08:00","id":1370704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370696#post1370696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) you could, but WW chose Caine, linked that myth with the rules, so those rules are 'how vampires descending from Caine work', at least in my mind, that is kinda how I think about most things, which makes me really good at vanishing into the weeds to build characters (absurdly fast to quote a previous ST, who by the end was getting me to stay 'generic' NPC's for him), and really bad at unchaining story (not calling it fluff, had a Dev on a different game object to that term, he told us why, and it made enough sense to make any time I use it since a slip) from rules, when I previously said 'rules are the scaffolding of story' I meant it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, is Caine actually canon though? The rules make it clear that the Antediluvians actually exist, but anything before that is pure speculation.<br /> <br /> Many BH, for example, accept that there was a first vampire before Haqim, but claim this first vampire Embraced Haqim directly, no &quot;second&quot; Generation. Orthodox Setites claim that Set and the Aeons (other Antediluvians) are where vampires started, with nothing before them. Some Bahari deny Caine completely and say that Lilith cursed each of the Antediluvians individually and that's where what we would now call &quot;vampirism&quot; started. All of them would say the &quot;standard&quot; system of counting Generations is wrong.<br /> <br /> (The Church of Set also says it has elders who remember when the whole &quot;Cain and Abel&quot; story was first invented by humans, and then when it was appropriated by vampires to explain their origins several centuries later. Which is a fun little bit of lore.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T22:35:34-08:00","id":1370705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370704#post1370704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, is Caine actually canon though? The rules make it clear that the Antediluvians actually exist, but anything before that is pure speculation.<br /> <br /> Many BH, for example, accept that there was a first vampire before Haqim, but claim this first vampire Embraced Haqim directly, no &amp;quot;second&amp;quot; Generation. Orthodox Setites claim that Set and the Aeons (other Antediluvians) are where vampires started, with nothing before them. Some Bahari deny Caine completely and say that Lilith cursed each of the Antediluvians individually and that's where what we would now call &amp;quot;vampirism&amp;quot; started. All of them would say the &amp;quot;standard&amp;quot; system of counting Generations is wrong.<br /> <br /> (The Church of Set also says it has elders who remember when the whole &amp;quot;Cain and Abel&amp;quot; story was first invented by humans, and then when it was appropriated by vampires to explain their origins several centuries later. Which is a fun little bit of lore.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Book Of Nod, Revelations of the Dark Mother and Gehenna certainly act as if it is, as does Demon The Fallen (which isn't a VtM book I know) as does Devils Due, which is a DA source admittedly, so it being Canon has more support than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T22:42:58-08:00","id":1370706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370705#post1370705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Book Of Nod, Revelations of the Dark Mother and Gehenna certainly act as if it is, as does Demon The Fallen (which isn't a VtM book I know) as does Devils Due, which is a DA source admittedly, so it being Canon has more support than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Book of Nod and Revelations of the Dark Mother books are like saying, &quot;The Bible acts as if Jesus is real.&quot; Caine is important to the religion of European Cainites and that is important but they're in-universe mythology that created the Caine myth.<br /> <br /> Gehenna is non-canon too in its own universe as it just presents scenarios.<br /> <br /> Lilith is also a vampire in that so that calls into question whether Caine was the first one.<br /> <br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary takes the piss several times at the Caine myth too, particularly the Laibon and Enoch sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T23:24:39-08:00","id":1370707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370701#post1370701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apocalypse 5e is coming in 2021, at least</div> </div> </div> </div>Well is this strange? they never give up three major gamelines. On the coantrary I haven't seen any signs of renewed KotE or HtR, at least<br /> <br /> Of course I also don't have much hope about these, because they have declared that 20th has released all in plan<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T01:30:31-08:00","id":1370716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1370704#post1370704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, is Caine actually canon though? The rules make it clear that the Antediluvians actually exist, but anything before that is pure speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. It's canon that the story of Caine is a common creation myth amongst, but there is no canonical statement as to whether there is any truth to such stories (other than, to a degree, <i>Gehenna</i>). As for the reality, very little has been determined. Perhaps Caine was invented by the Antedilivians, to disguise the fact that their real origin was rather embarrassing?<br /> <br /> It is, of course, worth noting that the immortality of vampires has a significant effect upon what could be regarded as existing in &quot;living&quot; memory. There are plenty of active Methusalehs around; Caine is only their great-grandparent, so there should be plenty of family history around, relating to what amounts to close relatives. I don't think that the game ever managed to get a decent grip upon what vampires ought to know about the history of their own game world...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T17:12:07-08:00","id":1370883,"title":"","content":"Absolutely yes, they should be. Kuei-Jin were probably what I wanted the vampire themes to be about (solidarity based on ideology and spirituality rather than politics or genealogy, default etiquette, education and discipline, preserved traditions, close-knit society, focus on restoration and growth rather than on survival and redemption, more general awareness of the ambivalence of the world around, and many more)<br /> <br /> It definitely had an absurd amount of cheese and shallowness in regards to Asian culture and mythology it was based upon, and I clearly realize it was not a game of undead of East Asian culture, it was a game of undead of westerner's image of East Asian culture. That's what I'd like them to improve, adjust the existing dharmas, make 'heretical dharmas' baseline along with original five, bring more dharmas, expand the regions poorly highlighted in original KotE (Myanmar, Indonesia, New Guinea, Oceania, Manchuria, Russian Far East/Siberia/Mongolia), expand the bridge between kin-jin and kuei-jin primarily via India.. that sort of things.<br /> <br /> I really would like to see a reinvigorated and polished version of KotE in V5, not the total redesign or outright removal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T19:02:52-08:00","id":1371150,"title":"","content":"Honestly Demon's 'christian-centric' depiction never bugged me the same way it didn't in most of the Vampire stuff because it was filtered through layers of ambiguity (myth and legend for Caine, unreliable narrator due to either being embodied for the fallen, insane for the Earthbound, or fractured cosmos. Take your pick.) I think the problem is Demon was really a rush job in a system that wasn't mean to be a rush job. There was alot of implied connections that never really were connected. There was stuff between HtR, KotE and DtF that never got fully developed (nevermind the connections between HtR and KotE that didn't seem to go anywhere.) DtF did have connections to werewolf (ex. Malhim) and VtM of course (Caine), and some to mage (faith and lores) but those were all more fully realized and independent systems with some age behind them (unlike DtF, HtR and maybe KotE) <br /> <br /> I really feel if you were going to revive those you'd do it in a way that tied DtF and HtR together and incorporate elements from KoTE that would fit (but wouldn't fit necessarily with the vampiric side of KotE)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T21:00:58-08:00","id":1371182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1371150#post1371150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly Demon's 'christian-centric' depiction never bugged me the same way it didn't in most of the Vampire stuff because it was filtered through layers of ambiguity (myth and legend for Caine, unreliable narrator due to either being embodied for the fallen, insane for the Earthbound, or fractured cosmos. Take your pick.) I think the problem is Demon was really a rush job in a system that wasn't mean to be a rush job. There was alot of implied connections that never really were connected. There was stuff between HtR, KotE and DtF that never got fully developed (nevermind the connections between HtR and KotE that didn't seem to go anywhere.) DtF did have connections to werewolf (ex. Malhim) and VtM of course (Caine), and some to mage (faith and lores) but those were all more fully realized and independent systems with some age behind them (unlike DtF, HtR and maybe KotE) <br /> <br /> I really feel if you were going to revive those you'd do it in a way that tied DtF and HtR together and incorporate elements from KoTE that would fit (but wouldn't fit necessarily with the vampiric side of KotE)</div> </div> </div> </div>DtF did not bug me nearly as much on that front, because we already had Nephandic demons, Malfean Incarna, Banes, the Wyrm etc all fighting over that role, so while the DtF demons claimed to be THE demons, fallen from grace, builders of the world etc, it was very clear that they were one of many, and probably either insane, or lying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T01:58:21-08:00","id":1371209,"title":"","content":"I just hope &quot;Kue-Jin&quot; never appears as a word.<br /> <br /> There are two acceptable language options<br /> 1- Classical chinese was the lingua franca of Asia historically. Use chinese. But I find Chinese names a lot more difficult to remember because of their conventions are so different.<br /> 2- Use english translations for everything. Not a single Asian word: Hungry ghosts, Ratkin, Werefox. This keeps everything neutral. <span style=\"font-size:8px\"> I'm painfully reminded that V5 replaced &quot;mentor&quot; with a foreign word to seem smart. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Using Chinese for some things and Japanese for others is the height of silly. I'm aware that 'Garou' and 'Bastet are loanwords, but 'Bastet' is very old and 'Garou' goes back a nebulous amount; Very distinctly Japanese words don't fit. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">But now we have the other problem<br /> Who writes this new book?<br /> <br /> White europeans (presumably middle class women) or Chinese-Americans? who think they've got a good understanding of Asian culture from Naruto? no.<br /> <br /> Asians ?<br /> Well, shit.<br /> Any Asian chosen from the job is likely going to be chosen by the <i>problematic</i> people above that have wrote V5 and who overtly wrote 'people who I agree with are good and people who disagree are evil' as if that wasn't a terrible decision. They are likely to have a white editors, who'll cut out all the important cultural stuff that doesn't fit with the politically correct slant they want. Like the huge differences between men and women in most asian societies (and belief systems) that westerners would like to erase. </span><br /> Then we have the question of how a local writers actually do things.<br /> Bar one, I've never read a Chinese, Japanese or Korean comic which mentioned another without trying to shit on it. From what I've heard, South-East Asia is hardly any kinder. Many of these groups have very different views on the same supernatural creatures too. Japanese fox spirits are somewhere between mischevious and malicious but can be good, Korean fox spirits are always natural calamities. Do we tell one group that their interpretation is wrong? (Actualy Fenrir was the good guy!)<br /> What I'm trying to say, is how can we make this not-a-racist/sexist-mess, without actually whitewashing very real cultural attitudes? We can't .<br /> Given how the folk of V5 have absolutely fucked up on the culture-wars of everything west of India, how can we expect good stuff to the east?<br /> <br /> would you trust Michael Bay to adapt the works of Achebe?<br /> <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">(I mean, that's generally how I think V5 is being handled, but it's only subtly racist at the moment, imagine if they got at Asia)</span></span><br /> <br /> More relevant: Would you trust someone to tone down the racism of a risque product when they've already amplified the problems of a safer one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-29-2020, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T02:15:48-08:00","id":1371211,"title":"","content":"Yes, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>, we get it, you hate V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01K