re used to justify the mistakes of the present. As has happened several times all around the globe. Enter the Kindred and the Wan Kuei, now the Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> That would open the door to having &quot;Kuei-jin&quot;-like blood-drinkers in Europe and America, and Cainites in Asia, etc... etc... etc... I still think it could be a very interesting setting, but the... disgusting, cheesy, disturbing implications and possibilities never let me go any deep into that...<br /> <br /> Uhmmm... I wonder...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:03:00-07:00","id":1388381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388358#post1388358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is really a matter of personal taste and preferences...<br /> <br /> Now, going on to something completely different... this thread has been for nine pages, and maybe I'm parroting some ideas, but...<br /> <br /> For a long time, I played with the idea of having, in ancient times, two types (all around the planet) of blood-drinking creatures: &quot;Cainites&quot; (or Kindred, or whatever...) and &quot;Revenants&quot; (or something similar): that is, those who were Embraced and those who returned from the Underworld. Both of them preyed on the Living... so, in the Eastern Hemisphere &quot;Blood Drinking Creatures Type 2&quot; won (due to different causes) and in the Western Hemisphere &quot;Blood Drinking Creatures Type 1&quot; won. If I remember correctly, lemures and larvas (&quot;ghost-vampires&quot; from Roman mythology) were, broadly speaking, quite similar to Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> Then, events became legends and legend became myths and myths were used to justify the mistakes of the present. As has happened several times all around the globe. Enter the Kindred and the Wan Kuei, now the Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> That would open the door to having &quot;Kuei-jin&quot;-like blood-drinkers in Europe and America, and Cainites in Asia, etc... etc... etc... I still think it could be a very interesting setting, but the... disgusting, cheesy, disturbing implications and possibilities never let me go any deep into that...<br /> <br /> Uhmmm... I wonder...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what i did in my iteration of WoD. Revenants have returned to the West in large numbers for the first time in Millennia and shaking things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:51:57-07:00","id":1388397,"title":"","content":"In fact, if I remember correctly, Night Horrors: the Wicked Dead (for V:tR) presented vampires (blood-drinking creatures) that weren't Kindred nor Cainites...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:00:18-07:00","id":1388401,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure who I agree with here. The Wan Kuei and the Drowned Legacies are both non-Cainite vampires, but the Laibon Lineages of Africa are basically just variations on the Western clans (I think; I haven\u2019t actually bought the book yet).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:02:01-07:00","id":1388402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388354#post1388354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the Setites are deluded, they are creatures of Christian myth pretending not to be, and an insult to the historical religion they take influence from. I'd rather no more culture appear in game, than have them ridiculed, degraded and polluted by making them creatures of Christian myth, the real world history of that 'cleansing' and associated genocides should not be mocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's several things here that need to be noted.<br /> <br /> 1. One, it's Jewish myth not Christian. Caine and his peeps have nothing to do with Christianity beyond being adopted by it. This is like saying Herakles is a Roman myth.<br /> <br /> 2. Second, they changed the origin so Caine sacrificed Able rather than killed him out of jealousy. So it is a satirical parodic take on Jewish mythology. Like telling a story where Lilith is a heroine rather than the enemy of pregnant women. I feel that this impacts its interpretation as an artistic presentation of religious iconography. Like saying, &quot;The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina&quot; (where she's the daughter of Satan) is Christian propaganda.<br /> <br /> 3. Chinese mythology is banned by the People's Republic of China with ghosts illegal to talk about. Use of them at all is a form of civic protest.<br /> <br /> 4. I feel that associating it with real life atrocities due to creating a unifying mythology is demeaning to said real life atrocities versus honoring them.<br /> <br /> I make my arguments primarily based on the fact that my association with V:TM fans in Hong Kong and Tawain online are that they tend to hate the Kuei Jin/Wan Kuei and don't WANT them fixed. They want to play Cainites in Hong Kong by Night and their hometowns like any other fans. Why? Because they want to play the game and not be Othered. There's exception to this rule but V:TM fans tend to be fans of the Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat, and other groups that Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei can't participate in like, say, the Laibon or Drowned.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to be persuaded otherwise but I feel that the perspective of fans involved from the cultures should be the primary guide on this. Over in TECHNOCRACY RELOADED, Asian fans had some opinions on the Five Metal Dragons for instance.<br /> <br /> &quot;We want to be Technocrats. Just not ones subordinates to Europeans.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-14-2020, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:22:14-07:00","id":1388408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388401#post1388401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure who I agree with here. The Wan Kuei and the Drowned Legacies are both non-Cainite vampires, but the Laibon Lineages of Africa are basically just variations on the Western clans (I think; I haven\u2019t actually bought the book yet).<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t know what the drowned legacies are yet, but they sound similar to the Laibon but each Legacy might have a unique nondiscipline power much like Changeling Birthrights, and heck they almost sound like mythological beings like Changelings that underwent a vampiric version of the Changeling way with the coming of the Europeans. And the Laibon are vampires that trace their legacy to the God Cagn, which might be the same being as Caine. They don\u2019t call themselves Cainite but they might be Cainites, their biggest diffference is they don\u2019t follow Humanity or roads but have a two part morality trait with one aspected towards heaven and the supernatural and one aspected toward Earth and humanity. What I like about them is they might seem more like demons or gods depending on their rating, and I am very fond of the idea that Vampirism evolves to the point of corpses closely resembling humans, but atavisms exist from the oldest nights when maybe vampires were less spiritually static and have demonic qualities like burning footprints and attract ill omens.<br /> <br /> And the Wan Gui are excellent in the lore and flavor department. What I want most is an update to their rules, and I think the fluff will naturally smooth out. But if they don\u2019t want them then I want them to at least say it, tell us they are wiped out or underwent a change similar to the Cainites. Because at least then it\u2019s easier to houserule anything you don\u2019t like. It\u2019s the worst of both worlds to ignore a whole continent and keep it in limbo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:26:39-07:00","id":1388410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388408#post1388408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Wan Gui are excellent in the lore and flavor department. What I want most is an update to their rules, and I think the fluff will naturally smooth out. But if they don\u2019t want them then I want them to at least say it, tell us they are wiped out or underwent a change similar to the Cainites. Because at least then it\u2019s easier to houserule anything you don\u2019t like. It\u2019s the worst of both worlds to ignore a whole continent and keep it in limbo.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is they should make it so Cainites have always been there and in vast numbers but make Wan Kuei as a supplement to Wraith the Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:42:02-07:00","id":1388417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388410#post1388410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My view is they should make it so Cainites have always been there and in vast numbers but make Wan Kuei as a supplement to Wraith the Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but even if you did that they occupy the same supernatural environmental niche as the Kindred, they would be fighting Kindred for the same territory not wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:02:25-07:00","id":1388424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388417#post1388417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but even if you did that they occupy the same supernatural environmental niche as the Kindred, they would be fighting Kindred for the same territory not wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same sense that Lupines would. However, it wouldn't interfere with Cainite Asian courts politicking and doing the usual VTM things while the Wan Kuei are fighting demons in Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:07:02-07:00","id":1388427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388402#post1388402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's several things here that need to be noted.<br /> <br /> 1. One, it's Jewish myth not Christian. Caine and his peeps have nothing to do with Christianity beyond being adopted by it. This is like saying Herakles is a Roman myth.<br /> <br /> 2. Second, they changed the origin so Caine sacrificed Able rather than killed him out of jealousy. So it is a satirical parodic take on Jewish mythology. Like telling a story where Lilith is a heroine rather than the enemy of pregnant women. I feel that this impacts its interpretation as an artistic presentation of religious iconography. Like saying, &amp;quot;The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina&amp;quot; (where she's the daughter of Satan) is Christian propaganda.<br /> <br /> 3. Chinese mythology is banned by the People's Republic of China with ghosts illegal to talk about. Use of them at all is a form of civic protest.<br /> <br /> 4. I feel that associating it with real life atrocities due to creating a unifying mythology is demeaning to said real life atrocities versus honoring them.<br /> <br /> I make my arguments primarily based on the fact that my association with V:TM fans in Hong Kong and Tawain online are that they tend to hate the Kuei Jin/Wan Kuei and don't WANT them fixed. They want to play Cainites in Hong Kong by Night and their hometowns like any other fans. Why? Because they want to play the game and not be Othered. There's exception to this rule but V:TM fans tend to be fans of the Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat, and other groups that Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei can't participate in like, say, the Laibon or Drowned.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to be persuaded otherwise but I feel that the perspective of fans involved from the cultures should be the primary guide on this. Over in TECHNOCRACY RELOADED, Asian fans had some opinions on the Five Metal Dragons for instance.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;We want to be Technocrats. Just not ones subordinates to Europeans.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating a unified mythology was part of the point of those genocides, don't aid and abet them. That's the point either honour different religions, mythologies etc by not declaring Abrahamic myth true (DtF also does this, and should not have, as much as I like parts of that game), leave things ambiguous, leave room for the interesting conflicts and mechanics of other vampires, other magic traditions, other afterlives etc etc, leave that room for stories, don't straight jacket things into the middle east and Europe are right, everyone else is a deluded, inferior Johnny foreigner as you want.<br /> <br /> Fair point I should have probably said Abrahamic myth, not Christian, the slight alteration to the Caine story is well within the wiggle room of interpretation that faiths in that tradition have used, with different translations, traditions etc disagreeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:46:18-07:00","id":1388440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388427#post1388427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creating a unified mythology was part of the point of those genocides, don't aid and abet them. That's the point either honour different religions, mythologies etc by not declaring Abrahamic myth true (DtF also does this, and should not have, as much as I like parts of that game), leave things ambiguous, leave room for the interesting conflicts and mechanics of other vampires, other magic traditions, other afterlives etc etc, leave that room for stories, don't straight jacket things into the middle east and Europe are right, everyone else is a deluded, inferior Johnny foreigner as you want.<br /> <br /> Fair point I should have probably said Abrahamic myth, not Christian, the slight alteration to the Caine story is well within the wiggle room of interpretation that faiths in that tradition have used, with different translations, traditions etc disagreeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with everything here but I doubt I will persuade you otherwise. I will, however, simply say that if you remove the Abrahamic religion from Demon then you basically remove the premise.<br /> <br /> At the end, I don't think depiction of a religion is endorsement of its worst history.<br /> <br /> But thank you for discussing the issue with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:52:45-07:00","id":1388441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388440#post1388440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree with everything here but I doubt I will persuade you otherwise. I will, however, simply say that if you remove the Abrahamic religion from Demon then you basically remove the premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, which is why it is the most problematic splat line. If it had been Nephandic Umbrood, things from the other side of the deep umbra etc, claiming to be the returned creators, you could maybe have hit similar themes (especially given the Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld conflict that it could have tied into, and the Abyss of Obtenerbration, this thing 3 lines together) you could have built a similar myth arc of fallen servants of the divine, and made it uniquely WoD ( hell CoD tried with it's god-machine if I am not mistaken)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T15:03:31-07:00","id":1388447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388441#post1388441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, which is why it is the most problematic splat line. If it had been Nephandic Umbrood, things from the other side of the deep umbra etc, claiming to be the returned creators, you could maybe have hit similar themes (especially given the Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld conflict that it could have tied into, and the Abyss of Obtenerbration, this thing 3 lines together) you could have built a similar myth arc of fallen servants of the divine, and made it uniquely WoD ( hell CoD tried with it's god-machine if I am not mistaken)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're saying a roleplaying game is inherently problematic by depicting Christian mythology even in a satirical Luciferian sense?<br /> <br /> Serious question: Do you see any place for using real world religion in a tabletop game? Or it Abrahamic religion in particular?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-14-2020, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T15:55:29-07:00","id":1388470,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> thank you. What you said about listening to the Asian fans makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thanks! You got me inspired to buy Kindred of the Ebony Kingdoms \ud83d\ude02.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:40:58-07:00","id":1388483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388424#post1388424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the same sense that Lupines would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, that famous werewolf activity: <i>drinking blood</i>.<br /> <br /> The reason Kindred and Wan Kuei compete with one another is because of blood. Sure, not all Wan Kuei need blood specifically, but most do from what I understand about Kindred of the East. Kindred would complete for blood sources and hunting territory for the same reason Kindred compete with <i>other Kindred</i>. No matter that both groups would have other things going for them, when it comes to vampires, Blood is the bottom line.<br /> <br /> Neither Lupines nor Wraiths are terribly interested in blood (except maybe Red Talons, in the sense they want to see human blood flow for its own sake). The Wan Kuei can be in conflict with them for other reasons, but their very survival puts them at odds with Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-14-2020, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:46:06-07:00","id":1388485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388483#post1388483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes, that famous werewolf activity: <i>drinking blood</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...Kuei Jin DON'T drink blood.<br /> <br /> Only the most pathetic and lowliest of their race do.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *impossibly smug lore grin*<br /> <br /> But yes, basically a big issue is that Kuei-Jin compete with Mages and Werewolves/Hengoyaki because they need caerns while regular vampires don't. They won't compete with Cainites anymore than they would with other supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-14-2020, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:48:00-07:00","id":1388487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388485#post1388485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But...Kuei Jin DON'T drink blood.<br /> <br /> Only the most pathetic and lowliest of their race do.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *impossibly smug lore grin*</div> </div> </div> </div>Most do though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:54:30-07:00","id":1388490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388487#post1388487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most do though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly my point. It doesn't matter if some Wan Kuei don't need blood. It just matters that enough do to make it a resource worth fighting about. If <i>most</i> do, it's functionally identical to All for the purposes of splat-wide antipathy.<br /> <br /> Everybody gangsta about their particular ideological conflict, until someone starts taking their food and making it harder to get more.<br /> <br /> With every other supernatural group, the myriad reasons to get into a conflict are X. With the Kindred, it's X + 1. With the 1 being &quot;Competition Over Feeding Rights&quot;. By definition, they have more to fight about with each other than with other groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T17:00:12-07:00","id":1388491,"title":"","content":"Civilization easily predates Caine even in the middle East it.. gets even sllier when you try to apply to India and China. So there probably should be a solid counter name/theme with Cainites being seen as &quot;Silly&quot; with theirown founders and myths..<br /> <br /> That being said even as someone who liked KOTE I don't think its a good addition for V:TM. I think they have a solid basis for a zombie setup. I think there should be a Zombie game. The Zombie game is the new Wraith. Zombies are the primary character with Ghosts being a secondary splat that can be interacted with. Ghosts try to become zombies and other stuff... My Ghost/Zombie game would perhaps be the most radical departure in that becoming Gods or proper spirits would be a thing.<br /> <br /> So what should Asian Vampires look like? I think we should look at Fera as our Guide. They function relatively like Garou, have some mechanical differences here and there.. have the occasionally radically different story. MAYBE even allow different forms of ressurection.. I mean it works for Requiem that wierd embraces happen....<br /> <br /> I thought the difference between te Deva and Ventrue in DA20 was a pretty good start. Also Ebony Kingdom does good use with unique variants fo discplines and AyA and Orun vs humanity/path. So maybe some tweaks some clan variants....who might claim to be the original. <br /> <br /> Might reuse some of the courts but having been hit by theirown version of the SI having forced them to play nice on a global scale like the Ashirra<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course maybe my opinions will change once we see the V5 sabbat. I always thought of KOTE as &quot;the Sabbat if it wasn't full of shit&quot; Dharmas actually work unlike paths. KJ packs are overseen by spirits. Their rituals shared and potent. Even the Rising from the graves thing wasn't some bullshit fake ritual but something that mattered. Humanity really was seen as the wrong way and a failure.<br /> <br /> if V5 Sabbat continues to fail to live up to the whole &quot;Trans-vampiric&quot; potential it had going for it maybe I will start screaming for KJ as a better counter point to the Cam than the Sabbat..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T17:06:43-07:00","id":1388494,"title":"","content":"Interesting comparison to the Sabbat, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>. I never thought of that.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest weakness of the Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei isn't actually their origin story, though. If I may be so bold as to make a suggestion, the biggest issue with the Wan Kuei is the fact that they are so far removed from V:TM that it's almost impossible to incorporate them into a game with Western vampires. As stated, if a Chinese gamer wants to make a Eastern vampire character, he basically is stuck playing an Eastern vampire game because the characters are set up to never want to have anything to do with the Camarilla, Sabbat, or Anarchs. Which means that they're their own splat that divorces them from the setting. It also deprives Asian settings of the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Anarch conflict that most Asian gamers will want to participate in.<br /> <br /> If Eastern vampires weren't all hostile and actually partcipated in Camarilla and Anarch politics as equals and were accepted as vampires, it'd be a very different scenario, IMHO.<br /> <br /> However, even if they were retconned, they entirely warp the narrative because once introduced you've got Hell, Akuma, Demon Princes, and so on that make regular vampire tussles over turf and humanity look silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T17:37:35-07:00","id":1388504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388402#post1388402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I make my arguments primarily based on the fact that my association with V:TM fans in Hong Kong and Tawain online are that they tend to hate the Kuei Jin/Wan Kuei and don't WANT them fixed. They want to play Cainites in Hong Kong by Night and their hometowns like any other fans. Why? Because they want to play the game and not be Othered. There's exception to this rule but V:TM fans tend to be fans of the Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat, and other groups that Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei can't participate in like, say, the Laibon or Drowned.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to be persuaded otherwise but I feel that the perspective of fans involved from the cultures should be the primary guide on this. Over in TECHNOCRACY RELOADED, Asian fans had some opinions on the Five Metal Dragons for instance.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;We want to be Technocrats. Just not ones subordinates to Europeans.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet when we tell you of our own groups over the decades from Indo, KL and other places who enjoy being able to use local folklore in games and not having to play 'American' vampires you utterly disregard them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T18:21:05-07:00","id":1388513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388504#post1388504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet when we tell you of our own groups over the decades from Indo, KL and other places who enjoy being able to use local folklore in games and not having to play 'American' vampires you utterly disregard them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never done such and I am happy to believe your anecdotes. I speak from my own personal experience but never want to put down anyone else's.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Wan Kuei but I don't dispute anyone who wants them at their games.<br /> <br /> Two different opinions can exist between two people and neither be right on canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We all have our preferences and I respect my own aren't always popular.<br /> <br /> (ANARCHS! MALKAVIANS!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T18:27:18-07:00","id":1388516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388402#post1388402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's several things here that need to be noted.<br /> <br /> 1. One, it's Jewish myth not Christian. Caine and his peeps have nothing to do with Christianity beyond being adopted by it. This is like saying Herakles is a Roman myth.<br /> <br /> 2. Second, they changed the origin so Caine sacrificed Able rather than killed him out of jealousy. So it is a satirical parodic take on Jewish mythology. Like telling a story where Lilith is a heroine rather than the enemy of pregnant women. I feel that this impacts its interpretation as an artistic presentation of religious iconography. Like saying, &amp;quot;The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina&amp;quot; (where she's the daughter of Satan) is Christian propaganda.<br /> <br /> 3. Chinese mythology is banned by the People's Republic of China with ghosts illegal to talk about. Use of them at all is a form of civic protest.<br /> <br /> 4. I feel that associating it with real life atrocities due to creating a unifying mythology is demeaning to said real life atrocities versus honoring them.<br /> <br /> I make my arguments primarily based on the fact that my association with V:TM fans in Hong Kong and Tawain online are that they tend to hate the Kuei Jin/Wan Kuei and don't WANT them fixed. They want to play Cainites in Hong Kong by Night and their hometowns like any other fans. Why? Because they want to play the game and not be Othered. There's exception to this rule but V:TM fans tend to be fans of the Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat, and other groups that Kuei-Jin/Wan Kuei can't participate in like, say, the Laibon or Drowned.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to be persuaded otherwise but I feel that the perspective of fans involved from the cultures should be the primary guide on this. Over in TECHNOCRACY RELOADED, Asian fans had some opinions on the Five Metal Dragons for instance.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;We want to be Technocrats. Just not ones subordinates to Europeans.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Christian Myth incorporates Jewish myth, I would call Hercules very much a Roman Myth. Otherwise if have signs some myths were Etruscan doesn\u2019t remove them from Greek Myth. I mean we use the Roman name for Hercules most often. We use Greek Achilles rather then Etruscan Achillius.<br /> <br /> 3. What was this in reference too? The government bans them but Chinese people still enjoy them as much as other countries, I would watch ghostly anime and American media with my Chinese roommate all the time.<br /> <br /> 4. History is included in game history. Famines and pograms shouldn\u2019t be ignored for convenience.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m Asian with a Asian friends online and in real life. I will say this, most would favor normal Vampire, but the reasoning is not how you describe, it\u2019s usually because they never had a copy of Kindred of the East because it\u2019s mostly a 2nd ed source and they are not likely to have read a niche product in a niche hobby. Those who have read read it usually like it just fine, more or less, but people don\u2019t like having to remember multiple rule sets. It\u2019s why when we have Anime it usual depicts western vampirism, it\u2019s the kind of media most often familiar to them, as you said superstition was silenced. It\u2019s similar even in Europe though, Romanians often will only remember vampire stuff from movies and not to the point of folks who dive into the genre. Though there are exceptions, like some families like to still hear stories of monsters from the older generation. And the Philippines and Japan never had the censorship that China had so there a lot of common myths and folklore, same with South America.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nice not having everything needing an Abrahamic lens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T18:29:55-07:00","id":1388519,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I don't want to play gatekeeper with people's hobbies either. I may not like the Wan Kuei at my table but I don't want to ever say someone is wrong for liking it either.<br /> <br /> I see some weaknesses and have friends who feel the same but I know it does have it sfans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:14:05-07:00","id":1388526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388485#post1388485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But...Kuei Jin DON'T drink blood.<br /> <br /> Only the most pathetic and lowliest of their race do.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *impossibly smug lore grin*<br /> <br /> But yes, basically a big issue is that Kuei-Jin compete with Mages and Werewolves/Hengoyaki because they need caerns while regular vampires don't. They won't compete with Cainites anymore than they would with other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're in the market for spiritual or power sites, wouldn't they kind of compete with the Tremere and Giovani/Heketa? Because the former have their ley line nexus points, and the latter have their 2spooky4u gathering locales for necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:54:10-07:00","id":1388540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388447#post1388447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're saying a roleplaying game is inherently problematic by depicting Christian mythology even in a satirical Luciferian sense?<br /> <br /> Serious question: Do you see any place for using real world religion in a tabletop game? Or it Abrahamic religion in particular?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using is fine, declaring any real world religion to be the one closest to being true is not, you can have them be parts of a truth, attempts to explain something inexplicable etc, but flat declaring a winner I will always have a problem with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:57:27-07:00","id":1388543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388540#post1388540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using is fine, declaring any real world religion to be the one closest to being true is not, you can have them be parts of a truth, attempts to explain something inexplicable etc, but flat declaring a winner I will always have a problem with</div> </div> </div> </div>So isn't that an argument to make them a separate splat? Or would you like Werewolf not to have a true cosmology?<br /> <br /> This is me serious, FYI.<br /> <br /> I just want to know how you view it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T20:08:54-07:00","id":1388546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388543#post1388543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So isn't that an argument to make them a separate splat? Or would you like Werewolf not to have a true cosmology?<br /> <br /> This is me serious, FYI.<br /> <br /> I just want to know how you view it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I don't think they would be financially viable as a separate splat, and are the best thematic fit within Vampire, (I also don't like the African bloodlines, as an aside), making it so things are less monolithic I would be fine with, so cities, towns and entire states being fought over would be interesting ( sorry if this rambles is really late but insomnia sucks)<br /> <br /> As to Werewolf being true...it isn't, even in universe it's a best fit attempt, as Mage and Wraith make utterly clear, with their spirit world's, the Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld are real, but they don't seem to be what the werewolves think they are, and the Wolves have no idea what the hell the Nephandi worship, or what is making deals with Infernalists (mostly, some are clearly Wyrm spirits, others not so much), or what exactly is at the bottom of Oblivion and being purely fictional this mythos doesn't have the baggage anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:42:42-07:00","id":1388562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388519#post1388519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I don't want to play gatekeeper with people's hobbies either. I may not like the Wan Kuei at my table but I don't want to ever say someone is wrong for liking it either.<br /> <br /> I see some weaknesses and have friends who feel the same but I know it does have it sfans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh but at home games I generally don't mind if the Storyteller says they want to change canon. I Mean I would sigh wistfully if Garou didn't exist but Werewolves were simple cursed men that turn into Wolves, but I would be okay with the Storyteller making the Campaign their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:46:24-07:00","id":1388563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388519#post1388519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I don't want to play gatekeeper with people's hobbies either. I may not like the Wan Kuei at my table but I don't want to ever say someone is wrong for liking it either.<br /> <br /> I see some weaknesses and have friends who feel the same but I know it does have it sfans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also how is asking for them not to exist at all not gatekeeping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T22:02:05-07:00","id":1388565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388563#post1388563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also how is asking for them not to exist at all not gatekeeping?</div> </div> </div> </div>In what sense do you mean?<br /> <br /> I don't work for Paradox and the question asked is, &quot;Should they exist in V5 or not.&quot; I gave my opinion. I don't begrudge people who disagree.<br /> <br /> If you want them in your games, that's your business.<br /> <br /> I think it's a better story if they were Cainites and Asia wasn't cut off from the rest of the setting but people at my own table disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:07:06-07:00","id":1388579,"title":"","content":"I think the Wan Kuei should be in V5, especially since they are in BJD which has been the metaplot bridge between V20 and V5. I think they should be a different splat, but I also think there should be some sort of VtM style vampires existing in Wan Kuei territory. However I think that Kindred of the East and Demon the Fallen should be merged mechanically as they have many similarities.<ul><li>Similarities/Merging Mechanics - This is far from complete or exhaustive, more of just some of the things that crossed my mind<ul><li>Both involve a demonic essence escaping an extraplanar prison, having a human frame, and dealing with some aspects of human mindset.<ul><li>For Demon's the P'o represents their tormented side while the Hun their angelic</li> <li>The &quot;human&quot; they are influences what nomenclature they use - a side effect of multilayered reality and incomplete memories of their time before their imprisonment</li> </ul></li> <li>Both involve game-crossover<ul><li>Demon tries to explain various WoD splats through itself, Wan Kuei interact with each of the various types (ghosts, hsien, spirits, etc)</li> </ul></li> <li>The Archdukes can be compared with the Yama Kings<ul><li>The Baali's Children of the Outer Darkness could be another group of such entities</li> </ul></li> <li>There's tales of pacts with the devil signed in blood, what if that's simply mortal misunderstanding of low &quot;Dharma&quot; (more on that below) Demons feeding on blood while succubi and the like are misunderstanding of Demons that can feed on breath<ul><li>With some tweaking Followers, Pacts, Thralls, and Herd could be merged into a one or two backgrounds</li> </ul></li> <li>Coming up with some sort of storage method like Jade shouldn't be that difficult, whether it's retooling the concept of reliquary and/or using different types of gemstones to be equivalent to the different types of Jade.</li> <li>I don't think Faith and Chi are irreconcilable. At the basic level Yin+Yang Chi is like Faith while Demon Chi is like Torment.<ul><li>People showing signs of possession could be explained as mortals misunderstanding a &quot;Yin&quot; aspected Demon or suffering a &quot;Chi&quot; imbalance</li> </ul></li> <li>Retooling Rites, Lores, Disciplines, and some of the inherent abilities into a single system just given different nomenclature.<ul><li>Apocalyptic form isn't that different from demon shintai, and the lore of flame could be ghost-flame shintai as just a couple of examples</li> </ul></li> <li>Both games have redemption among their themes Demon with trying to get rid of their torment and KotE having the road to enlightenment<ul><li>The Houses are translated into Dharmas, representing the Demon's understanding of what their role should be.<ul><li>If the idea of an Demon being able to choose a different House from what they were before they fell, just explain it as the influence of their human side. Demon made a big deal of the spark of divine within humanity, that spark allows a Demon to tweak their role<ul><li>It could feed into the whole idea that it's all part of the divine plan - the angels made choices that caused them to fall now they have a choice to fulfill a duty; in the same way their human part has a second chance at life to fix what sin sent them to hell in the first place</li> <li>Or it could be that their imperfect memories means they misremember what their role is or confuses it with a close ally, and that as long as they are attempting to fill a role as an angel it's a step towards redemption or that in falling they lost their role and part of their redemption involved finding one again</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Earthbound and unrepentant/pure evil demons are equatable with akuma<ul><li>Perhaps have some mechanic for akuma to bind themselves to a location, the Wan Kuei use of dragon lines and dragon nests could feed into this. By binding themselves to a single location they form an artificial dragon nest that has aspects similar to a broken mirror</li> </ul></li> <li>Tales of nephilim and the son of a demon/the devil are mortal misunderstanding of the &quot;dhampir&quot; or &quot;Yang&quot; aspected/imbalanced Demons</li> <li>Neither got another edition to smooth over and fix the mechanical issues within them, meaning their rules are less refined</li> </ul></li> <li>There's nothing saying they have to be the same at all, just use the same mechanics<ul><li>Any of the similarities above could be coincidence if the ST wants</li> </ul></li> <li>Things this method fixes<ul><li>Abrahamic religion is no longer treated as being correct. Bringing in the idea of a multilayer reality allows for any number of deific entities to be the source of the Wan Kuei/Demons</li> <li>Regionality is more easily explained as the influence of their human part<ul><li>It explains why Wan Kuei haven't been rising in the west, they have they're just Demons/Angels/Jinn/Ifrit etc</li> <li>It could also be related to conflicts between the Archdukes, Yama Kings, and any other equivalent as they've made their little hells and claimed territory in the mortal world as &quot;theirs&quot; (or they are actually different)</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>VtM style vampires/Cainites in KotE territory<ul><li>They could be like the way the Drowned Legacies are described, something slightly different while still very similar to vampires</li> <li>They could be new clans descending from other antediluvians (similar to the above with &quot;Caine&quot; being a being cursed by a deific entity for murder in a multilayered reality)</li> <li>They could be bloodlines of the existing clans like how Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom appear<ul><li>Any disconnect from the main body of the clan is because whatever Methuselah founded them had no desire to deal with their kin (just look at Dracon slaying Triglav for ways Cainites don't always get along with their broodmates)</li> </ul></li> <li>In another thread I posited the idea that Xue might be a 3rd Generation vampire that left before the other Antediluvians rose up and slew their sires. As such he was uncursed by Caine. Instead his childer's Clan curse is a combination of a stronger beast (the P'o) and their Generation being tied to enlightenment rather than who sired who. The former is the product of Xue's experiments with the beast and trying to find balance while the later is Xue limiting his childer knowing that too much power in the hands of the unenlightened is a recipe for disaster<ul><li>A similar idea would be to have Xue be an equivalent to Caine, not necessarily the same being but another who was cursed (by the August Personage of Jade perhaps) and ended up with the same flaws as western Cainites<ul><li>In the same way maybe Caine isn't the sire of all the current Clans of vampires. Maybe the Setites and Banu Haqim are on to something with tales of their progenitors</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> I admit it's hardly perfect and it won't please everybody but I think it solves a number of religious and regional concerns that regularly crop up when KotE are discussed while still allowing everyone the chance to have what they like. The same is true of the brief discussion of VtM style vampires<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:31:53-07:00","id":1388587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369702#post1369702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to look at KotE is &quot;do you want to play vampire, but without the usual baggage&quot;?<br /> <br /> V:tM is a stand alone system while KotE is a kitchen sink cross over system.<br /> V:tM is about being isolated from humanity while KotE has a strong family connection theme and other Asian community values<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V:tM is about hiding the supernatural while KotE is about managing the supernatural balance<br /> V:tM is about Caine screwing up and you being collateral damage, while KotE is about you screwing up your life and paying for it.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V:tM is about being an emo teenager for eternity while KotE is about growing up/maturing for power gain.<br /> <br /> I would say that what needs to happen with the Kuei-jin is their mechanics need a serious overhaul to remove excess bloat and crunch, then fold the heretical dharmas into the original ones, make the dharmas much less antagonistic to everyone, and finally retcon the california invasion. KotE was a good alternative flavor of vampirism, but it was used in a poor fashion in relation to the metastory of the game line.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. I haven't read even the core book yet but this sounds very interesting and more attractive to me than the normal VtM take.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T00:34:55-07:00","id":1388591,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar727_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"727\" data-vbnamecard=\"727\">Thoth</a> Excellent points, you are really selling me on KotE, but I mean I was already sold on it! :P<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it would be worthwhile if Vampire had something like a sect, or a faction of the Anarchs that accepts any supernatural that wants to support the Masquerade, or at least other Undead like Risen and Wan Gui.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:05:27-07:00","id":1388609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thanks. Again, this is really helpful.<br /> <br /> I like the Wan Gui and I hope they do come back in some form in V5, but I also hope they include Asian Cainites as well. I think the two can coexist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:33:40-07:00","id":1388615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388609#post1388609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thanks. Again, this is really helpful.<br /> <br /> I like the Wan Gui and I hope they do come back in some form in V5, but I also hope they include Asian Cainites as well. I think the two can coexist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, like the region around India seems to have an equal amount of Cainites and Wan Gui, and it rocks as a setting. And I have bloodlines exist in Wan Gui Territory, no way is it only the childer of Zao-lat that survive there. In fact it really seems like the Ravnos should have made inroads in other parts of Asia, since their mission was to war with the Wan Gui. And Gangrel and Nosferatu are great at surviving and hiding. And the Lasombra book says they explored China. I also have the Talmaherah experiment with making Cainite Bloodlines in Asia based off the 4 Divine Beasts, and a revenant family for each of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:52:42-07:00","id":1388619,"title":"","content":"What an interesting thread this is becoming! Thanks you all for your interesting comments, specially <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a>... Excuse if I miss anyone whose posts I enjoyed reading...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:55:44-07:00","id":1388620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388615#post1388615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely, like the region around India seems to have an equal amount of Cainites and Wan Gui, and it rocks as a setting. And I have bloodlines exist in Wan Gui Territory, no way is it only the childer of Zao-lat that survive there. In fact it really seems like the Ravnos should have made inroads in other parts of Asia, since their mission was to war with the Wan Gui. And Gangrel and Nosferatu are great at surviving and hiding. And the Lasombra book says they explored China. I also have the Talmaherah experiment with making Cainite Bloodlines in Asia based off the 4 Divine Beasts, and a revenant family for each of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I mean canonically there are Cainites everywhere throughout Asia except perhaps mainland China ( and theres probably a few there, the damn things are like cockroaches). Books have detailed Cainite populations of Japan, Korea, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Mongolia, SE Asia, South Asia etc.<br /> <br /> They're everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:00:02-07:00","id":1388622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388620#post1388620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I mean canonically there are Cainites everywhere throughout Asia except perhaps mainland China ( and theres probably a few there, the damn things are like cockroaches). Books have detailed Cainite populations of Japan, Korea, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Mongolia, SE Asia, South Asia etc.<br /> <br /> They're everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically, now, Tokyo is a Camarilla City.<br /> <br /> I remember reading the Lasombra Clan Book which talked about how the Lasombra used to influence the Imperial throne of China, which indicated that the Eurocentrism hadn't taken root yet in the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:04:36-07:00","id":1388624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388615#post1388615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely, like the region around India seems to have an equal amount of Cainites and Wan Gui, and it rocks as a setting. And I have bloodlines exist in Wan Gui Territory, no way is it only the childer of Zao-lat that survive there. In fact it really seems like the Ravnos should have made inroads in other parts of Asia, since their mission was to war with the Wan Gui. And Gangrel and Nosferatu are great at surviving and hiding. And the Lasombra book says they explored China. I also have the Talmaherah experiment with making Cainite Bloodlines in Asia based off the 4 Divine Beasts, and a revenant family for each of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very, very interesting paragraph. Excuse me, what are the 4 Divine Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:08:39-07:00","id":1388625,"title":"","content":"I'm again remembering a Dark Ages chronicle I storytold during the summer of... 2017, I guess, set in Lahore. The main characters were three European/Mediterranean Cainites (Lasombra, Malkavian and Assamite) sent by their sires to look for a fabled &quot;Black Lotus&quot; that was supposed to free Cainites from their Hunger. In the city they ended trapped in a three-side conflict between Indian... undead from the Face of the Gods Dharma, Ravnos Indian (and Hindu and Jain) Kindred, Muslim (and Hindu) Assamites and Daytya and Danava Kindred... oh, and a Jain Salubri...<br /> <br /> It was pretty amazing and the players enjoyed it a lot...<br /> <br /> Maybe I should gather all my notes and sell it in the Storyteller's Vault... Uhmmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 05-15-2020, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:15:56-07:00","id":1388626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388620#post1388620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I mean canonically there are Cainites everywhere throughout Asia except perhaps mainland China ( and theres probably a few there, the damn things are like cockroaches). Books have detailed Cainite populations of Japan, Korea, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Mongolia, SE Asia, South Asia etc.<br /> <br /> They're everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not in large numbers, at least not in modern times, the Anda were arguably the dominant bloodline of the Gangrel in their time and they were oddly genocided by a vague ritual.<br /> <br /> In revised Cainites would seem to have a foothold in the Areas around India, probably fading to a trickle around Thailand. Korea had a enclave of refugee Nagarajah. And the Islands influenced by Europe, like Singapore, Hong Kong, Macau, ect allowed for Cainites to compete with the Wan Gui in very specific territories. Otherwise the Giovanni were permitted limited diplomatic/business options in China. But Mainland and Japan were harsh lands for the Kindred, and Tibet had hermit Children of Osiris, some who achieved Golcanda but it was also the Holy heart of the Wan Gui territory that they seemed cursed not to be able to withstand. Only the Wu Zao were able to survive in the deep core of Wan Gui territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> It leaves room so that my headcanon is Cainites survive in Asia but at beast they would be viewed comparable to Caitiff in the more lenient territories, or they invested enough manpower to claim a foothold city. Meanwhile I would probably do the same allowing Wan Gui in Asian communities in the west with the Assumption that if they stayed they are outnumbered and have to carve out defended territories or Wander. So in locals were the Ravnos Vacuum was prominent it left enough of a power vacuum for a new faction of Kindred to cooexist with outcast Wan Gui, like Heretical Dharmas and the like. As well as Baali teaming up with Akuma. And I have Indonesia/Malaysia/Philippines have native bloodlines of Cainites who if they ever were part of the main clans they forgot long ago like most of the Laibon, and they are competing with the Wan Gui.<br /> <br /> But it would be Ironic if the Demonic Vampires are the ones that are most prone to get along and kumbaya with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:26:30-07:00","id":1388629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388625#post1388625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm again remembering a Dark Ages chronicle I storytold during the summer of... 2017, I guess, set in Lahore. The main characters were three European/Mediterranean Cainites (Lasombra, Malkavian and Assamite) sent by their sires to look for a fabled &quot;Black Lotus&quot; that was supposed to free Cainites from their Hunger. In the city they ended trapped in a three-side conflict between Indian... undead from the Face of the Gods Dharma, Ravnos Indian (and Hindu and Jain) Kindred, Muslim (and Hindu) Assamites and Daytya and Danava Kindred... oh, and a Jain Salubri...<br /> <br /> It was pretty amazing and the players enjoyed it a lot...<br /> <br /> Maybe I should gather all my notes and sell it in the Storyteller's Vault... Uhmmm...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:35:22-07:00","id":1388633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388626#post1388626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But not in large numbers, at least not in modern times, the Anda were arguably the dominant bloodline of the Gangrel in their time and they were oddly genocided by a vague ritual.<br /> <br /> In revised Cainites would seem to have a foothold in the Areas around India, probably fading to a trickle around Thailand. Korea had a enclave of refugee Nagarajah. And the Islands influenced by Europe, like Singapore, Hong Kong, Macau, ect allowed for Cainites to compete with the Wan Gui in very specific territories. Otherwise the Giovanni were permitted limited diplomatic/business options in China. But Mainland and Japan were harsh lands for the Kindred, and Tibet had hermit Children of Osiris, some who achieved Golcanda but it was also the Holy heart of the Wan Gui territory that they seemed cursed not to be able to withstand. Only the Wu Zao were able to survive in the deep core of Wan Gui territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> It leaves room so that my headcanon is Cainites survive in Asia but at beast they would be viewed comparable to Caitiff in the more lenient territories, or they invested enough manpower to claim a foothold city. Meanwhile I would probably do the same allowing Wan Gui in Asian communities in the west with the Assumption that if they stayed they are outnumbered and have to carve out defended territories or Wander. So in locals were the Ravnos Vacuum was prominent it left enough of a power vacuum for a new faction of Kindred to cooexist with outcast Wan Gui, like Heretical Dharmas and the like. As well as Baali teaming up with Akuma. And I have Indonesia/Malaysia/Philippines have native bloodlines of Cainites who if they ever were part of the main clans they forgot long ago like most of the Laibon, and they are competing with the Wan Gui.<br /> <br /> But it would be Ironic if the Demonic Vampires are the ones that are most prone to get along and kumbaya with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>As stated Tokyo is nominally a Camarilla city, Korea also had Camarilla enclaves as did Vietnam, Malaysia, Indonesia and Cambodia. As most of the local Hungry Ghost courts in the SE Asian region are Thrashing Dragons or Heretic Dharmas I doubt they really give a shit about them as long as they keep their noses out of local business.<br /> <br /> <br /> A very large area that should have equal numbers of Hungry Ghosts and Kindred are the 7-stans. I don't think any books have covered the area. It would be very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:41:58-07:00","id":1388634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388624#post1388624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Very, very interesting paragraph. Excuse me, what are the 4 Divine Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are God Beast Guardians of the 4 cardinal directions. I had a secret project of some Talmaherah, the most prominent of whom is a Daitya who helped engineer a Taoist Vampiric Sorcery through his knowledge of Sadhana and the aid of a Dur-An-Ki Ashipu, and a Nagarajah Necromancer, create the first generation of the four bloodlines and a clan of mortal revenants who they are embraced from. They act as agents believing themselves literally descended from the blessings of the Gods in their blood.<br /> <br /> \u767d\u864e/Baihu/the White Tiger of the West<br /> They serve as the Warriors and Assassins.<br /> <br /> \u9752\u9f99/Qinlong/the Azure Dragon of the East<br /> They serve as the sages, sorcerers, and probably the closest to the leaders.<br /> <br /> \u7384\u6b66/Xuanwu/ the Ebon Tortoise of the North<br /> They serve as the sentinels and guardians, very much the defense to the White Tiger's Offense.<br /> <br /> \u6731\u96c0/Zhuque/ the Vermillion Bird of the South<br /> They serve as the scouts, diplomats, and spies, notably they have the Discipline of Flight as a favored Discipline.<br /> <br /> Being the project multiple potent methuselahs and their strict control of who is embraced the Four Clans are of notably low generation, but of small but growing numbers. They understand if they misstep they could be crushed by the Wan Gui who outnumber them. But they have notable populations in China, Taiwan, Singapore, Japan, Vietnam and Korea.<br /> <br /> You might recognize their Japanese names Byakko the White Tiger, Suzaku the Phoenix, Seiryu the Blue Dragon, and Genbu the Turtle. They are common in the stories and traditions of countries that they spread to from China. The principles of Fengshua tie them to the directions and Japan even has them in Buddhist and Shinto temples and gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:45:14-07:00","id":1388636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388633#post1388633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As stated Tokyo is nominally a Camarilla city, Korea also had Camarilla enclaves as did Vietnam, Malaysia, Indonesia and Cambodia. As most of the local Hungry Ghost courts in the SE Asian region are Thrashing Dragons or Heretic Dharmas I doubt they really give a shit about them as long as they keep their noses out of local business.<br /> <br /> <br /> A very large area that should have equal numbers of Hungry Ghosts and Kindred are the 7-stans. I don't think any books have covered the area. It would be very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did have a World of Darkness Hong Kong and Tokyo and it had some interesting NPCs like the 48th Ronin, maybe my favorite idea for a Wraith NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:55:49-07:00","id":1388638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388636#post1388636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They did have a World of Darkness Hong Kong and Tokyo and it had some interesting NPCs like the 48th Ronin, maybe my favorite idea for a Wraith NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I've got those two. I tend to throttle them down a little as they approach Chicago levels of gonzo in parts but they're solid books...even if the geography is a bit off in both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T04:12:51-07:00","id":1388639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388638#post1388638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I've got those two. I tend to throttle them down a little as they approach Chicago levels of gonzo in parts but they're solid books...even if the geography is a bit off in both.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also very much feels like it was was written early in the Kindred of the East development, like Ancestors and other potent Kindred of the East never go past five in disciplines but have a robust amount of lower level disciplines, much like how they handle V5 or Requiem Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T04:39:13-07:00","id":1388644,"title":"","content":"As I am comming from W20 as first exposing in WoD and my only run downs with Wang Kue are in Bloodlines and the Malkavian Character in V20 from HK I would love them be part in 5 so I could learn more of them. I only fear that they will botchered again with this time having to much Political Correctness. A japanese friend of mine ranting always how I and the rest of the western media so gravely misinterpret japan from just looking that afar. Though more I would love a KotE20 book because I like more the old gameplay and my english as an austrian is only good enough for talking but not enough for reading P&amp;P books and enjoying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T04:45:07-07:00","id":1388651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388609#post1388609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thanks. Again, this is really helpful.<br /> <br /> I like the Wan Gui and I hope they do come back in some form in V5, but I also hope they include Asian Cainites as well. I think the two can coexist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only people in Asia calling themselves Cainites should be converts to the Church of Caine. They should have theirown localized groups with theirown history. They don't need to be theirown supernatural type but if they are calling themselves Cainites and clearly just funny hat clans its... a fail.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T05:30:49-07:00","id":1388655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388651#post1388651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only people in Asia calling themselves Cainites should be converts to the Church of Caine. They should have theirown localized groups with theirown history. They don't need to be theirown supernatural type but if they are calling themselves Cainites and clearly just funny hat clans its... a fail.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they're Asian Christians, Jews, or Muslims.<br /> <br /> How many Muslims live in Asia?<br /> <br /> 1.4 <b><i>billion</i></b><br /> <br /> This is part of the reason that I think the Wan Kuei have some serious problems because they're basically engaged in a lot of ethnocentricism. Not only did they combine Chinese and Japanese and Indian mythologies (three VERY different ones) but they basically cede the entirety of region's mythology to their 1000 Hells interpretation. Part of the reason why I bring up it's not JUST Christian mythology is the fact, again, a huge chunk of that part of the world DOES believe in the Myth of Cain and Abel.<br /> <br /> At least metaphorically.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure this would mean the Banu Haqim and Ashirra would have a sizeable chunk of territory there.<br /> <br /> So with 1/4th of all people there believing in a Abrahamic worldview, how does that influence the Wan Kuei since you don't have to believe in the 1000 Hells to be a Wan Kuei--just live in the region?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-15-2020, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T05:50:05-07:00","id":1388657,"title":"","content":"There would certainly be a an Ashirra presence in Indonesia. That said being Muslim is no issue for a Hungry Ghost outside the Quincunx, ( outside of the usual issues of being a dead thing that lives on blood and still trying to follow the sunnah).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T06:03:47-07:00","id":1388659,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting how this question never really goes away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Fixed spelling. 05-15-2020, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T06:16:38-07:00","id":1388662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388659#post1388659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fi6it interesting how this question never really goes away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it boils down to the fact the Wan Kuei have a lot going for them. It's just figuring out how to polish off the rough spots.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how I hated the Ravnos but the Revised Ravnos are some of my favorite Kindred, so I wonder why they were wiped out anyway.<br /> <br /> I've never hated the Wan Kuei, I just prefer a unified cosmology and rules set. They were very fun villains in Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-15-2020, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T07:44:11-07:00","id":1388676,"title":"","content":"@Lian okay, how about Kindred? That\u2019s not Abrahamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T07:52:11-07:00","id":1388677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388655#post1388655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless they're Asian Christians, Jews, or Muslims.<br /> <br /> How many Muslims live in Asia?<br /> <br /> 1.4 <b><i>billion</i></b><br /> <br /> This is part of the reason that I think the Wan Kuei have some serious problems because they're basically engaged in a lot of ethnocentricism. Not only did they combine Chinese and Japanese and Indian mythologies (three VERY different ones) but they basically cede the entirety of region's mythology to their 1000 Hells interpretation. Part of the reason why I bring up it's not JUST Christian mythology is the fact, again, a huge chunk of that part of the world DOES believe in the Myth of Cain and Abel.<br /> <br /> At least metaphorically.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure this would mean the Banu Haqim and Ashirra would have a sizeable chunk of territory there.<br /> <br /> So with 1/4th of all people there believing in a Abrahamic worldview, how does that influence the Wan Kuei since you don't have to believe in the 1000 Hells to be a Wan Kuei--just live in the region?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably they end up dead at the hands of the Cainites who are already hiding in those populations, before they ever get found by the Courts.<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> If they don't, well their Dharma would certainly be different and how they view the spirits they have to deal with. Apart from that, what culture they would have..who knows. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> You are right about the mashing together of cultures having been a bad idea, it tainted a great concept. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T08:40:16-07:00","id":1388690,"title":"","content":"This has been an interesting thread to read, it has helped me a lot with considering how I might want to handle the Wan Kuei in my own stories. There are a couple of points that have been brought up which have raised a question I have regarded the lore developed for the 'Middle Kingdom' and its relation to the wider mythology of the WoD. There has been some back and forth on the extent to which the portrayal of Asian culture and mythology in KotE and related content has been accurate or respectful. People have also debated the extent to which the mythologies of VtM and DtF depend on Abrahamic religion being true to some degree, and whether or not that subordinates other cultural and religious perspectives.<br /> <br /> Now, a great deal of my knowledge of the World of Darkness comes from wiki-browsing, but much of what I have read on this forum suggests that the wiki shouldn't be treated as an ironclad source. But, on the wiki, &quot;August Personage of Jade&quot; immediately redirects to the article for (the Judeo-Christian) God, while &quot;Emerald Mother&quot; sends you to WtA's &quot;Gaia.&quot; Obviously, Storytellers can do what they wish with their own game, but it seems to me like this relationship is as close to canon as you generally get from White Wolf. My question is, to those in the thread more familiar with various Asian cultures and mythologies than myself, how accurate or respectful is that particular bit of canon-welding to the source material? It seems a lot easier to reduce the mythic/historic perspectives of VtM/DtF to &quot;just one point of view&quot; when something capable of fulfilling the role of God in their myths doesn't relegate all other myths to falsehoods and distortions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T08:43:23-07:00","id":1388692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388662#post1388662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of like how I hated the Ravnos but the Revised Ravnos are some of my favorite Kindred, so I wonder why they were wiped out anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all Chimestry dude. <br /> <br /> <br /> Ravnos are a very fun clan to play with. People not liking the Ravnos after revised did so out of ignorance, just like how some people don't like the Tremere and wanted to make something new out of them, or how the Camarilla's monopoly is wonderful and vital to the setting. Chimestry is such a fun and creative discipline, second only to dominate, though you really need to read up on it because the descriptions in the corebook are a little lacking; I love the philosophical bent of needing to understand that your chimestry creations are both real and not. . And whilst the path of paradox was initially a mess,<i> Lore of the Clans </i>comes with paradox variations which are <i>the best paths ever </i>(Except maybe honourable accord?) Samsara is my jam. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, if the book says the Ravnos ante really did die, that's just a great example of the effectiveness of Chimestry. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://wrestlingsmarks.com/data/avatars/l/14/14597.jpg?1576204398\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T09:22:49-07:00","id":1388700,"title":"","content":"I think the final trick of the Ravnos Founder was to turn their world in the WoD RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:49:47-07:00","id":1389249,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say there\u2019s a good basis for a sect of vampires, sort of like a quasi-Buddhist counterpart to the Ashirra or Camarilla, but it needs to be redesigned pretty heavily, they don\u2019t need to be their own species, and the name \u201ckuei-jin\u201d has absolutely got to go.<br /> <br /> It helps if we keep in mind that the Caine myth is... well, a myth. \u201cCainites\u201d haven\u2019t always believed it. Could have some truth to it, but it\u2019s been filtered through the lens of the dominant culture, which in the case of the Camarilla was medieval Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-17-2020, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T04:56:30-07:00","id":1389251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389249#post1389249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say there\u2019s a good basis for a sect of vampires, sort of like a quasi-Buddhist counterpart to the Ashirra or Camarilla, but it needs to be redesigned pretty heavily, they don\u2019t need to be their own species, and the name \u201ckuei-jin\u201d has absolutely got to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, &quot;kuei-jin&quot; should stay, has a nice ring to it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:05:18-07:00","id":1389256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389251#post1389251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, &quot;kuei-jin&quot; should stay, has a nice ring to it</div> </div> </div> </div>I must disagree. It\u2019s a linguistic impossibility that tries to cram two languages\u2019 morphemes together in a way that only someone who didn\u2019t speak either language would think was possible. Nor is there any way to write it in the languages in question so that it would be pronounced this way. There\u2019s just no way the term could have been coined and survived all this time. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s as bad as the fake Latin that keeps popping up in the Sabbat material, even though the Sabbat was founded by vampires whose grasp of Latin should have been excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:08:34-07:00","id":1389259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389256#post1389256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must disagree. It\u2019s a linguistic impossibility that tries to cram two languages\u2019 morphemes together in a way that only someone who didn\u2019t speak either language would think was possible. Nor is there any way to write it in the languages in question so that it would be pronounced this way. There\u2019s just no way the term could have been coined and survived all this time.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s as bad as the fake Latin that keeps popping up in the Sabbat material, even though the Sabbat was founded by vampires whose grasp of Latin should have been excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div>you seem to forget that this is a game, not a latin degree<br /> <br /> the fake latin parody is what gives it its charm,<br /> same for the church titles and the wack chinese-japanese in kote","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:16:14-07:00","id":1389264,"title":"","content":"Kue-Jin might work as a specific name for Cathayans in California or Sydney or some place outside of Asia where the Japanese and Chinese both have had a big presence and needed to set aside their differences to work together against the Cainite threat.<br /> <br /> It doesn't work anywhere else. Difficult topic, but For hundreds of years, the Japanese and Chinese have (broadly speaking) hated each-other. Even before Japan went imperial and commited all kinds of acts that the Chinese are having a hard time forgiving, the Chinese thought all Japanese were pirates, because most Japanese they dealt with <i>were</i> pirates. The Japanese that weren't pirates thus thought the chinese were... not very nice to them. I don't want to go to into it because I don't want to get in trouble, but the Chinese have historically thought themselves the centre of the world and culture, with the most divine head of state, and they've had the richest lands. They wouldn't demean themselves by mixing up their name with the Japanese unless they had too. The &quot;lingua franca&quot; of asia was of course, Classical chinese, so if the &quot;Cathayans&quot; are going to agree on a name for<i> all of them</i> that westerners can use, they'll use that. Otherwise they will call themselves something wholly in their language (an All-Vietnamese name, an All-Korean name, An All-japanese name) they would never, ever use a portmantau.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:34:18-07:00","id":1389273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389264#post1389264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kue-Jin might work as a specific name for Cathayans in California or Sydney or some place outside of Asia where the Japanese and Chinese both have had a big presence and needed to set aside their differences to work together against the Cainite threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, this plays into an irony of the Kuei-Jin there.<br /> <br /> By smashing all the Asian mythology together, they're basically doing the same thing they've been accused of doing with making Cainites and Eastern Vampires the same.<br /> <br /> Incompatible mythologies pushed together for ease of storytelling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't work anywhere else. Difficult topic, but For hundreds of years, the Japanese and Chinese have (broadly speaking) hated each-other. Even before Japan went imperial and commited all kinds of acts that the Chinese are having a hard time forgiving, the Chinese thought all Japanese were pirates, because most Japanese they dealt with <i>were</i> pirates. The Japanese that weren't pirates thus thought the chinese were... not very nice to them. I don't want to go to into it because I don't want to get in trouble, but the Chinese have historically thought themselves the centre of the world and culture, with the most divine head of state, and they've had the richest lands. They wouldn't demean themselves by mixing up their name with the Japanese unless they had too. The &quot;lingua franca&quot; of asia was of course, Classical chinese, so if the &quot;Cathayans&quot; are going to agree on a name for<i> all of them</i> that westerners can use, they'll use that. Otherwise they will call themselves something wholly in their language (an All-Vietnamese name, an All-Korean name, An All-japanese name) they would never, ever use a portmantau. </div> </div> </div>The generalizing here isn't particularly good but there's quite a bit of truth about conflicts (speaking as a guy with his college degree in Asian history). So I'm not too harsh on it and I agree Kuei-Jin is a word that should never be used versus Wan Kuei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:07:22-07:00","id":1389285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389273#post1389273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The generalizing here isn't particularly good but there's quite a bit of truth about conflicts (speaking as a guy with his college degree in Asian history). So I'm not too harsh on it and I agree Kuei-Jin is a word that should never be used versus Wan Kuei.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not wrong, Kuei-Jin is CHINESE+JAPANESE, whereas Wan Kuei is just Chinese, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:14:07-07:00","id":1389286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389285#post1389285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm not wrong, Kuei-Jin is CHINESE+JAPANESE, whereas Wan Kuei is just Chinese, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> They tried to clean up the Wan Kuei a bit in BJD but my understanding is Paradox's take on them is much harsher as a whole. Matthew Dawkins has shared, and I paraphrase, &quot;The problem is that if we cleaned them up as much as we wanted to, it wouldn't really be the Kuei Jin anymore so we're not sure how to proceed.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T07:53:54-07:00","id":1389306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389259#post1389259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you seem to forget that this is a game, not a latin degree<br /> <br /> the fake latin parody is what gives it its charm,<br /> same for the church titles and the wack chinese-japanese in kote</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not forgetting anything. For people who actually understand these languages, and there\u2019s a good number of us, screwing them up to that degree isn\u2019t charming; it\u2019s immensely distracting at best, often just plain tiresome, and it\u2019s lazy work on the part of the authors. <br /> <br /> Also, \u201ckuei-jin\u201d just doesn\u2019t work. Even in California, Sydney, etc., for reasons that are hard to explain in brief, this is not at all how Chinese and Japanese get mixed together, which in the real world they do all the time. In fact \u201cJin\u201d is a Japanese pronunciation of a Chinese word to begin with. Chinese-speakers would just say it in Chinese if they came across it, and Japanese speakers would use a Japanese pronunciation for the first character. <br /> <br /> As an analogy, we have a lot of French loanwords in English, and there are conventions for these things. But there\u2019s no way to write a standard word so that people pronounce the first half in a French way and the second half in an English way. That\u2019s about the level of absurdity we\u2019re talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:00:07-07:00","id":1389308,"title":"","content":"Again, and again, and again, I remember the laughs (and the tears) when I read in Clanbook: Lasombra (no idea whether it was 1st edition or Revised) &quot;Les Amies Noirs&quot; (wrong) = &quot;Las amigos negras&quot; (wrong again, in a different language). (Of course, in French it would be LES AMIS NOIRS or LES AMIES NOIRES)<br /> <br /> I mean, Google Translator didn't exist at that point in history, but was it so difficult to ask someone to use a dictionary, to use a dictionary or to find a person who spoke real Spanish?<br /> <br /> Also, I remember the headbutt I got from one J* A* (former developer of a game called V*:t*M* and writer for V*:t*R* when I told him, in the White Wolf Forums... &quot;If Lancea Sanctum means what you say it means, it is wrong&quot; and he replied &quot;It is impossible to know how it was said in Latin&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Note: I'm a teacher. I teach English in Secondary School. According to the Council of Europe, I have a C2 degree in English. According to Cambridge, I have a Proficiency degree. According to my I.D. and secondary education degrees, I'm a native Spanish speaker)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 05-17-2020, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:04:51-07:00","id":1389311,"title":"","content":"It also makes no sense because Kuei-Jin doesn't function with a non-Latin alphabet.<br /> <br /> The kanji would be totally different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:16:17-07:00","id":1389317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389286#post1389286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They tried to clean up the Wan Kuei a bit in BJD but my understanding is Paradox's take on them is much harsher as a whole. Matthew Dawkins has shared, and I paraphrase, &quot;The problem is that if we cleaned them up as much as we wanted to, it wouldn't really be the Kuei Jin anymore so we're not sure how to proceed.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is where my previous discussion of merging KotE with Demon comes in. It allows those thorny bits to be cleaned up in such a way that the &quot;in game&quot; manifestations of those can be laid at the feet of malefic entities or misunderstanding and misinformation among the Kindred.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","user":"Cynic01","date":". 05-17-2020, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T17:44:17-07:00","id":1389501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389308#post1389308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, and again, and again, I remember the laughs (and the tears) when I read in Clanbook: Lasombra (no idea whether it was 1st edition or Revised) &quot;Les Amies Noirs&quot; (wrong) = &quot;Las amigos negras&quot; (wrong again, in a different language).</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of grammatical gender just baffles a lot of people who aren\u2019t used to it. There are people who honestly do not believe that it could possibly be important or that a failure of agreement could render a phrase nonsensical, just because it\u2019s no longer a thing in their native language. <br /> <br /> \u200bSee also <i>Manus Nigrum </i>and <i>Lancea Sanctum</i>. In both cases the writer has tried to modify a feminine noun with a neuter adjective. A Swedish company came out with a product called <i>Lex Occultum</i>, same exact problem. They assume all nonhuman things are neuter. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I remember the headbutt I got from one J* A* (former developer of a game called V*:t*M* and writer for V*:t*R* when I told him, in the White Wolf Forums... &quot;If Lancea Sanctum means what you say it means, it is wrong&quot; and he replied &quot;It is impossible to know how it was said in Latin&quot;. </div> </div> </div>All the classical scholars I know just died a little. Fun fact: there are more Latin-speakers in the world now than at any point in history (not native, obviously, but as you know, non-native doesn\u2019t mean ignorant). Yet it\u2019s apparently too damn hard to consult with a single one of them. Or French or Spanish or Chinese or Japanese. And don\u2019t get me started on the Sanskrit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:54:17-07:00","id":1389522,"title":"","content":"I insist that it is CAMA-RILLA<br /> <br /> Not Cama-RIA.<br /> <br /> Why should the vampire society be pronounced right!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T19:11:23-07:00","id":1389525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389522#post1389522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I insist that it is CAMA-RILLA<br /> <br /> Not Cama-RIA.<br /> <br /> Why should the vampire society be pronounced right!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, the eternal shibboleth!<br /> <br /> I do speak Spanish, but I\u2019m with you on this one. Most languages, including English, that have adopted the word pronounce it with the L sound. I remember my surprise when I found the word \u03ba\u03b1\u03bc\u03b1\u03c1\u03af\u03bb\u03b1 in Greek. It\u2019s a surprisingly global word, not a bad choice for the sect after all.<br /> <br /> Now, if only people would pronounce <i>Sabbat </i>correctly! \ud83e\udddb\ud83c\udffb<br /> <br /> \u200b(<i>Sabbatojin</i> in Japan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:09:46-07:00","id":1389997,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> that there's nothing charming about the Sabbat's shitty Latin (and similar linguistic blunders -- the fancy English term for a duel is <i>monomachy,</i> not &quot;monomacy.&quot;) One day I should make a topic about fixing all of White Wolf's bad Latin in particular, if only to put stuff like &quot;Auctoritas Ritae&quot; to bed forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:13:55-07:00","id":1389998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1389997#post1389997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> that there's nothing charming about the Sabbat's shitty Latin (and similar linguistic blunders -- the fancy English term for a duel is <i>monomachy,</i> not &quot;monomacy.&quot;) One day I should make a topic about fixing all of White Wolf's bad Latin in particular, if only to put stuff like &quot;Auctoritas Ritae&quot; to bed forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do, I\u2019ll be there. And yes, it\u2019s kind of amazing how simple typos have been perpetuated across editions, just because people don\u2019t know the words they\u2019re using, isn\u2019t it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T13:07:50-07:00","id":1390364,"title":"","content":"YMMV strikes again. I grew up in the typically insular US-centric bubble that WoD developed in, so learning about these things doesn't surprise me because I always saw the setting as blinded by its own conceits. It doesn't make the system terrible mind, and I still enjoy it, but I do think its worth noting those flaws and problems they create (notably things like KotE and KotEK) that stemmed directly from such similar 'blinders.' Something I find charming is going to annoy someone else because they have a context informing that which I lack. Won't be the first time such things have bitten WoD on the butt, and probably won't be the last. <br /> <br /> I think its safe to say while some of the Pre-V20 (or even V20) concepts can be recycled, they probably wouldn't ever be lifted out and transplanted verbatim and without change. Times change, and so will the material to at least some degree. For example, while the 'origin/nature' and alot of the fluff of the KotE game may be changed, I think alot of the mechanics and their intentions could be adopted in some form. I always did like how they tied 'development' to virtue/belief rather than to generation. I consider that a good 'alternative' to Vampire development, and I think it provides a more workable and nuanced approach to Golconda than the 'all or nothing' approach. And given that Saulot either received or stole the Golconda concept from the East it fits rather well IMHO. <br /> <br /> Indeed you could adopt such mechanics to alot of belief systems OTHER than humanity. Under Golconda or other methods. Like I think it has uses in salvaging parts of Ebony Kingdom that made them weaker than 'European' Kindred, of course I always interpreted that material to sort of ignore generational limits anyhow so it wasn't THAT great a transition since there were similarities to KotE there too. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T10:57:24-08:00","id":1431710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369765#post1369765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Similarly, but of an older vintage. the case of the Order of Hermes's favored practice, the Enochian language. It's like Klingon for Christian Alchemists!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a random unrelated aside, i would like to point out that Enochian comes from the writings of John Dee. That is a Tremere in VtM.<br /> I bet the Tal'Mahe'Ra is very much <i><b>not </b></i>amused....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T14:46:32-08:00","id":1436082,"title":"","content":"I really like the Wan Kuei (or Hungry Ghosts, if you prefer), and would love to see a <b>playable update</b> for the Storyteller 5th edition, and don't mind in what format it comes (supplement, splat, companion)... And yeah, to get the culture, politics, views and history right and weave it well with the WoD part of the game (which is the most important) is a tricky problem, that requires sensitive and smart solutions. A lot of talking I would say. <br /> <br /> For me also, the Wan Kuei are more like a &quot;<b>spiritual/ghost vampire</b>&quot;, as opposed to the &quot;<b>blood vampire</b>&quot; that are the Cainites and Laibon (let's call them Kindred for simplicity sake), and maybe the Drowned Legacies too. As such, these spiritual vampires are much more akin to wraith (restless dead), demons/changelings/mummies than the kindred, but I think it's fair to call them either vampires or hungry ghosts. But what is interesting for me is that as souls that came back to their bodes not only they are akin to revenants (as real world folklore), but also that they could and maybe should be present in other cultures. In my view, Hungry Ghosts or spiritual vampires should be present in practically every region with animistic culture. And they could, more than most, rub shoulders with mummies often (as the Undying would mostly sniff them out to find if they are following a righteous path or not), as they are both beings of spirit returned to their body in some way. And interesting note also, is how in <b>Demon the Fallen</b>, it is said that &quot;in the beginning&quot; the reality was multifaced, and the Creation was as much Abrahamic angels with wings molding the world, as particles and electrons and heat making the universe in the course of hundreds of thousands of years. That would mean that they could be Olorum's (Yoruba) many faces or even agents shaping the lands and skies, or Atum who made Tefnut and Shu who made Geb and Nut (Egyptian) whose creations and breeding made the world itself, or even the Chinese Taoist &quot;the Way gave birth to unity, unity gave birth to duality, duality gave birth to trinity, trinity gave birth to the myriad creatures&quot;. Everything could be right, and the idea that after the Fall, the Age of Wrath and the Deluge the multifaceted reality became shattered and not singular permits that all myths and religions to be somewhat true in it. I mean, you could say that August Personage of Jade, and the Dragon and Empress could be all analogs to &quot;angels&quot; or even to the creator himself. In that way, the Cainites and the Wan Kuei would both have been cursed by angels (I mean, most of the curses of Caine were laid down by angels). In that sense, they are basically two sides of the same coin, the Kindred and the Hungry Dead.<br /> <br /> The spiritual vampires as I said could, in that way, be present in America, Africa, Asia, Oceania and even some regions of Europe too. Just as the Kindred should also be. I mean, I agree, the blood vampires should be <b>worldwide phenomenon</b>. As they are not bound by land, belief or spirits (and that's maybe), so they probably already are in Asia, having their fill, and probably wrestling with Hungry Dead for territory, herd and secular power. I would even assume that the tradition Asian Kindred, like the Laibon of Africa, wouldn't be too keen on having American or European Kindred (what we could say are the Cainites) invading their territory, and would try to keep them away (maybe that way the Cainites think the Wan Kuei did what mostly other Kindred did?). So yeah, they would <b>coexist</b>, and some fun power dynamics could be had, and still maintain that: while the written material until now was true, there has been some misunderstanding (like there not having Kindred in Asia, only Hungry Dead, before Cainites). And I mean, we saw how V5 maintained a lot of truths while reshaping the setting and the system (which I'm biased to say I loved wholeheartedly); blood, generations, bonds, disciplines, clans, it all kind of changed, but yet stayed the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> So in the end I want to see the Wan Kuei anew, and I think they should still be non-Kindred (but that there should be traditional Kindred in Asia, and other continents, as well), even if the P'o, Hun, Yin and Yang and Dharma part be a little retooled or at least simplified, cuz I remember how time-consuming and annoying was to keep track of the Hierarchy of Sin, even worse when there were two simultaneously with the Laibon, or even worserer when there were multiple Paths of Wisdom in a table. And even now with V5 sometimes I forget the Ressonance and Humors when in play, so I want less with more punch (personally). I understand that it could be just me being bad at multitasking d=<br /> <br /> Some other idea would to irritate both old and new fans alike by making the Wan Kuei capable of <b>Embracing </b>via rituals (like something out of Mummy), or even a newfound power to spit the Dharma infused chi into a corpse (like the Embrace via vitae) of a willful soul, making it comeback most the same way of the Hungry Dead (with some 2 months time till then maybe). Of course, this expenditure of Chi and especially Dharma would be heavy (like Embracing in 5th edition), and not something to make Wan Kuei pop like water on hot oil.<br /> Buuuut I would only make this if people really wanted to make the Wan Kuei more akin to Kindred, and would be more of a metaplot change than anything (a new way to do Wan Kueis). I mean, technically the Bodhisattvas were gone, the last Great Maelstrom wrecked the shit out of the spiritual world, and all the Hungry Dead society would be in disarray or at the very least at a moment of change and reorganization. Not much different from the changes of V5. But who knows, I'm not sure we are going to get Wan Kuei anytime soon, and although I love them and is homebrowing them up, I'm not in a hurry to see them 5thfied. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T21:08:55-08:00","id":1436137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1436082#post1436082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really like the Wan Kuei (or Hungry Ghosts, if you prefer)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this entire post. And I agree with its conclusion. But I also doubt there is way make a simple (in terms of game mechanics) generic, universal vampire or hungry ghost that is not a Kindred. Or at least not one fans will embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T21:38:47-08:00","id":1436146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1436137#post1436137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this entire post. And I agree with its conclusion. But I also doubt there is way make a simple (in terms of game mechanics) generic, universal vampire or hungry ghost that is not a Kindred. Or at least not one fans will embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Thank You !! =D<br /> This entire Forum has been awesome, and I'm glad to be part of it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I too don't think it would be easy. But hey, V5 did a lot of things I thought would never happen, so a man can dream, and until then I will homebrew something, or at the very least work the concept in my table and setting. Hell, if I get enough pumped up I might make an STV book about it, although I'm not as used to V20 as I am to V5, and for now and probably for a while we won't be able to make V5 material in it. Either way, I liked the idea, so at least I will used it, and will be slowly working on a homebrew for Hungry Dead on V5. It should be as fun as it is hard.<br /> But V5 just came out, kinda, so we might still see the Drowned Legacies, Laibon and other vampires very slowly, bit by bit, if we are luck lol.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T12:06:29-08:00","id":1436250,"title":"","content":"The funny thing is that several things in V5 were more or less taken from KotE. The concept of Coterie or Wu composition having mechanical interactions, the concept that like Demon Shintai disciplines are built with choices, etc.<br /> <br /> KotE will always be a niche game due to the cultural knowledge requirements on the part of the ST &amp; Players to make it really click. Vampire on the other hand has been largely removed from any particular cultural influence on a game level from the start. Thus KotE will never be a flagship line for White Wolf, but it is an excellent side project that adds some much needed variation for playing a &quot;vampire&quot; in the main line.<br /> <br /> Sadly it's not like White Wolf can just try to sell KotE in parts of asia to make up for the line not selling in western countries. The biggest markets with disposable income in asia each comes with its own issues. Japan is the home of anime, south Korea has e-sports, and china..... has made it illegal to use time travel or other story elements that revise history, thus making most of the meta story of WoD that is based on real world history an automatic problem, this is also on top of the variety of problems where the dark, gritty, over sexualized, edgelord nature of WoD would probably be banned by chinese cultural ministers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T12:39:20-08:00","id":1436262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1436137#post1436137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this entire post. And I agree with its conclusion. But I also doubt there is way make a simple (in terms of game mechanics) generic, universal vampire or hungry ghost that is not a Kindred. Or at least not one fans will embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the best way to incorporate KotE in a broader context would be a wholesale rewrite of the Risen from Wraith; perhaps even tying in Mummy as a specific brand of magic that makes the process easier.<br /> <br /> My specific thinking is that Risen might be a general type, with KotE and Mummies as specific cultural expressions of that supernatural type with strengths and weaknesses akin Clans or Traditions, find 3-5 more expressions (perhaps the classic revenant/vengeful ghost concept might be one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T17:04:24-08:00","id":1436324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1436262#post1436262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the best way to incorporate KotE in a broader context would be a wholesale rewrite of the Risen from Wraith; perhaps even tying in Mummy as a specific brand of magic that makes the process easier.<br /> <br /> My specific thinking is that Risen might be a general type, with KotE and Mummies as specific cultural expressions of that supernatural type with strengths and weaknesses akin Clans or Traditions, find 3-5 more expressions (perhaps the classic revenant/vengeful ghost concept might be one).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of this - but it might be something best handled by fan supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T18:30:52-08:00","id":1436479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1436324#post1436324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like all of this - but it might be something best handled by fan supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Or it might be something that would play a larger role in a potential Wr5 since one of the original goals when Paradox took over was a \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d where all the supernaturals are on the same playing field and Risen can interact with the other splats WAY more easily than Wraiths typically do.<br /> <br /> I will say though that I\u2019d really need to see what at least W5 looks like mechanically before I could really judge how well Risen might be adapted into the 5e system.<br /> <br /> I mean, I had a VERY easy time creating streamlined mummies and KotE that referenced only mechanics within V20, by using a slightly looser interpretation of clan weaknesses that included straight up trade-offs in addition to weaknesses; but the powers in V5 are a lot more mechanically specific and physical states simplified in ways that might make it harder to do a proper Risen concept.<br /> <br /> Within the complexity of the X20 and earlier rules the associations that make KotE more a culturally specific expression of a Risen are clearer... ex. instead of a conduit for the Risen\u2019s Shadow, the KotE incorporate the Shadow directly into themselves in the form of the Po (which enables them to sidestep some of the normal difficulties in becoming a Risen) while Vulnerability to sunlight might be their Risen type weakness (akin to a clan weakness, but for different types of Risen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T19:23:32-08:00","id":1436490,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think, for me, the biggest challenge for the people developing <b>WtA5</b> is (or was) not only make a Rage (or similar) marker/tracker that works in a way similar to Hunger in V5 but isn't an exact copy (because the idea is awesome, but each supernatural should have it work in different ways). Not only that, but reworking the expansive setting of Werewolf, and especially the <b>Umbras </b>and Spiritual World (and the spirits of course) are a big deal, like, for more than half the other game lines. So they could try to make the scope smaller, give just some tidbits of info, just enough to work but no enough to understand it completely (I guess the Forsaken did something similar). And well, we are kind of under the impression that the Umbra and Underworld are both under a shitstorm, are still under I should say. But these new definitions for the setting will be very important, so must be handled with care, although games of Mummy and Demon are kind of made with that in mind....<br /> <br /> Either way, I think the shake up of the spiritual storm (which I hope is given other reason other than the spiritual bombs, that don't make sense for many settings to know about) is cool for the World of Darkness, especially for Werewolf and the Wan Kuei. And I'm waiting for WtA5 to make some conclusions on my own headcanon/homebrew of the Hungry Dead. And the Drowned Legacies and Laibon would probably get some too.<br /> <br /> But.... a<b> Risen outbreak</b> could be possible because of it (I almost remember somewhere stating that the Risen frequency has gotten higher because of the Spiritual Storm) and as such, the devs. could try to make Wan Kuei suffer the Second Breath even faster (or the opposite) and/or make some changes about them, and even mash them up with the other Risen, only that they have their own society, philosophy and developed powers. Although it would take some work lorewise, and quite some time to adapt all (or most of) the functions and distinctions between the two, and there ain't exactly a popular option here (it has been mostly to keep it down, and wait for local companies to contact them for it, if this Forum's information is right).<br /> In some way I hope for Werewolf and Wraith 5th edition to come out before anything playable on the Wan Kuei (otherwise I think it would be lacking in depth, but it doesn't prevent it from being any good), and also before Mage (I love Mage, but the system M20 left me confused and the setting for me is a mess, that needs both mechanically and setting-wise to be treated by a mature and experienced 5th edition team). <br /> ...I may have ran a train of thought a bit too far from the forum's tracks ={ <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T19:25:33-08:00","id":1436491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1436479#post1436479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. Or it might be something that would play a larger role in a potential Wr5 since one of the original goals when Paradox took over was a \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d where all the supernaturals are on the same playing field and Risen can interact with the other splats WAY more easily than Wraiths typically do.<br /> <br /> I will say though that I\u2019d really need to see what at least W5 looks like mechanically before I could really judge how well Risen might be adapted into the 5e system.<br /> <br /> I mean, I had a VERY easy time creating streamlined mummies and KotE that referenced only mechanics within V20, by using a slightly looser interpretation of clan weaknesses that included straight up trade-offs in addition to weaknesses; but the powers in V5 are a lot more mechanically specific and physical states simplified in ways that might make it harder to do a proper Risen concept.<br /> <br /> Within the complexity of the X20 and earlier rules the associations that make KotE more a culturally specific expression of a Risen are clearer... ex. instead of a conduit for the Risen\u2019s Shadow, the KotE incorporate the Shadow directly into themselves in the form of the Po (which enables them to sidestep some of the normal difficulties in becoming a Risen) while Vulnerability to sunlight might be their Risen type weakness (akin to a clan weakness, but for different types of Risen).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're being a stickler for actual differences between a Vigor Soul and a Jungian Shadow, that might not work out so well. Broadly speaking, the systems differ in that the Po should theoretically be a mass of all of a Wraith's Passions, Shadow or otherwise, while the Hun covers the Fetters. You can ignore this, of course, but then, you aren't really using the cosmological concepts, so you might as well just use the Jungian terms and give them an Angst rating in place of Po.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:51:18-08:00","id":1438258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1369899#post1369899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've seen otherwise in Chicago by Night with the Touchstones. But yes, a bit like Spider-Man, being a friend to mortals can expose them to danger.<br /> <br /> I recommend a really touching relationship on display in THE SACRIFICE accompanied by a terrible one by Red Moon Roleplaying. Matthew Dawkins is amazing and terrifying in that one [and not the guy with a good Touchstone].</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had seen them. I hate the entire concept and it has no place in VtM, it is a paedophilia/domestic violence simulator put in by the same people who put in neonazi heroes and paedophile vampires as the goal to strive for (I saw their insincere apology and claims of ignorance, I just didn't believe them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:54:56-08:00","id":1438260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438258#post1438258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had seen them. I hate the entire concept and it has no place in VtM, it is a paedophilia/domestic violence simulator put in by the same people who put in neonazi heroes and paedophile vampires as the goal to strive for (I saw their insincere apology and claims of ignorance, I just didn't believe them)</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read GHOULS: FATAL ATTRACTION?<br /> <br /> Just checking.<br /> <br /> Vampires abusing their slaves and victims is pretty much a well-established thing from the start of the franchise.<br /> <br /> Its not something players should do but the point of MD's character is he's an evil piece of shit.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying it doesn't endorse it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:57:20-08:00","id":1438262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438260#post1438260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read GHOULS: FATAL ATTRACTION?<br /> <br /> Just checking.<br /> <br /> Vampires abusing their slaves and victims is pretty much a well-established thing from the start of the franchise.<br /> <br /> Its not something players should do but the point of MD's character is he's an evil piece of shit.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying it doesn't endorse it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Making it a required mechanic does endorse it. Now you can only be human thru domestic, physical and sexual abuse. It used to be a choice: Do you have Ghouls? Do you avoid humans? Now it isn't, you have to be an abuser. (Which is a fine option for a character, but should not be the requirement, any more than being on a path should be mandatory)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-06-2021, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:01:20-08:00","id":1438265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438262#post1438262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making it a required mechanic does endorse it. Now you can only be human thru domestic, physical and sexual abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can also be the kid you put through college.<br /> <br /> If you believe vampires can only show affection through abuse, the Touchstone doesn't actually change that or make it less prominent.<br /> <br /> So I can't help but think you just hate Touchstones because they're linked to regaining Humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:08:41-08:00","id":1438266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438265#post1438265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can also be the kid you put through college.<br /> <br /> If you believe vampires can only show affection through abuse, the Touchstone doesn't actually change that or make it less prominent.<br /> <br /> So I can't help but think you just hate Touchstones because they're linked to regaining Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Theirs two parts to it: But the first part: The kid you put through college: you painted a massive target on them by doing so, your enemies know the easiest way to destroy you is to hit your touchstones and drive you to wassail, and by the mechanics of touchstones, you cannot allow them to change in any way, they have to stay the same, you have to make them static, they graduate? You have to drive them back into college, Get a partner? Nope they have to stay the same, so you have to destroy that relationship. That is the RAW, they have to stay perfect, you have to abuse them <br /> <br /> The second part is with the externalising of moral struggle, morality (and hence humanity/path) is THE internal struggle, it is the most private and personal thing, it is literally the war within the mind, having it be parasitised onto an external relationship robs it of all narrative power and makes it morality pokemon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:14:04-08:00","id":1438268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438266#post1438266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Theirs two parts to it: But the first part: The kid you put through college: you painted a massive target on them by doing so, your enemies know the easiest way to destroy you is to hit your touchstones and drive you to wassail, and by the mechanics of touchstones, you cannot allow them to change in any way, they have to stay the same, you have to make them static, they graduate? You have to drive them back into college, Get a partner? Nope they have to stay the same, so you have to destroy that relationship. That is the RAW, they have to stay perfect, you have to abuse them<br /> <br /> The second part is with the externalising of moral struggle, morality (and hence humanity/path) is THE internal struggle, it is the most private and personal thing, it is literally the war within the mind, having it be parasitised onto an external relationship robs it of all narrative power and makes it morality pokemon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the static part of things is being overemphasized. They're meant to be a reminder of your humanity but dealing with the changing of Touchstones is something to handle in game, I think to do stories baout Humanity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Betsy used to remind you of your teenage daughter. She's grown up now, getting married, and is a dental hygenist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you find a new Touchstone or try to adjust to her life.<br /> <br /> Trying to find tools to keep yourself sane is like finding ethical blood. It's HARD but being hard is kind of the point of the game. Yes, also, it could be putting a target on their backs but living in the World of Darkness puts a target on your back too.<br /> <br /> Having a vampiric patron is also an advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:21:43-08:00","id":1438271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438268#post1438268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the static part of things is being overemphasized. They're meant to be a reminder of your humanity but dealing with the changing of Touchstones is something to handle in game, I think to do stories baout Humanity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Betsy used to remind you of your teenage daughter. She's grown up now, getting married, and is a dental hygenist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you find a new Touchstone or try to adjust to her life.<br /> <br /> Trying to find tools to keep yourself sane is like finding ethical blood. It's HARD but being hard is kind of the point of the game. Yes, also, it could be putting a target on their backs but living in the World of Darkness puts a target on your back too.<br /> <br /> Having a vampiric patron is also an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> that does nothing to negate the morality pokemon aspect. Morality is internal, it is personal, it is not a tamagothi (to show my age, and yes I meant gothi not gotchi)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","