:0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T07:13:38-08:00","id":1438309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438305#post1438305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact: One of the Chicago by Night 1st Edition characters is a Malkavian film director who achieved Golconda and is living among humanity as a normal guy.<br /> <br /> He'd be ashamed and saddened for what Damien's become.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, IIRC it was Rebekah that found Golconda by hermitage and fasting, but I haven't looked thru that book in a while. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T08:33:24-08:00","id":1438317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1438309#post1438309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yup, IIRC it was Rebekah that found Golconda by hermitage and fasting, but I haven't looked thru that book in a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also through Jewish rituals, which notably are very social but I understand why many prefer the &quot;Isolated Yoda&quot; trope for Golconda.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T17:48:02-07:00","id":1443429,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering how they'll handle the issue of the Kuei Jin in the future. It's kind of weird to note that so much of 5th Edition is about promoting Bloodlines as the basis for how &quot;vampire&quot; is supposed to be played but they're effectively erasing an element that was a central part of that game. On the other hand, Paradox really might just want to remove it entirely from the gameworld and pretend it doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> I do hope they address it in some way, though. If they have to do it then have the Thousand Hells open up and swallow up the Kuei-Jin with the final battle against the Yama Kings finally happening. I think I'd prefer that instead of just OOC saying that they never existed in the first place. Mind you, I'd like for there to have always been Cainites in Asia as well.<br /> <br /> Its a difficult needle to thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T18:33:23-07:00","id":1443431,"title":"","content":"They were mentioned in <i>Night Road</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T18:42:18-07:00","id":1443432,"title":"","content":"Oh? Did Night Road say anything about them or just name drop them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T21:55:06-07:00","id":1443441,"title":"","content":"I think they could be downgraded in spectacle and numbers, you could say either Maelstrom (through other names), death of the 3 Bodhisattvas at Bangladesh, endless battle against the Sabbat that is also advancing on their territory imbued with powerful blood... or going to fight the Yama Kings in their own Gehenna/Apocalypse/Reckoning, although that probably would mean a complete annihilation of the Wan Kuei, with only a handful being left.<br /> They could work better as a very small society in each city or hermits, because their society is a bit too big as it was in the corebook. But the way they work internally, the Dharmas, the struggles, the magic/power systems, the possible stories and chronicles, are just too cool to throw away. Of course it has a lot of exaggeration and stereotype, which isn't a good thing, but 100% &quot;Westernize&quot; it doesn't seem the right call neither. And yeah, I think there probably are &quot;Cainites&quot; (vamps that drink only blood and burn in the sun) in Asia, and probably always were, many times called Kuei-Jin or Cathayans by Europeans and Americans by mistake and ignorance. That's how I imagine, and the &quot;real&quot; Wan Kuei probably wouldn't respect them either, thinking them as lesser spiritually.<br /> <br /> This very thread said there was some talk that they wouldn't officially do anything with Wan Kuei until something like a local company or studio do it, so it really isn't something we can be sure is going or not to happen. I do hope it does, cuz I would love Wan Kuei in 5th edition Storyteller. But I understand they're a bit niche, and mostly misunderstood or downright hated. Also, it seems the IPs are taking longer to release, and we kind of don't have any confirmation on Mage, Wraith or Changeling, much less Demon, Mummy or Kindred of the East, so it really might take one hell of a time before we even get to know if it is a &quot;100% no&quot;, &quot;maybe, or &quot;yes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T06:14:10-07:00","id":1443468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1443432#post1443432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? Did Night Road say anything about them or just name drop them?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I recall reading, the &quot;Wan Kuei&quot; and Ming Xiao were just name dropped. The former was part of a small list of terms, along with Sabbat and Carna, that the PC knew as a ghoul, but tdidn't understand. I think that Ming Xiao's name was associated with some sort of magical tool offered as a reward for the DLC's new mission. Also, the Great Leap Outward was one of the issues that caused the Giovanni to &quot;panic&quot; in recent years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T06:43:02-07:00","id":1444194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1443468#post1443468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I recall reading, the &quot;Wan Kuei&quot; and Ming Xiao were just name dropped. The former was part of a small list of terms, along with Sabbat and Carna, that the PC knew as a ghoul, but tdidn't understand. I think that Ming Xiao's name was associated with some sort of magical tool offered as a reward for the DLC's new mission. Also, the Great Leap Outward was one of the issues that caused the Giovanni to &quot;panic&quot; in recent years.</div> </div> </div> </div>can I get a source on this? since I don't have Night Road and what small info did they give about them?<br /> <br /> speaking of this topic, if the wan kuei are retconned, hope the writers would use the gaki from wod 1e and make their origins more muddier since i don't want another sad copy paste like Canarl or Cagn.<br /> <br /> their clan bane would be them being eternally hungry for blood even if there is abundance of it, since hungry ghosts and pretas in myth are insatiable and can never be satisfied. idk about their clan compulsion but probably similar to something like the shadow/p'o. their disciplines would be oblivion, potence and obfuscate, their discipline of rift from wod1e would be an amalgam of obfuscate and oblivion but don't know if this is a good combination.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T08:15:07-07:00","id":1444208,"title":"","content":"In the latest episode of <a href=\"http://www.kenandrobintalkaboutstuff.com/index.php/episode-441-cheese-made-of-cheese/\" target=\"_blank\">Ken and Robin Talk About Stuff</a> they discuss story possibilities set in Cambodia, specifically ones dealing with local vampire owl creatures. It lays out some solid story possibilities. While these story hook are created with Nights Black Agents, or Fall of Delta Green, in mind those same hooks could be used in a VtM game. All this to say, yes Eastern vampires should have a place in VtM, because VtM is (or should be) about engaging stories about monsters. It comes down to how it is carried off, which is terribly difficult. On a related note, Lindsay Ellis could a great deal of hell mostly for just observing structural similarities between ATLA and RTLD. The point being, there is probably no way to produce a game presenting Eastern anything without it offending people and becoming so problematic and triggering so much backlash that it will not be worth the trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T08:40:04-07:00","id":1444210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444208#post1444208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the latest episode of <a href=\"http://www.kenandrobintalkaboutstuff.com/index.php/episode-441-cheese-made-of-cheese/\" target=\"_blank\">Ken and Robin Talk About Stuff</a> they discuss story possibilities set in Cambodia, specifically ones dealing with local vampire owl creatures. It lays out some solid story possibilities. While these story hook are created with Nights Black Agents, or Fall of Delta Green, in mind those same hooks could be used in a VtM game. All this to say, yes Eastern vampires should have a place in VtM, because VtM is (or should be) about engaging stories about monsters. It comes down to how it is carried off, which is terribly difficult. On a related note, Lindsay Ellis could a great deal of hell mostly for just observing structural similarities between ATLA and RTLD. The point being, there is probably no way to produce a game presenting Eastern anything without it offending people and becoming so problematic and triggering so much backlash that it will not be worth the trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having discussed it with my friends from Tawain and Hong Kong, it boils down to essentially a curious idea of what Vampire: The Masquerade is among fans:<br /> <br /> 1. Fans want to play Eastern Kindred or people from Asian countries as well as Asian descent.<br /> <br /> 2. They feel &quot;Othered&quot; when they are asked to play Kindred fundamentally different from other vampires with different rules, cultures, and goals.<br /> <br /> 3. The people who want them to have different rules tend to be assumed to be white developers rather than Asian men. Which I feel is an unfair assumption for FUTURE Wan Kuei write-ups.<br /> <br /> 4. The fans of Vampire: The Masquerade of Asian descent that pre-exist are people who want to play local versions of Tremere, Ventrue, Salubri, and so on because they're fans of the pre-existing game. So selling them on Kuei-Jin is selling them on an entirely new gameline.<br /> <br /> Or as one said:<br /> <br /> &quot;Imagine you're a guy who enjoys doing Dublin by Night as an Irishman and has a whole court already with LARPing then told Irish people have their own entirely new race of fairy/human hybrid that have wiped out the local Cainites and are violent xenophobes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T09:51:59-07:00","id":1444216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444210#post1444210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having discussed it with my friends from Tawain and Hong Kong, it boils down to essentially a curious idea of what Vampire: The Masquerade is among fans:<br /> <br /> 1. Fans want to play Eastern Kindred or people from Asian countries as well as Asian descent.<br /> <br /> 2. They feel &quot;Othered&quot; when they are asked to play Kindred fundamentally different from other vampires with different rules, cultures, and goals.<br /> <br /> 3. The people who want them to have different rules tend to be assumed to be white developers rather than Asian men. Which I feel is an unfair assumption for FUTURE Wan Kuei write-ups.<br /> <br /> 4. The fans of Vampire: The Masquerade of Asian descent that pre-exist are people who want to play local versions of Tremere, Ventrue, Salubri, and so on because they're fans of the pre-existing game. So selling them on Kuei-Jin is selling them on an entirely new gameline.<br /> <br /> Or as one said:<br /> <br /> &quot;Imagine you're a guy who enjoys doing Dublin by Night as an Irishman and has a whole court already with LARPing then told Irish people have their own entirely new race of fairy/human hybrid that have wiped out the local Cainites and are violent xenophobes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that making more room for Kindred in Asia would help to address this?<br /> <br /> Or do you think that the Wan Kuei being this distinctive Thing that exists in Asia but nowhere else generally carries with it an inevitable and detrimental &quot;Othering&quot;?<br /> <br /> To expand on the example that you offered a bit, do you think that having the fairy/human hybrids not be violently xenophobic and having regular Kindred still existing alongside them would significantly address the problem? Or would the Irish players still having to try and work their Kindred chronicles around the existence of these fairy/human hybrids in the local metaplot while other parts of the world can just enjoy the core Vampire experience without that extra effort still be an issue, along with a degree of Othering still being present?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:24:21-07:00","id":1444220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444216#post1444216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think that making more room for Kindred in Asia would help to address this?<br /> <br /> Or do you think that the Wan Kuei being this distinctive Thing that exists in Asia but nowhere else generally carries with it an inevitable and detrimental &quot;Othering&quot;?<br /> <br /> To expand on the example that you offered a bit, do you think that having the fairy/human hybrids not be violently xenophobic and having regular Kindred still existing alongside them would significantly address the problem? Or would the Irish players still having to try and work their Kindred chronicles around the existence of these fairy/human hybrids in the local metaplot while other parts of the world can just enjoy the core Vampire experience without that extra effort still be an issue, along with a degree of Othering still being present?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, mostly reiterating the gist of what I got from the conversations, I think the issue is three-fold with Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> 1. The initial presentation really was a chop-sockey set of stereotypes that combined Japanese, Indian, and Chinese legends together that really have almost nothing in common. The basis for the Wan Kuei is a distinctly Chinese legend and India's own vampire mythology is totally different. Japan also has plenty of scary undead, albeit they tend to be ghosts, and the three just do not work together very well as one creature.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that European legends work together that well but the V:TM vampire is based on the CINEMATIC vampire rather than the mythological one and there's already a distance from the &quot;source material&quot; so to speak that most people already have a distance from the monster's cultural heritage. Or, to put it as a friend put it, &quot;I know what a vampire is. I've watched Hellsing. I'm not sure what these things are.&quot; Another guy had a less flattering, &quot;Kuei Jin are a game about <i>Big Trouble in Little China</i> except without the implicit assumption Jack Burton has no idea what the fuck he's seeing or dealing with.&quot;<br /> <br /> So untangling the Wan Kuei to an iconic monster that Asian people recognize and want to play is already hard because they are an entirely new thing. Ironically due to the attempt to make something closer to RL myths.<br /> <br /> 2. Wan Kuei are troublesome for the fact that they're too close to V:TM to be their own line but don't fit into V:TM themselves. I do think that if the Kindred of the East didn't intrude on local Chinese, Japanese, and Indian Cainite courts that people wouldn't mind them so much. However, lore-wise they are supposed to fill the local niche. Except the thing about the local niche is that Kindred of the East games are<i> nothing like </i>V:TM games.<br /> <br /> They're about kung fu fighting zombies fighting demons and practicing deep spirituality to transcend your physical weaknesses. It's a very-very different game. To use another European example, it's like wanting to play Interview with a Vampire or Underworld and instead playing the Crow crossed with the Prophecy. The Crow is awesome but not the same.<br /> <br /> They should be separate gamelines and communities.<br /> <br /> 3. Wan Kuei are not very LARP friendly by contrast as the big selling point of V:TM is it is primarily a game about talking. What puts it above Werewolf: The Apocalypse is that game where you don't need big action scenes or battles to do games. KOTE leans heavily into the metaphor of fighting and tabletop friendly things whereas the V:TM community as a whole is the more social aspect. So the very DNA of the Kindred of the East is divorced from some of the social aspects of gaming that make V:TM so popular.<br /> <br /> So the issue isn't so much they can't be fixed but....how does one go about untangling this? What is the end goal and what should it look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:34:33-07:00","id":1444221,"title":"","content":"Said it before and I'll say it again... The best way to make the Wan Kuei non-problematic is to stop trying to pretend they should slot into the &quot;Vampire&quot; category of the WoD mythology, but rather link it and Mummy to the generic Wraith concept of the Risen (called such because VtM had already ripped off Revenant for their super-ghouls). This makes the Wan Kuei just a particular cultural expression of the Risen concept in the same way that &quot;Hengeyoki&quot; is just a particular cultural expression of a Garou or the &quot;Spirit Folk&quot; are just a particular cultural expression of Changelings.<br /> <br /> With that accomplished, its simply a matter of making the Wan Kuei's feeding a particular means for gathering the &quot;mana&quot; needed to maintain their animate body... with the idea that needing to eat flesh (or brains in the case of low tier Western Risen/Zombies), blood, breath and eventually just drink from the cosmos reflect differing levels of ability among all Risen. That most Risen need to feed by consuming parts of living humans puts them into natural competition with vampires for resources, but you're no longer pretending they're remotely the same type of creature; one is a cursed human, the other is basically a ghost animating its corpse (and covering it up with a pretty illusion in the process).<br /> <br /> Refine the feeding criteria a bit and, for the Risen/Wan Kuei &quot;flesh and blood&quot; could be basically the same level and drinking blood instead of eating someone's flesh is just a less lethal means of obtaining sustenance for the more moral Risen. The next step up might be the &quot;strong emotions&quot; part where they feed off fear or pain or desire, which lets them feed without physically hurting someone, but flesh and blood is sometimes just easier (or a way of doubling up... feeding on both the pain from the wound they drink from and the blood proper).<br /> <br /> Basically, slide the Wan Kuei into a cultural expression of the universal Risen concept and just about all the problematic aspects fall away. The Eastern Courts reflect their culture's stronger traditions towards organization... a social construct like the Camarilla vs. something intrinsic to the Risen state.<br /> <br /> Thus, the Wan Kuei becomes a creature type that a Masquerade vampire might encounter in the same way they encounter any other type of Risen (or werewolves or generic ghosts); as a supernatural being, but not even intended to be &quot;a vampire, but oriental.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:48:23-07:00","id":1444224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wan Kuei are not very LARP friendly by contrast as the big selling point of V:TM is it is primarily a game about talking.</div> </div> </div> </div>VTM was/is popular because you got to be a Vampire. Beyond that before certain new additions forced you into one particular style, you could do anything with it on the type of stories you wanted to tell. Not everything was purely only in the speaking lens, and even within the speaking &quot;primacy&quot; of the game it wasn't about angsty typecast stuff such as attending to a &quot;Touchstone&quot; or &quot;we make the game just more speakey 'cuz LARP&quot;; it was about the cold hard realities of the Kindred existence and the Jyhad, which itself has always accompanied some form of fighting; whether it be an Elder manipulating human authorities to assault a gang in turn manipulated by another Elder, or full on sieges among the night.<br /> <br /> To divorce all action from the setting negates one of the primary drivers of VTM. Even V5 itself has violence a centerpiece of driving the plot along, with the Anarchs apparently overpowering the Sabbat from many of their territories or the subsequent Beckoning&quot; where all the Elders proceeded to the Middle-East for some massive battle.<br /> <br /> And remember, Tabletop should always be the primary focus in the first place (I know I'm probably stepping on a few toes here, oh well). To say or imply KOTE is bad because it &quot;leans heavily into the metaphor (what exactly did you mean by &quot;metaphor&quot; in this instance, specifically?) and tabletop friendly things&quot; doesn't make it bad.. because its primarily Tabletop, so that'd be the main focus; its first job would be ensuring that aspect is up to par, before worrying about anything else (i.e in the case for accounting for LARP).<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but rather link it and Mummy to the generic Wraith concept of the Risen</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrible idea, since the Wan Kuei are way too different and have a way too different powerbase and lore than Risen. First of all; Risen don't eat brains to fuel themselves, they use Pathos. Second; Becoming a Wan Kuei is one of clawing yourself from the Thousand Hells, one of the hardest things for a previously unsupernatural/mortal person can do. Becoming a Risen is easy as getting the right teacher in Puppetry and bargaining with your Shadow, but that comes with its own issues. Three; Like I mention before, Risen can be strong, yes, but they're nothing compared to Wan Kuei with have levels of Haxx that basically make them certainly NOT Risen... and also the fact that Wan Kuei cannot use Arcanos nor Risen can even use Dharma powers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: (Oh, and don't forget depending on whether the particular Wan Kuei is either Yang or Yin aspected, they can commune with Spirits from the Middle and High Umbra, something the Risen can never do. Not to mention the Wan Kuei like the Garou or Awakened can travel to said Middle or High Umbra)<br /> <br /> I think the best path for the Wan Kuei is that they already ARE their own thing. Pretending they aren't.. is iffy and just causes more plot contention. They didn't come from Caine, they weren't a central part to the chronicles of the First or Second cities, they have a completely different backstory. They aren't &quot;Vampires, but oriental&quot; (that was the Anda, Gaki, and others I forgot)... and even if it THAT really was the case isn't that what the side that is clamoring to remove the Wan Kuei want in the first place?<br /> <br /> The best path for the part of the oWoD fandom that what Kindred stories in Asia is just have the current writers make the formerly existing few Kindred there just have newfound prominence, while not stupefying or outright retconning the Wan Kuei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-16-2021, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:52:35-07:00","id":1444227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444224#post1444224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VTM was/is popular because you got to be a Vampire. Beyond that before certain new additions forced you into one particular style, you could do anything with it on the type of stories you wanted to tell. Not everything was purely only in the speaking lens, and even within the speaking &quot;primacy&quot; of the game it wasn't about angsty typecast stuff such as attending to a &quot;Touchstone&quot; or &quot;we make the game just more speakey 'cuz LARP&quot;; it was about the cold hard realities of the Kindred existence and the Jyhad, which itself has always accompanied some form of fighting; whether it be an Elder manipulating human authorities to assault a gang in turn manipulated by another Elder, or full on sieges among the night.<br /> <br /> To divorce all action from the setting negates one of the primary drivers of VTM. Even V5 itself has violence a centerpiece of driving the plot along, with the Anarchs apparently overpowering the Sabbat from many of their territories or the subsequent Beckoning&quot; where all the Elders proceeded to the Middle-East for some massive battle.<br /> <br /> And remember, Tabletop should always be the primary focus in the first place (I know I'm probably stepping on a few toes here, oh well). To say or imply KOTE is bad because it &quot;leans heavily into the metaphor (what exactly did you mean by &quot;metaphor&quot; in this instance, specifically?) and tabletop friendly things&quot; doesn't make it bad.. because its primarily Tabletop, so that'd be the main focus; its first job would be ensuring that aspect is up to par, before worrying about anything else (i.e in the case for accounting for LARP).</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than debate the point, I'll just say, &quot;A game that can be played as tabletop AND Larp will always have more fans than a game that can only be done tabletop.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.lessitermedia.com/wp-content/uploads/Photos/Mike-Drop.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:16:34-07:00","id":1444234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444220#post1444220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, mostly reiterating the gist of what I got from the conversations, I think the issue is three-fold with Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> 1. The initial presentation really was a chop-sockey set of stereotypes that combined Japanese, Indian, and Chinese legends together that really have almost nothing in common. The basis for the Wan Kuei is a distinctly Chinese legend and India's own vampire mythology is totally different. Japan also has plenty of scary undead, albeit they tend to be ghosts, and the three just do not work together very well as one creature.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that European legends work together that well but the V:TM vampire is based on the CINEMATIC vampire rather than the mythological one and there's already a distance from the &quot;source material&quot; so to speak that most people already have a distance from the monster's cultural heritage. Or, to put it as a friend put it, &quot;I know what a vampire is. I've watched Hellsing. I'm not sure what these things are.&quot; Another guy had a less flattering, &quot;Kuei Jin are a game about <i>Big Trouble in Little China</i> except without the implicit assumption Jack Burton has no idea what the fuck he's seeing or dealing with.&quot;<br /> <br /> So untangling the Wan Kuei to an iconic monster that Asian people recognize and want to play is already hard because they are an entirely new thing. Ironically due to the attempt to make something closer to RL myths.<br /> <br /> 2. Wan Kuei are troublesome for the fact that they're too close to V:TM to be their own line but don't fit into V:TM themselves. I do think that if the Kindred of the East didn't intrude on local Chinese, Japanese, and Indian Cainite courts that people wouldn't mind them so much. However, lore-wise they are supposed to fill the local niche. Except the thing about the local niche is that Kindred of the East games are<i> nothing like </i>V:TM games.<br /> <br /> They're about kung fu fighting zombies fighting demons and practicing deep spirituality to transcend your physical weaknesses. It's a very-very different game. To use another European example, it's like wanting to play Interview with a Vampire or Underworld and instead playing the Crow crossed with the Prophecy. The Crow is awesome but not the same.<br /> <br /> They should be separate gamelines and communities.<br /> <br /> 3. Wan Kuei are not very LARP friendly by contrast as the big selling point of V:TM is it is primarily a game about talking. What puts it above Werewolf: The Apocalypse is that game where you don't need big action scenes or battles to do games. KOTE leans heavily into the metaphor of fighting and tabletop friendly things whereas the V:TM community as a whole is the more social aspect. So the very DNA of the Kindred of the East is divorced from some of the social aspects of gaming that make V:TM so popular.<br /> <br /> So the issue isn't so much they can't be fixed but....how does one go about untangling this? What is the end goal and what should it look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the problem is almost certainly intractable from the perspective of a business that needs to maximize audience and sales. Hand-waving them out of existence or dropping a bridge on them is probably the best response for a big company, though I'm sure other posters might disagree.<br /> <br /> I'm asking more from the perspective of my private Storyteller-canon; I'm essentially facing this problem in microcosm regarding my own setting. I've been working on ideas to try and address point #1; point #3 is largely irrelevant for my private canon. But that's where my question about whether that problem of Othering is insurmountable or not. I tend to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> that at least bringing them much closer to something that already exists in the WoD like the Risen diminishes the &quot;Oriental snowflake&quot; element somewhat. But it also falls into a wider trend I've noticed with OWoD that in most cases, non-&quot;Western&quot; perspectives are almost always lumped with Spirit. Sure, they wink at it with the Dreamspeakers, but it's also present in the Nunnehi, the Menehune, the Hsien, and the Wan Kuei. Instant exoticism, just add Spirit. Especially frustrating given that &quot;Western&quot; traditions have tended to involve dealings with &quot;spirits&quot; (angels, demons) just as often. Just been wrestling with how I want to handle these things for a little bit, and it felt kind of relevant to the problem with the Wan Kuei, hope people don't mind the tangent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:26:14-07:00","id":1444236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444221#post1444221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, slide the Wan Kuei into a cultural expression of the universal Risen concept and just about all the problematic aspects fall away. The Eastern Courts reflect their culture's stronger traditions towards organization... a social construct like the Camarilla vs. something intrinsic to the Risen state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, and would say strip out as much of the old KOTE social system as possible, and have each region possess its own social dynamics, own set of names and terms, and own set of magics. Some of the physical powers would be the same (bonus to strength should be same for the sake of simplicity in terms of game mechanics). You could say the names and systems of the original KOTE were a mix of what Westerners saw and thought they understood and what Imperial China tried to pass off, but that neither are true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444227#post1444227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than debate the point, I'll just say, &quot;A game that can be played as tabletop AND Larp will always have more fans than a game that can only be done tabletop.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this - the original KOTE was too mechanically dense, too rules complicated. Something vastly simpler would go with LARP.<br /> <br /> But this is all something of a moot point, or at least academic. A revised KOTE will not happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:32:52-07:00","id":1444237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444234#post1444234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that the problem is almost certainly intractable from the perspective of a business that needs to maximize audience and sales. Hand-waving them out of existence or dropping a bridge on them is probably the best response for a big company, though I'm sure other posters might disagree.<br /> <br /> I'm asking more from the perspective of my private Storyteller-canon; I'm essentially facing this problem in microcosm regarding my own setting. I've been working on ideas to try and address point #1; point #3 is largely irrelevant for my private canon. But that's where my question about whether that problem of Othering is insurmountable or not. I tend to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> that at least bringing them much closer to something that already exists in the WoD like the Risen diminishes the &quot;Oriental snowflake&quot; element somewhat. But it also falls into a wider trend I've noticed with OWoD that in most cases, non-&quot;Western&quot; perspectives are almost always lumped with Spirit. Sure, they wink at it with the Dreamspeakers, but it's also present in the Nunnehi, the Menehune, the Hsien, and the Wan Kuei. Instant exoticism, just add Spirit. Especially frustrating given that &quot;Western&quot; traditions have tended to involve dealings with &quot;spirits&quot; (angels, demons) just as often. Just been wrestling with how I want to handle these things for a little bit, and it felt kind of relevant to the problem with the Wan Kuei, hope people don't mind the tangent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think making them Risen and their own thing would work best then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:34:33-07:00","id":1444238,"title":"","content":"There's an interesting thing about this as the DROWNED which were introduced in Beckett's Jyhad Diary are something that the writers at OPP don't seemingly want to make into Cainites.<br /> <br /> Nerissa Blackwater's description seems to go out of its way to make multiple suggestions that Drowned can copy Kindred powers but aren't Kindred.<br /> <br /> Perhaps because they don't want to link indigineous monsters to Cainites.<br /> <br /> OTOH, that runs into potentially the same problems as the Wan Kuei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T13:23:06-07:00","id":1444251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444234#post1444234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that the problem is almost certainly intractable from the perspective of a business that needs to maximize audience and sales. Hand-waving them out of existence or dropping a bridge on them is probably the best response for a big company, though I'm sure other posters might disagree.<br /> <br /> I'm asking more from the perspective of my private Storyteller-canon; I'm essentially facing this problem in microcosm regarding my own setting. I've been working on ideas to try and address point #1; point #3 is largely irrelevant for my private canon. But that's where my question about whether that problem of Othering is insurmountable or not. I tend to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> that at least bringing them much closer to something that already exists in the WoD like the Risen diminishes the &quot;Oriental snowflake&quot; element somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you dig too far into wraith, you run into what caused the problem in the first place with the paradigms of death. Which for some reason make no difference for Hunpo wraiths becoming Risen even though DKoJ made a really big deal about how the hun and po aren't just another name for the psyche and shadow, guys! (But they totally are in operation, of course; the effort to try and differentiate the two fell flat, there)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it also falls into a wider trend I've noticed with OWoD that in most cases, non-&quot;Western&quot; perspectives are almost always lumped with Spirit. Sure, they wink at it with the Dreamspeakers, but it's also present in the Nunnehi, the Menehune, the Hsien, and the Wan Kuei. Instant exoticism, just add Spirit. Especially frustrating given that &quot;Western&quot; traditions have tended to involve dealings with &quot;spirits&quot; (angels, demons) just as often. Just been wrestling with how I want to handle these things for a little bit, and it felt kind of relevant to the problem with the Wan Kuei, hope people don't mind the tangent. </div> </div> </div>I regard that as Mage's fault. It didn't build its own stuff well enough and just ended up squatting in W:tA's backyard half the time. And it then set the standard of making the Umbra rather generic for the setting, making it okay to squat in the Middle Umbra instead of anywhere else. Though, technically, when it comes to &quot;Western&quot; tradition and folks, a lot of the time that they run into &quot;demons&quot;, they might actually be seeing a spirit from the Middle Umbra, but not really capable of describing it very well because Christianity trained them to see anything otherworldly through a very limited lens. Notably, his wife's dabbling in spiritualism for kicks turned Premium Oil's owner into a bane-ridden monster (as opposed to just an &quot;I drink your milkshake!&quot; kind of human monster). There was also the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon, of the same sorts of people tapping into a warped interpretation of BSD lore. It's not often explored, but humans tripping across spirits and tapping into them for a terrible price is a thing that Werewolf does without leaving Euro-places or their perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T13:49:27-07:00","id":1444258,"title":"","content":"I feel like that is definitely a weakness because European mythology is no less spiritual focused but people are much happier to remove the Angels/Demons and so on out of it all.<br /> <br /> When a Changeling/Demon: The Fallen/Wraith part of the Umbra would be just as interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T13:58:11-07:00","id":1444259,"title":"","content":"I think the Wan Kuei question will be treated as the Laibon and Drowned Legacies, which won't be decanonized but won't be talked about either in depth. Something that seemed to bother everyone, even those who liked the idea that I talked to is the fact that Wan Kuei community is way to big for a phenomenon that seems so special, which is a Risen/Wraith kind of situation, but with something else. Especially cuz there is still ghosts and spirits in the area where Hungry Ghosts rise. I' ve already made some long ass posts in this very forum about how I think it could be handled, which is basically make Wan Kuei and their creation rarer; make it so that Cainites thought many vampires in Asia were Wan Kuei but just weren't (which would let the Clans exist and have existed all this time around there) and they mashed them together erroneously; don't call them Kindred cause they just aren't, in any way, and I think that was a bad name to call them, for not only they aren't the Cainite Kindred but they aren't Kindred among themselves either, they don't form lineages, not as it is normally understood at least, and aren't themselves connected by blood.<br /> <br /> For me, the greatest problem in cosmology of KotE is &quot;why exactly do they exist?&quot;. Why aren't them just ghosts or risen? Is it some form o Spell like the ones in Mummy? Is it something divine or made by spirits like a Geist or Awakening? ... besides that, one thing everyone likes about Vampire is that it is mysterious, everything is mostly myth, and that makes the vampires in urban setting bizarre, and that's what makes the World of Darkness World (reality) before Darkness (fantasy). Wan Kuei seem to know and be certain of way too much stuff (like Garou, and many Mages), which steals from the mystique and well, just makes the whole Asian Legend thing annoying, as if Asians were inherently different &quot;cuz they know the supernatural truth&quot; or something, which is terribly alienating. In my opinion, they should have a ton of different origin myths, which is different from the Christianity that made a more homogenous mentality in Euroamerican cultures (which could be called The West), which is a really stretch, cuz people even only in lets say West Europe had very different ideas only about religion, in a faith that calls for an ecumenic community, and even had Schisms, antipopes, Protestantism, Reforms...etc. So yeah, have an even more constraint and homogenous culture in the whole Asia is pretty bs. And i'm mostly ignorant in these matters, but from the little I know it already is weird. Maybe the whole unified concepts and myths from the Wan Kuei showed in the book could be said (like the Hengeyokai) to be from only Japan, which is a more homogenous culture, but it still wouldn't be enough, and its far from representing all Asia.<br /> <br /> Problem is, I love Vampire, I love Mage, I love Wraith, and I love the Wan Kuei, and they should all have their own spotlight, be their own thing, like you people have been saying here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T14:49:38-07:00","id":1444265,"title":"","content":"(Phone reply, will try to do better later)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> It's on the table <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But the Drowned Legacies are kind of the other side of the fence. Not every kind of Vampire in the world needs to be Cainite. It's just a question of whether or not the Wan Kuei are more trouble than they're worth to salvage, with the Orientalism and such. I probably lean towards salvage because of their place in the Week of Nightmares, that delicious pile of smelly cheese.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> The irony is that I actually really like the mess that results from smooshing Mage and Werewolf cosmology together. I will probably be starting a thread on the subject down the road lol. But my point about Angels and Demons was a comment about OOC writing decisions, not the IC interpretation that mortals might conflate spirits with them. CTPhipps kind of hit it above with his point about spirituality and European folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T17:27:22-07:00","id":1444276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444258#post1444258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like that is definitely a weakness because European mythology is no less spiritual focused but people are much happier to remove the Angels/Demons and so on out of it all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think to a large degree there was a wariness about officially stating whether the whole Christian mythos is true or not, and if it was, whether the Christian God was the one true God or just another diety. Even when we got Demon the Fallen (right at the tail end of the World of Darkness) White Wolf put up a lot of hoops like the whole multiple versions of history, and whether or not the Fallen even remembered things or were just delusional. It's why, while Vampire was talking about demons and devils and Faustian bargains for years and years, we never really got writeups of those guys, whereas White Wolf was more willing to write up demons and devils of other religious mythos.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:01:10-07:00","id":1444284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444265#post1444265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every kind of Vampire in the world needs to be Cainite. It's just a question of whether or not the Wan Kuei are more trouble than they're worth to salvage, with the Orientalism and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I 100% agree with the first part. But I also think the KOTE cannot be salvaged from the Orientalism, or at least that it would be more trouble than it is worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:19:38-07:00","id":1444287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444284#post1444284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I 100% agree with the first part. But I also think the KOTE cannot be salvaged from the Orientalism, or at least that it would be more trouble than it is worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and I'm a huge fan of continuity in all its forms.<br /> <br /> I think its the problem that if you removed all the Orientalism, they'd in no way shape or form resemble the Kuei-Jin as we know them.<br /> <br /> It'd be easier to just say Ming Xiao is a particularly nasty Chinese Tzimisce with a Horrid Form and some local Koldunism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:44:47-07:00","id":1444289,"title":"","content":"I wonder if anyone has tried adapting Risen for KOTE or anything else. I should go take a look at the Vault...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:59:31-07:00","id":1444290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444289#post1444289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if anyone has tried adapting Risen for KOTE or anything else. I should go take a look at the Vault...</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had time from my professional career, I might do a non-canon, &quot;CAINITES OF THE MIDDLE KINGDOM&quot; and how to adapt the basics of the Kuei Jin to regular rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:23:48-07:00","id":1444297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444224#post1444224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To say or imply KOTE is bad because it &quot;leans heavily into the metaphor (what exactly did you mean by &quot;metaphor&quot; in this instance, specifically?) and tabletop friendly things&quot; doesn't make it bad.. because its primarily Tabletop, so that'd be the main focus; its first job would be ensuring that aspect is up to par, before worrying about anything else (i.e in the case for accounting for LARP).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think most of the people making valid criticisms against KotE care more about things like reductively mashing conflicting Asian cultures and spiritual beliefs together, leaning heavily on stereotypes that range from superficial to downright dangerous (sexualization of Asian women, &quot;Yellow Peril,&quot; etc.), and disrupting the ability of players from an entire continent to play the game without feeling singled out as the Other due to their home region being described as fundamentally different from the rest of the planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444287#post1444287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree and I'm a huge fan of continuity in all its forms.<br /> <br /> I think its the problem that if you removed all the Orientalism, they'd in no way shape or form resemble the Kuei-Jin as we know them.<br /> <br /> It'd be easier to just say Ming Xiao is a particularly nasty Chinese Tzimisce with a Horrid Form and some local Koldunism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, Bloodlines was what introduced me to the World of Darkness, but I've never gotten far enough into the game to meet Ming Xiao. Completing games is kind of rare for me lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:26:50-07:00","id":1444298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1388622#post1388622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canonically, now, Tokyo is a Camarilla City.<br /> <br /> I remember reading the Lasombra Clan Book which talked about how the Lasombra used to influence the Imperial throne of China, which indicated that the Eurocentrism hadn't taken root yet in the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>It indicates that Eurocentrism is totally in charge European vampires colonise the globe! (Yes I know originally Middle Eastern, but like the God that canonically made them, they are euro now. The Cainite conquers the world and by existing alone declares one God, one faith, one truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:28:24-07:00","id":1444299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444298#post1444298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It indicates that Eurocentrism is totally in charge European vampires colonise the globe! (Yes I know originally Middle Eastern, but like the God that canonically made them, they are euro now. The Cainite conquers the world and by existing alone declares one God, one faith, one truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by your view, because a Judeao-Christian mythology is canon to the fictional monster, it doesn't matter if a character is Asian, they're automatically whitey?<br /> <br /> What do you think of Christian or Muslim people living in Asian countries?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Islam_percent_population_in_each_nation_World_Map_Muslim_data_by_Pew_Research.svg/1280px-Islam_percent_population_in_each_nation_World_Map_Muslim_data_by_Pew_Research.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\"> Islam in Asia - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because there's over a billion Muslims living in Asia. They also believe in Caine. Are they Euro?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The above is not calling out Taggie in particular but actually mentioning that part of what makes the Kuei-Jin so frustrating is they don't even have a particularly reflective morality of their population centers. Their mythology is a kind of slap-dash verison of Daoist mythology applied to Japan, South Asia, and India. Which is really culturally ignorant. Doubly so because, again, there are more Muslims in Asia than there are in Africa and the Middle East combined.<br /> <br /> But a Muslim Chinese man could become a Kuei-Jin but not a San Fransisco man of Japanese descent or a ethnically variable convert to Daoism. Which is doubly weird because Asia is not particularly racially homogeneous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:34:04-07:00","id":1444302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444289#post1444289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if anyone has tried adapting Risen for KOTE or anything else. I should go take a look at the Vault...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> there is the Ghost Families book written by a Storyteller Vault writer although I assume she's still writing the other books. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/299573/Ghost-Families-Penangalan--Pishacha-BUNDLE?src=by_author_of_product\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...hor_of_product</a> I used it as inspiration when writing my non-Cainite but still kindred version of them in my own personal Asian homebrew I'm writing myself. I would have posted my doc here but still incomplete.<br /> <br /> I usually make the courts of Eastern kindred be similar to princedoms during the War Of Princes but certain countries have an Ashirra influence, such as Malaysia and Indonesia. the other sects also have some hold on certain cities like the Camarilla having Singapore, Tokyo, and Hong Kong while the Sabbat mostly have the Philippines, although Manila is being contested for control due to the Cammies holding some parts of the city as Manila is a big place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:47:21-07:00","id":1444303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444299#post1444299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So by your view, because a Judeao-Christian mythology is canon to the fictional monster, it doesn't matter if a character is Asian, they're automatically whitey?<br /> <br /> What do you think of Christian or Muslim people living in Asian countries?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Islam_percent_population_in_each_nation_World_Map_Muslim_data_by_Pew_Research.svg/1280px-Islam_percent_population_in_each_nation_World_Map_Muslim_data_by_Pew_Research.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\"> Islam in Asia - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because there's over a billion Muslims living in Asia. They also believe in Caine. Are they Euro?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The above is not calling out Taggie in particular but actually mentioning that part of what makes the Kuei-Jin so frustrating is they don't even have a particularly reflective morality of their population centers. Their mythology is a kind of slap-dash verison of Daoist mythology applied to Japan, South Asia, and India. Which is really culturally ignorant. Doubly so because, again, there are more Muslims in Asia than there are in Africa and the Middle East combined.<br /> <br /> But a Muslim Chinese man could become a Kuei-Jin but not a San Fransisco man of Japanese descent or a ethnically variable convert to Daoism. Which is doubly weird because Asia is not particularly racially homogeneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>but what about before the arrival of Islam and Christianity in Asia? would the eastern kindred elders and methuselahs that predated the spread even believe that story? although most of Southeast Asia has been Islamized, there are still some ethnic groups such as Hindus in Bali Indonesia, or certain tribes in the Philippines that still cling to their old pre-Islamic beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:53:59-07:00","id":1444304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444303#post1444303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but what about before the arrival of Islam and Christianity in Asia? would the eastern kindred elders and methuselahs that predated the spread even believe that story? although most of Southeast Asia has been Islamized, there are still some ethnic groups such as Hindus in Bali Indonesia, or certain tribes in the Philippines that still cling to their old pre-Islamic beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm certainly not saying all Asian peoples believe in Islam. The current official government of China is atheism after all.<br /> <br /> BUttttttt.... Europe has Helena and Mithras and people still believe in Caine there. Certainly, plenty of Gangrel Elders still believe in Odin probably..<br /> <br /> Cappadocius also proves that even ancient than dirt people can convert to newer religions too.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that if we're going strictly by religious beliefs then the Caine Myth shouldn't be restricted to Europe nor should Cainites be viewed strictly through the lens of Western European (read: white) Christianity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T00:05:47-07:00","id":1444310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444299#post1444299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Muslim Chinese man could become a Kuei-Jin but not a San Fransisco man of Japanese descent or a ethnically variable convert to Daoism. Which is doubly weird because Asia is not particularly racially homogeneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, in the books all of those types of people can become Wan Kuei. <br /> <br /> I think the issue is that, as I mentioned in another thread the lack of western (Christian) demons. If we had a Christian hell (and other cultural hells as well of course) where souls without virtue went after they died, we could have Wan Kuei as more of a global event. <br /> <br /> Honestly I was expecting to see just that happen when Demon the Fallen was announced and we'd be getting a western version of the group. Instead Wan Kuei remained a regional group due to the unique position of the Yama Kings and the 1000 Hells and the fact that there isn't anything like them anywhere else on the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-17-2021, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T01:05:45-07:00","id":1444312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444310#post1444310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to note, in the books all of those types of people can become Wan Kuei.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I thought it was established that you had to be:<br /> <br /> A. Asian descent<br /> B. AND in Asia<br /> <br /> Your religious beliefs didn't matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T01:51:02-07:00","id":1444313,"title":"","content":"Certain areas outside of Asia like sections of California, Toronto, etc have seen Wan Kuei popping up. Some of them have speculated it's been happening for a long time, and in other locations, but without training those who came back were never able to rise about chih meh status and were eventually put down as mindless monsters, but nobody in setting knew if that was true.<br /> <br /> Religious beliefs don't matter but people who moved to Asia and adopted the culture could see their souls falling into Yomi after they died. Presumably in the modern WoD people living near places like Little China towns could find themselves also falling into Yomi. I mean, there's a lot of funky stuff going on in the Final Nights with the Great Leap Outward, the Yama Kings creating Broken Mirrors and the like.<br /> <br /> I think one of the ideas that never got explored because the game ended was that in their desire to &quot;take the war to the West&quot; the Wan Kuei were inadvertently going to end up creating western Wan Kuei with few, if any, ties to Asia simply by expanding their spiritual footprint as well as that of the Yama Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T03:24:54-07:00","id":1444316,"title":"","content":"Theres a few products on Storytellers Vault ( Analects, Ghost Families, Wicker Wars etc.) that do a much better job of setting up Hungry Ghost history and background than the corebook does and they are well worth picking up as alternatives if you haven't already completely reworked things to remove all the &quot; Anime and Shaw Brothers &quot; that passes for such in the corebook.<br /> <br /> I know I've already gone over this a dozen times ( perhaps more?) with Mr Phipps but looking at post #263 literally nothing I've ever posted has made any impression at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Obviously there are also hundreds of Cainites throughout Asia itself and have been for thousands of years spreading through South East Asia( Vietnam/Laos/Cambodia/Malaysia/Thailand/Indonesia/Phillipines) first with the Hindu kingdoms ( mostly Ravnos and some others) and empires out from India then with the Muslim expansion ( Most Cainite Clans) at later dates and then with the Colonial Powers. Before this there were undoubtedly scattered individual Gangrel and Nosferatu. In northern asia ( Mongolia/Korea/Japan) the Anda, Nagaraja, Nosferatu and Niktuku have existed since ancient times, many more came with western ventures and fleeing Baba Yaga both in ancient times and more recently. South Asia ( Bangladesh/Sri Lanka/India/Nepal/Pakistan) has always been a melting pot of Cainite and Hungry Ghost societies. In fact the only place in Asia absolutely without Cainites is Central China simply because it is the centre of Quincunx power. But as said I've already posted this dozens of times....<br /> <br /> I could mention the numerous Indonesian, Indigenous, Pinoy and other groups I've run campaigns for who were glad to play beings from their own or neighbouring folklore because they were kind of over the Hollywood Viral Vampire that Cainites represent.....not that they didn't play them as well they were just considered a little silly next to homegrown horrors. And yes we made a lot of fun of the KotE corebook and its overwhelming US filtered Sinoism but theres an awesome game in there.<br /> <br /> Of course over time we arrived at making Hungry Ghosts a world wide phenomenon in slow retreat from the ever spreading horde of Cainites spreading out exponentially from Africa some 20,000 years ago to the Levant then the Middle East, South Asia and Europe and then to the rest of the world. And had some great campaigns dealing with NA, Polynesian and Australian Hungry Ghosts.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I've posted this all before....so I probably shouldn't have bothered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T03:44:44-07:00","id":1444319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444302#post1444302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> there is the Ghost Families book written by a Storyteller Vault writer although I assume she's still writing the other books. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/299573/Ghost-Families-Penangalan--Pishacha-BUNDLE?src=by_author_of_product\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...hor_of_product</a> I used it as inspiration when writing my non-Cainite but still kindred version of them in my own personal Asian homebrew I'm writing myself. I would have posted my doc here but still incomplete.<br /> <br /> I usually make the courts of Eastern kindred be similar to princedoms during the War Of Princes but certain countries have an Ashirra influence, such as Malaysia and Indonesia. the other sects also have some hold on certain cities like the Camarilla having Singapore, Tokyo, and Hong Kong while the Sabbat mostly have the Philippines, although Manila is being contested for control due to the Cammies holding some parts of the city as Manila is a big place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> Ghost Familes, Analects of the Damned and Dions Phillipines material ( Wicker Wars, The Manila Trio) are all very good books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T04:31:23-07:00","id":1444321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444299#post1444299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So by your view, because a Judeao-Christian mythology is canon to the fictional monster, it doesn't matter if a character is Asian, they're automatically whitey?<br /> <br /> What do you think of Christian or Muslim people living in Asian countries?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Islam_percent_population_in_each_nation_World_Map_Muslim_data_by_Pew_Research.svg/1280px-Islam_percent_population_in_each_nation_World_Map_Muslim_data_by_Pew_Research.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\"> Islam in Asia - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Asia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because there's over a billion Muslims living in Asia. They also believe in Caine. Are they Euro?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The above is not calling out Taggie in particular but actually mentioning that part of what makes the Kuei-Jin so frustrating is they don't even have a particularly reflective morality of their population centers. Their mythology is a kind of slap-dash verison of Daoist mythology applied to Japan, South Asia, and India. Which is really culturally ignorant. Doubly so because, again, there are more Muslims in Asia than there are in Africa and the Middle East combined.<br /> <br /> But a Muslim Chinese man could become a Kuei-Jin but not a San Fransisco man of Japanese descent or a ethnically variable convert to Daoism. Which is doubly weird because Asia is not particularly racially homogeneous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't have to be Kuei Jin, it has to be not Cainites, because they are the only myth that is true, and they are a European myth, based on a European dominated religion, taking their rules and putting a new local name on it doesn't fix this issue, it's at best mockery to do that, and that is the kindest interpretation.<br /> <br /> As to being Christian making someone white, no it doesn't, but it does mean colonialist indoctrination and ideology has done it's job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T04:52:03-07:00","id":1444325,"title":"","content":"Yep. The common defense for just splattering Cainites everywhere with no context throughout the world is that the &quot;Cain myth was always unreliable&quot;; as if we didn't have multiple VTM supplement books, the Gehenna Chronicles, and D:TF all but confirming Caine as the 1st Vampire\u2122 already. The Judeo-&quot;Christian&quot; (I put that in parentheses because lately actual Jewish people nowadays dispute this framework) is the norm surrounding the Kindred, has been since 1st Edition so you can't scramble from that. They literally have Generation, in which makes you weaker with each new Embrace with how far removed you are from Caine. Don't get me WRONG, I love oWoD, but one of the things right CofD/VTR did was decoupling a central plotpoint character from Vampires; and NOT making them explicitly center around a biblical myth only.<br /> <br /> To remove/retcon the Wan Kuei is to assert that the belief systems and/or religions that definitely <b>predated</b> Judaism, Christianity, and Islam (in chronological order of emergence) were wrong or the aforementioned three is the <i>right</i> way. The Wan Kuei weren't perfect at ALL, but atleast White Wolf tried; even as feeble as it was in not trying to lamcast this orientalist facet many critiques of KotE see in it.<br /> <br /> You say that KotE isn't an accurate depiction of the morality of the population centers they're involved? Fair. But atleast they are something that is atleast half-way accurate or atleast DOES reflect the beliefs of the populations they're involved with. Abrahamic religions however before colonialism definitely weren't native reflections of their morality at all.<br /> <br /> What KotE really would need is the current maintainers/writers looking at the inaccuracies of the past and merely just sprucing it up (and this can certainly be done with extreme advances to the internet not really available in the 90s, so there can't be any excuses), as to not remove the Wan Kuei considering how important they are to oWoD. The only answer for just killing off the Wan Kuei unceremoniously would just be the laziness we see in the overall &quot;5th&quot; modern modus operandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-17-2021, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T07:51:50-07:00","id":1444331,"title":"","content":"Culturally, I think the biggest disconnect between 'the west' and 'the east' is that the west modernized on its own, changing as it pleased shedding off outdated values for the sake of progress, while &quot;the east&quot; modernized at gunpoint (often literally) and has largely tried to balance the ideas of their traditions and modernity. This is obviously a gross simplification, but it's a good chunk of the reason why western authors get all star-eyed looking at these well preserved &quot;spiritual&quot; traditions, while very similar traditions in europe and western asia are consigned to history and largely forgotten about. Some regions of europe are particularly disconnected from tradition and thus some feel like they're missing out, becoming greatly enamored with the idea of eastern balance between modernity and tradition. I think it's rather natural honestly, even if I have grown to detest the idea. <br /> <br /> Just talking about Hungry ghosts (HG) in general (not in v5, but in the future) I think there absolutely is room for them, the issue is that there are issues, and they can be fixed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The part where they war with Kindred for no particular reason... Mostly stems from racism, but there are aspects to this that I think should stay, I mean, Kindred are nasty, and it's very likely that, were the kindred to become dominant, they would try to assert authority over the Cathayans and likely start destroying newly born HG &quot;In the name of the Masquerade&quot; or something like that; HG might win battles, but Cainites win wars. It's not entirely weird for HG to pre-emptively fight kindred influence... though traveling to california for it is clearly clownish stupidity and the result of writers being fools. The biggest issue from the player's perspective is that the HG supposedly mean you can't do a Camarilla game in Asia... which is unrealistic when you consider... Colonialism. Hell, Hong-Kong had 3000 inhabitants split among a dozen villages before the British took it; No doubt it'd be a hotbed for kindred. The British, French, Portuguese.. very few places escaped Colonial rule and the few that did were highly influenced by the europeans, probably losing a port-city to the Kindred as a result. <br /> <br /> I'd push the more militant HG inland/Outside the cities where the kindred don't go. The more moderate HG would work great as characters to work with/against in an Asian Camarilla court. The big problem with everything I've said is that it still kinda excludes someone from playing Vampire<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />ark Ages: Pyeongyang... unless maybe you flirt with mongols or something. <br /> <br /> I don't think there's an especially huge problem with the HG not matching up precisely to local legends (Kindred don't match up either, and there's enough movies to cast some doubt that they match any particular movie) <br /> The pretentious Dharma/Ki stuff... honestly, from reading a fair few translations of cultivation novels, it fits. It fits really well. Only thing it's missing is the part where they all learn to fly upon reaching a certain level and lines such as &quot;You dare!&quot; and &quot;You are unworthy of my blade/You made me draw my sword&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T08:39:02-07:00","id":1444336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue from the player's perspective is that the HG supposedly mean you can't do a Camarilla game in Asia</div> </div> </div> </div>I never understood this conceit in general from the crowd that dislike the Wan Kuei or want them &quot;removed because it stops VTM chronicles from happening in Asia&quot;... No it doesn't, you can certainly have games take place in Asia; but that doesn't mean it would be an easy course from an IC standpoint. But since when has VTM supposed to be &quot;easy&quot;? I thought part of the main fun of VTM was making up elaborate intrigues or moves for survival after becoming a Kindred, against all odds. If you'd want to be in engrossed in a higher bout of interesting difficulty, trying to survive being a Cainite despite the presence of the dominant Wan Kuei would be interesting.<br /> <br /> And in-lore from various supplements, we know some assortment of Kindred HAVE inhabited or dealt in length somehow in Asia for a long time (specifically from the Lasombra supplement book off the top of my head, from the thread last year where I debated over the Obtenebration/Low Umbra/Oblivion argument), so what exactly is the problem? Nothing ever stopped anyone from doing specific games they want to set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T10:15:01-07:00","id":1444353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444319#post1444319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Familes, Analects of the Damned and Dions Phillipines material ( Wicker Wars, The Manila Trio) are all very good books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad I learned these titles, I'm going to look them up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T10:19:10-07:00","id":1444355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444336#post1444336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never understood this conceit in general from the crowd that dislike the Wan Kuei or want them &quot;removed because it stops VTM chronicles from happening in Asia&quot;... No it doesn't, you can certainly have games take place in Asia; but that doesn't mean it would be an easy course from an IC standpoint. But since when has VTM supposed to be &quot;easy&quot;? I thought part of the main fun of VTM was making up elaborate intrigues or moves for survival after becoming a Kindred, against all odds. If you'd want to be in engrossed in a higher bout of interesting difficulty, trying to survive being a Cainite despite the presence of the dominant Wan Kuei would be interesting.<br /> <br /> And in-lore from various supplements, we know some assortment of Kindred HAVE inhabited or dealt in length somehow in Asia for a long time (specifically from the Lasombra supplement book off the top of my head, from the thread last year where I debated over the Obtenebration/Low Umbra/Oblivion argument), so what exactly is the problem? Nothing ever stopped anyone from doing specific games they want to set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's the attitude that led to the Lasombra joining the Camarilla actually. People love the Lasombra and loved playing them in Camarilla games. However, they felt it was stupid and punishing to have them constantly deal with the assassins the Lore said they would.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to deal with a popular story element being &quot;punished&quot; then I don't think that's a bad thing, especially if you want to play a Camarilla Hong Kong game and think Kuei Jin are a racist concept to begin with.<br /> <br /> Which is pretty much what my friends there say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T11:21:58-07:00","id":1444360,"title":"","content":"Eh, anyone who really wants to play a Magister should either have a 'come at me bro' attitude, hidden behind a thick veneer of etiquette of course, or a seige mentality. I will say the books do greatly exaggerate the drive for the sabbat to prioritize Magister killings. The keepers rarely have such means to attack magisters with any consistency.<br /> <br /> The magisters wpuld be better served by more embraces than mass defections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T11:31:06-07:00","id":1444362,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the source material super closely, but based on my understanding of the Lasombra the only thing about their defection to the Camarilla that seems especially surprising or out of character was there apparently being some Lasombra Elders that willingly got torched as a sign of &quot;good faith&quot; to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:01:17-07:00","id":1444366,"title":"","content":"I do not know if I already posted here but I have suggestion that mayby could work. How about Wan Kuei are big in China but to retcon saying that there presence in japan whas exagerated, and in reality japan is dominated by a cainite bloodline that mayby is even their own clan because it whas founded back in the 11th century after christ from very old cainite following the path of the nomad and she embraces one of the proto ninja because they impressed her somehow and those vampireninja clans are still out their fighting a shadow war against the wan kuei and mayby the cainite invasors because they never knew they are actually one of their clans. This could even turn into a 14th clan because the vampireninjas ally with the cam to finally keep the Wan Kuei out of their holy land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:02:46-07:00","id":1444367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444362#post1444362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the source material super closely, but based on my understanding of the Lasombra the only thing about their defection to the Camarilla that seems especially surprising or out of character was there apparently being some Lasombra Elders that willingly got torched as a sign of &quot;good faith&quot; to the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took that as a sign of Lasombra genius. They knew they'd have to kill and murder a bunch of Sabbat hardliners on their way out. So they did the, &quot;oh please, please don't make us kill our Elders [who disagree with this defection] oh mighty Ventrue.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You must kill these Elders!&quot;<br /> <br /> Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:21:08-07:00","id":1444370,"title":"","content":"Lasombra strive to be leaders, not followers, and nobody wants to be given extra work and... As someone who's played slightly more Lasombra characters than he has other clans (like, 2, since I tend to play new clans a lot. Also a bunch as an ST but that's neither here nor there. The longer running lasombra was actually a cammy) all I can say is... agh it's just a terrible idea to sign yourself up for that bullshit. Also you'd think you'd actually make the deals at a local level rather than have the lasombra agree to some worldwide scheme to defect...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444366#post1444366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know if I already posted here but I have suggestion that mayby could work. How about Wan Kuei are big in China but to retcon saying that there presence in japan whas exagerated, and in reality japan is dominated by a cainite bloodline that mayby is even their own clan because it whas founded back in the 11th century after christ from very old cainite following the path of the nomad and she embraces one of the proto ninja because they impressed her somehow and those vampireninja clans are still out their fighting a shadow war against the wan kuei and mayby the cainite invasors because they never knew they are actually one of their clans. This could even turn into a 14th clan because the vampireninjas ally with the cam to finally keep the Wan Kuei out of their holy land.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh... it sounds like you're throwing people under the bus simply to save some people you like the idea of a little more. But then again I suppose I'm just saying -Throw the mean Wan Kuei into central china and give kindred the coast- but I suppose I have some rational for it. Also I think everyone would really appreciate it if we stayed a healthy distance away from samurai and ninja, at least pop-culture ideas of them. Even if you like that stuff, it doesn't look great in writing. What you've wrote especially; fighting over &quot;holy lands&quot; aren't a good idea when people still bitterly remember 'divine winds', comfort women and nanjing massacres. The less stuff that can be taken as nationalist the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-17-2021, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:27:52-07:00","id":1444371,"title":"","content":"As a Lasombra fan, I fully don't think the Ventrue are competent enough to keep the Keepers from running the Camarilla in 5 years. They haven't shown the Kings in a good light recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:44:59-07:00","id":1444372,"title":"","content":"The thing with the Ventrue is that they're <i>mostly </i>top-blokes (yeah they're 80% men at least, it's an old boys club) and they're mostly everyone's favourite princes; Dominate, Presence and Fortitude is just the spread of a charming friend you want on your side. A good ventrue is so unexceptional it doesn't get noticed, but a bad ventrue is sensational worth writing about. It'd be an error to base an understanding of the ventrue on the few notables that aren't up to par. As for the Lasombra taking them on? If they ally with the Tremere (who are themselves on a downards spiral) and the Assamites (who are very likely to side with the ventrue given their personalities) they mgiht have a chance. The issue is that the new lasombra in the cam are starving wolves while the Ventrue are entrenched and literally the best clan for building up allies. It'd be a miracle if the lasombra could take 10% of princedoms in 100 years, nevermind 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:49:49-07:00","id":1444373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444372#post1444372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the Ventrue is that they're <i>mostly </i>top-blokes (yeah they're 80% men at least, it's an old boys club) and they're mostly everyone's favourite princes; Dominate, Presence and Fortitude is just the spread of a charming friend you want on your side. A good ventrue is so unexceptional it doesn't get noticed, but a bad ventrue is sensational worth writing about. It'd be an error to base an understanding of the ventrue on the few notables that aren't up to par. As for the Lasombra taking them on? If they ally with the Tremere (who are themselves on a downards spiral) and the Assamites (who are very likely to side with the ventrue given their personalities) they mgiht have a chance. The issue is that the new lasombra in the cam are starving wolves while the Ventrue are entrenched and literally the best clan for building up allies. It'd be a miracle if the lasombra could take 10% of princedoms in 100 years, nevermind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Lasombra will be allying with the Banu Haqim and not the Tremere due to the ancient eminity between the Lasombra and Tremere. I also think that the Lasombra will perceive the Tremere as being in a state of weakness (wrongly). You see the thing is that &quot;Goratrix&quot; had a bit of fiction where he showed up at a meeting with Karl Sckret and the Carna to say that they weren't planning on making any aggressive moves.<br /> <br /> The Tremere aren't in a state of Civil War. The Lasombra are making a mistake assuming they're not going to rebound and rebound hard. Besides, if you're a Cammie then you know the dangerous Clan isn't the Tremere or the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> It's the Toreador.<br /> <br /> As for Princedoms? There's a lot of cities that are now opened thanks to the Second Inquisition. Maybe the next Prince of London will be a Keeper.<br /> <br /> Or Berlin if they retake it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:10:45-07:00","id":1444377,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra have no beef with the Tremere. you're thinking of the Tzmisce and... a lot of other guys. Honestly the Lasombra are what the Tremere would be were it not for all the organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:26:09-07:00","id":1444379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444372#post1444372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the Ventrue is that they're <i>mostly </i>top-blokes (yeah they're 80% men at least, it's an old boys club) and they're mostly everyone's favourite princes; Dominate, Presence and Fortitude is just the spread of a charming friend you want on your side. A good ventrue is so unexceptional it doesn't get noticed, but a bad ventrue is sensational worth writing about. It'd be an error to base an understanding of the ventrue on the few notables that aren't up to par. As for the Lasombra taking them on? If they ally with the Tremere (who are themselves on a downards spiral) and the Assamites (who are very likely to side with the ventrue given their personalities) they mgiht have a chance. The issue is that the new lasombra in the cam are starving wolves while the Ventrue are entrenched and literally the best clan for building up allies. It'd be a miracle if the lasombra could take 10% of princedoms in 100 years, nevermind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The take that the Ventrue are super popular is a new one for me. They're in charge most of the time because, most of the time, no one else cares as much as they do, IMO.<br /> <br /> But what matters is the Lasombra perception of the Ventrue. And broadly speaking, they've always hyped themselves up as superior to the Ventrue. So regardless of whether or not the Lasombra actually CAN take the Camarilla from the Ventrue, I don't find it especially hard to believe that they THINK they can (&quot;They&quot; being the Friends of the Night, &quot;mainstream&quot; leadership of the Clan, etc.)<br /> <br /> As a side note, I'm generally inclined to agree with the point made above about &quot;Clans leaving/joining the Camarilla&quot; being a much messier affair than such statements might indicate. Lots of Brujah and Gangrel are still with the Camarilla. A bunch of Lasombra are probably still with the Sabbat. And it is even messier with the Brujah and the Gangrel because they AREN'T Clans like the Lasombra or Ventrue, with sticks up the- I mean, centralized and organized leadership capable of making decisions collectively for the group.<br /> <br /> The thing for me is, across many Clans not just the Lasombra, one of the most common sentiments you see among Sabbat Elders is &quot;what the fuck has happened to us?&quot; There are probably lots of younger Lasombra that buy in to the Sabbat ideology and the bonds of vaulderie, along with Elder Lasombra among the Abyss Mystics who definitely fit in with the more esoteric groups that reject Humanity rather than wanting to mingle with it. But the Lasombra have largely been depicted as a Clan of shadowy manipulators wielding power from behind the scenes long before the Masquerade came along. And given that even the Sabbat maintains the &quot;Silence of the Blood,&quot; the whole idea that the concept of the Masquerade would offend the ego of any Lasombra just doesn't really hold up to me. Between the radical wings of Abyss Mystics and anarchic packs of shovelheads, I could see the &quot;mainstream&quot; Clan Lasombra, the predatory social Darwinists, looking at their membership in the Sabbat and saying &quot;well this was a good experiment, but I think it's time to abandon ship&quot; and thinking that stealing the Camarilla out from under the Ventrue would be just as much of a Take That as beating the Camarilla with another Sect. Especially since I don't really get the feeling that the Camarilla cares much about how &quot;nice&quot; you are maintaining the Masquerade. If all your asshole dickery can be covered up with &quot;gang violence&quot; or what have you, I don't think the Inner Circle is going to get too worked up if the Lasombra maintain their Masquerade with the same brutality that they did in the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:30:23-07:00","id":1444382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444377#post1444377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra have no beef with the Tremere. you're thinking of the Tzmisce and... a lot of other guys. Honestly the Lasombra are what the Tremere would be were it not for all the organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra have been killing Tremere for centuries. They also have no respect for anyone who has any form of failure.<br /> <br /> Remember the Tremere were treated like crap in the Sabbat even beyond the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Just saying I think they'd go with the Banu over the Warlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T14:51:20-07:00","id":1444392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444370#post1444370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra strive to be leaders, not followers, and nobody wants to be given extra work and... As someone who's played slightly more Lasombra characters than he has other clans (like, 2, since I tend to play new clans a lot. Also a bunch as an ST but that's neither here nor there. The longer running lasombra was actually a cammy) all I can say is... agh it's just a terrible idea to sign yourself up for that bullshit. Also you'd think you'd actually make the deals at a local level rather than have the lasombra agree to some worldwide scheme to defect...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eh... it sounds like you're throwing people under the bus simply to save some people you like the idea of a little more. But then again I suppose I'm just saying -Throw the mean Wan Kuei into central china and give kindred the coast- but I suppose I have some rational for it. Also I think everyone would really appreciate it if we stayed a healthy distance away from samurai and ninja, at least pop-culture ideas of them. Even if you like that stuff, it doesn't look great in writing. What you've wrote especially; fighting over &quot;holy lands&quot; aren't a good idea when people still bitterly remember 'divine winds', comfort women and nanjing massacres. The less stuff that can be taken as nationalist the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah mayby it does not look so well on second look. I just tried to bringing a &quot;new&quot; cainity type in japan, origin of Ninjutsu and the staying in shadows and not Wan Kuei everywhere under a hat and with Cainites being able to live long and keeping their grudges I thought this would make sense the most","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:00:29-07:00","id":1444415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444372#post1444372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the Ventrue is that they're <i>mostly </i>top-blokes (yeah they're 80% men at least, it's an old boys club) and they're mostly everyone's favourite princes; Dominate, Presence and Fortitude is just the spread of a charming friend you want on your side. A good ventrue is so unexceptional it doesn't get noticed, but a bad ventrue is sensational worth writing about. It'd be an error to base an understanding of the ventrue on the few notables that aren't up to par. As for the Lasombra taking them on? If they ally with the Tremere (who are themselves on a downards spiral) and the Assamites (who are very likely to side with the ventrue given their personalities) they mgiht have a chance. The issue is that the new lasombra in the cam are starving wolves while the Ventrue are entrenched and literally the best clan for building up allies. It'd be a miracle if the lasombra could take 10% of princedoms in 100 years, nevermind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also worth noting that even if the Lasombra have technically been forgiven and accepted by the upper echelons of the Camarilla, there's going to be lots of rank and file members and local princes who think it's just all a huge con on the part of the Sabbat to infiltrate the Camarilla and they're not going to trust the Lasombra at all, let alone allow them to start moving up to Prince status in a short period of time. If the Lasombra try to force it you'll start seeing some major rebellions against them and I imagine you'd see a lot of vampires or territories defecting to the Anarchs - better to be an Anarch than serve under some &quot;Sabbat Prince.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:17:51-07:00","id":1444419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444415#post1444415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also worth noting that even if the Lasombra have technically been forgiven and accepted by the upper echelons of the Camarilla, there's going to be lots of rank and file members and local princes who think it's just all a huge con on the part of the Sabbat to infiltrate the Camarilla and they're not going to trust the Lasombra at all, let alone allow them to start moving up to Prince status in a short period of time. If the Lasombra try to force it you'll start seeing some major rebellions against them and I imagine you'd see a lot of vampires or territories defecting to the Anarchs - better to be an Anarch than serve under some &quot;Sabbat Prince.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how much you think present-day vampires know about the Sabbat. The Sabbat in the first few Editions were things that the vast majority of vampires had never encountered in their life. Yeah, you HEARD about the Sabbat being evil monstrous Satanist vampires but you could live your entire unlife never meeting them. It was why the 1999 Crusade was so shocking since pretty much the entire East Coast had to deal with them and Atlanta too.<br /> <br /> Most vampires Embraced in the past 20 years will have no idea what a Lasombra is. Ironically, I think Ancilla among the Anarchs are most likely to remember fighting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:36:36-07:00","id":1444422,"title":"","content":"I think most of the mid-ranking members of the Camarilla (that is those embraced before 1950) probably have some fairly good ideas about the Sabbat, know those guys are dangerous, and either have their own stories or know other vampires who have been hurt or killed by them. And ~50+ year old vampires are the ones who hold more of the power in any given Camarilla city than vampires embraced less than 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> I view it kind of like if the US government had granted amnesty to half of Al-Queda members, then invited those Al-Queda members into the US, gave them citizenship and then they started taking positions of political leadership. Everything else aside, I think a lot of Americans (even people traditionally liberal) would find that to be a pretty questionable and concerning policy and there would be a ton of pushback. Younger people born after 9/11 might not care all that much, but most people older than that would be very weary of that. And for most people in the US, the Al-Queda/US dispute only goes back around a quarter of a century. Meanwhile the Sabbat has been a fanatical fundamentalist organization that's been at the throat of the Camarilla for a few centuries.<br /> <br /> I have a hard time imagining that just because the Inner Circle of the Camarilla said, &quot;These guys are cool, trust us!&quot; everyone else in the Camarilla would just nod and go along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:02:34-07:00","id":1444424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444422#post1444422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most of the mid-ranking members of the Camarilla (that is those embraced before 1950) probably have some fairly good ideas about the Sabbat, know those guys are dangerous, and either have their own stories or know other vampires who have been hurt or killed by them. And ~50+ year old vampires are the ones who hold more of the power in any given Camarilla city than vampires embraced less than 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> I view it kind of like if the US government had granted amnesty to half of Al-Queda members, then invited those Al-Queda members into the US, gave them citizenship and then they started taking positions of political leadership. Everything else aside, I think a lot of Americans (even people traditionally liberal) would find that to be a pretty questionable and concerning policy and there would be a ton of pushback. Younger people born after 9/11 might not care all that much, but most people older than that would be very weary of that. And for most people in the US, the Al-Queda/US dispute only goes back around a quarter of a century. Meanwhile the Sabbat has been a fanatical fundamentalist organization that's been at the throat of the Camarilla for a few centuries.<br /> <br /> I have a hard time imagining that just because the Inner Circle of the Camarilla said, &quot;These guys are cool, trust us!&quot; everyone else in the Camarilla would just nod and go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that if lower-ranking Al-Qaeda members offered up the higher ranks of such that they'd definitely take that deal. I remind you we have OPERATION: PAPERCLIP and other examples of enemies being brought in exchange for concessions or wealth.<br /> <br /> Whether they intend to fulfill their promises or not, the fact is that the Camarilla is not an organization that has any professed ideals. It helps things considerably in terms of real politic that the Camarilla propagates vampiric supremacy, power, and a gerontocracy rather than making nonsense promises of being for any higher ideal.<br /> <br /> It's not like the Camarilla disapproves of mass murder, lies, or torture.<br /> <br /> What they disliked about the Sabbat was they were rivals for power and prestige. Power and prestige which the Lasombra will bring while it is greatly weakened from losing so many members to the Beckoning, Anarch Revolts, and Second Inquisition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:09:01-07:00","id":1444426,"title":"","content":"Sure but the Sabbat just launched major invasions throughout Camarilla territory and killed tons of kindred like a decade ago. I just don't see most Camarilla vampires opening their arms and welcoming the Lasombra as their new leaders. The Lasombra <i>want</i> to be in charge, but I have a hard time imagining that they aren't going to have to spend decades or even a century or two, proving themselves before most Camarilla members are willing to fully trust them (insofar as vampires ever fully trust someone else) with positions of leadership. There might be a couple of places where Lasombra who've just shown up might be able to set themselves up as Princes, because of various local troubles, but those places are going to be exceptions<br /> <br /> It should be a long, long time before the Lasombra are able to amass the support of the Camarilla to the point that they can rival or or threaten the Ventrue's political power, unless something crazy happens like, we get a book telling us that the Second Inquisition suddenly wiped out half of the Ventrue in Camarilla or something silly like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:13:13-07:00","id":1444427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444426#post1444426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure but the Sabbat just launched major invasions throughout Camarilla territory and killed tons of kindred like a decade ago. I just don't see most Camarilla vampires opening their arms and welcoming the Lasombra as their new leaders. The Lasombra <i>want</i> to be in charge, but I have a hard time imagining that they aren't going to have to spend decades or even a century or two, proving themselves before most Camarilla members are willing to fully trust them (insofar as vampires ever fully trust someone else) with positions of leadership. There might be a couple of places where Lasombra who've just shown up might be able to set themselves up as Princes, because of various local troubles, but those places are going to be exceptions<br /> <br /> It should be a long, long time before the Lasombra are able to amass the support of the Camarilla to the point that they can rival or or threaten the Ventrue's political power, unless something crazy happens like, we get a book telling us that the Second Inquisition suddenly wiped out half of the Ventrue in Camarilla or something silly like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my biggest and best argument there is the fact that as nasty and angry as people might hate the Lasombra for the Sabbat's actions, they will probably hate the Ventrue more.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra provide an alternative.<br /> <br /> Mind you, canonically we know how it might go in SHADOWS OF NEW YORK where the Lasombra Embraced after the defection is treated like shit by the Primogen. They abuse her, humiliate her, and block her from any advancement even though she had nothing to do with it. The actual Lasombra defector stays out of the courts completlely while letting her absorb all the brunt of it. Which, of course, allows her to be driven to turn things around and get REAL power as a Primogen by exploiting the fact that as much as they hate her--they hate each other worse. She ends up Clan Leader and Primogen within a year of her Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:18:44-07:00","id":1444428,"title":"","content":"People don't like the Ventrue, but there are other clans that haven't spent centuries at war with the Camarilla, so it seems kind of weird that so many vampires in the Camarilla would feel that the only choice is between a Ventrue and Lasombra to the point that they would immediately begin trusting the Lasombra with positions of power and importance rather than viewing them as Sabbat infiltrators and such, which is what IMO, a lot of Camarilla vampires should be thinking about the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I think this tangent has gotten way far away from the thread topic about Kindred of the East so I'mma shut now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:22:22-07:00","id":1444429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444428#post1444428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People don't like the Ventrue, but there are other clans that haven't spent centuries at war with the Camarilla, so it seems kind of weird that so many vampires in the Camarilla would feel that the only choice is between a Ventrue and Lasombra to the point that they would immediately begin trusting the Lasombra with positions of power and importance rather than viewing them as Sabbat infiltrators and such, which is what IMO, a lot of Camarilla vampires should be thinking about the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I think this tangent has gotten way far away from the thread topic about Kindred of the East so I'mma shut now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, one of us should make a Lasombra thread to discuss their defection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:01:17-07:00","id":1444444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444316#post1444316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres a few products on Storytellers Vault ( Analects, Ghost Families, Wicker Wars etc.) that do a much better job of setting up Hungry Ghost history and background than the corebook does and they are well worth picking up as alternatives if you haven't already completely reworked things to remove all the &quot; Anime and Shaw Brothers &quot; that passes for such in the corebook.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I mean V:TM has never been particularly good about getting the Folklore right and always been a missmash of popculture takes. You have the vampire book of Mormon that's apparently so true that it violates everything we know about archaeology! We have a vampire society built on the back of comics. We have them take function from novels only a couple centuries back vs any real folklore.. I'm not even going to get into how the Followers of Set have more in common with RE Howards snakemen than anything an Egyptologist might recognize...<br /> <br /> I want native voices interpetting the dumb shit in their nation. I don't think you get a Native version of V:TM by even trying to ignore stupid popculture bits even if they've been around a couple centuries and we call them &quot;classics&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:45:49-07:00","id":1444450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444444#post1444444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? I mean V:TM has never been particularly good about getting the Folklore right and always been a missmash of popculture takes. You have the vampire book of Mormon that's apparently so true that it violates everything we know about archaeology! We have a vampire society built on the back of comics. We have them take function from novels only a couple centuries back vs any real folklore.. I'm not even going to get into how the Followers of Set have more in common with RE Howards snakemen than anything an Egyptologist might recognize...<br /> <br /> I want native voices interpetting the dumb shit in their nation. I don't think you get a Native version of V:TM by even trying to ignore stupid popculture bits even if they've been around a couple centuries and we call them &quot;classics&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the answer tends to come down to &quot;the people who actually live in those places that might want to buy the product otherwise aren't interested in having those superficial (if not dangerous: see above post) stereotypes fisted into the textbook description of the part of the world that they would presumably be playing in.&quot; And combined with those of us that think &quot;that's a reasonable thing to want,&quot; the business tries to decide which group will earn them more dollars.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember when complaining about pop culture infecting the &quot;Western&quot; depictions of vampires in Vampire: the Masquerade is that the authors are &quot;Western.&quot; They recycled Western tropes for Western audiences, having some understanding of the context of what they were influenced by and what they were creating. And even that doesn't save them from occasionally fucking up horribly (WoD: G****s). But we are all fallible humans, learning everyday, and hindsight is 20/20.<br /> <br /> To the extent that pop culture &quot;anime-esque&quot; tropes are not necessarily harmful, I don't think that removing them from the Wan Kuei, or removing the Wan Kuei over them, is absolutely necessary. But I think that fans who actually live in those places have as much, if not more, right to have their opinions and feelings considered by the writers as the fans who don't live in those places but have enjoyed the superficial portrayal of those places up to now. Ultimately, the writers themselves have the right to decide how they might want to update their setting, and the business will consider the decision that they think will produce the most profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:57:40-07:00","id":1444453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444444#post1444444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? I mean V:TM has never been particularly good about getting the Folklore right and always been a missmash of popculture takes. You have the vampire book of Mormon that's apparently so true that it violates everything we know about archaeology! We have a vampire society built on the back of comics. We have them take function from novels only a couple centuries back vs any real folklore.. I'm not even going to get into how the Followers of Set have more in common with RE Howards snakemen than anything an Egyptologist might recognize...<br /> <br /> I want native voices interpetting the dumb shit in their nation. I don't think you get a Native version of V:TM by even trying to ignore stupid popculture bits even if they've been around a couple centuries and we call them &quot;classics&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mostly because I ( and most of the people I've played with over the years) think that VtM shouldn't get a pass on unbelievably stupid shit which is why everything you've mentioned there has been reworked by us in our campaigns to be less FUBAR and occasionally thrown out wholesale. Sure, some people love the stupid shit and think it should be sacrosanct but I don't know any of them in real life so they don't really have any impact on MyWoD.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T00:34:39-07:00","id":1444457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444422#post1444422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I view it kind of like if the US government had granted amnesty to half of Al-Queda members, then invited those Al-Queda members into the US, gave them citizenship and then they started taking positions of political leadership.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should know the US literally did that to Nazis and to a lesser extent (but more shockingly) Japanese war criminals (who asked for amnesty in exchange for the results of brutal human experimentation.)<br /> <br /> Anyhow, its not hard to insert most clans into the east. The Lasombra particularly like coastal settlements, the gangrel are everywhere, the nosferatu are wanting to flee papa nos, Toreador reproduce like rabits and maybe want to see art. The malks get everywhere no matter how you try, the other clans follow the work... I think only Tzmisce are a difficult sell. Perhaps one got stollen by the mongols and transplanted himself in the east, setting up a brood. or perhaps the eldest himself established some bloodlines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-18-2021, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T11:08:44-07:00","id":1444524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444457#post1444457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should know the US literally did that to Nazis and to a lesser extent (but more shockingly) Japanese war criminals (who asked for amnesty in exchange for the results of brutal human experimentation.)<br /> <br /> Anyhow, its not hard to insert most clans into the east. The Lasombra particularly like coastal settlements, the gangrel are everywhere, the nosferatu are wanting to flee papa nos, Toreador reproduce like rabits and maybe want to see art. The malks get everywhere no matter how you try, the other clans follow the work... I think only Tzmisce are a difficult sell. Perhaps one got stollen by the mongols and transplanted himself in the east, setting up a brood. or perhaps the eldest himself established some bloodlines</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're willing to dip into Revised, one of the eldest childer of the Eldest is supposed to be in torpor in Sri Lanka, Kartarirya. Their childer, Ratti-Ben, is in turn described as a thorn in the side of the local Ravnos authorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T18:30:20-07:00","id":1444579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444258#post1444258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like that is definitely a weakness because European mythology is no less spiritual focused but people are much happier to remove the Angels/Demons and so on out of it all.<br /> <br /> When a Changeling/Demon: The Fallen/Wraith part of the Umbra would be just as interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still be spiritually focused without having to share in the same spirit world as Werewolf. Changeling managed it by making the Dreaming not the same thing as the Umbra. Demon even did this to some extend, as the Abyss that imprisoned the Elohim was definitely not like other spiritual worlds, in being a nullity, an oubliette without time; they also never go to the Middle Umbra of Werewolf. It doesn't exist, as far as D:tF is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T18:33:08-07:00","id":1444580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444579#post1444579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can still be spiritually focused without having to share in the same spirit world as Werewolf. Changeling managed it by making the Dreaming not the same thing as the Umbra. Demon even did this to some extend, as the Abyss that imprisoned the Elohim was definitely not like other spiritual worlds, in being a nullity, an oubliette without time; they also never go to the Middle Umbra of Werewolf. It doesn't exist, as far as D:tF is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, it is explictly linked to Wraith: The Oblivion because those are the souls that the Demon Lords in the Labyrinth torment and use the dreams of to make a more traditional Hell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:47:50-07:00","id":1444618,"title":"","content":"The Wan kuei literally believe in a thousand hells (which might be a euphemism for a really big, difficult to count number rather than specifically 1000) it's quite reductionist to insist on a limited number of abysses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-19-2021, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T04:55:35-07:00","id":1444628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444618#post1444618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wan kuei literally believe in a thousand hells (which might be a euphemism for a really big, difficult to count number rather than specifically 1000) it's quite reductionist to insist on a limited number of abysses</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For good or ill it looks like that is going to change, the spirit world already got streamlined by linking Obten explicitly to Necromancy, rather than leaving it open to being connected to the far horizon. So we are already down 1 abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:27:10-07:00","id":1444633,"title":"","content":"I fail to see why the Abyss(es) are being mentioned here in regards to KotE. In the lore behind the Yama Kings within the said line, the August Personage of Jade never punished them, despite them being the cause for the Wan Kuei's corruption and becoming what they became; nor punishing them at all for abusing their offices assigned by the August Personage of Jade for being the Wardens' of Hell. The August Personage of Jade just disappeared one day and they merely continued on with their ambitions. <br /> <br /> This is directly contrary to any of the &quot;Abyss drama&quot; we see in D:TF and the subsequent derailing of who's actually who in the lane of Demons in oWoD and who actually the so-called &quot;creator&quot; is due to how D:TF panned out (especially the awkwardness of how these supposed D:TF &quot;Demons&quot; don't know about the Yama Kings at all; nor any semblance of the other Umbra beside the Low Umbra, even despite claiming to have made the Universe with the help of the &quot;God&quot; from D:TF) . <br /> <br /> Regardless of this and to continue on point, the Yama Kings have nothing to do with the Abyss and most of their functions reside in the Middle-Umbra at this point, where most of the 1000 Hells exist (though of course the 1000 Hells itself has periphery overlap with the Low Umbra). They never were trapped rendered helpless to do anything. They've probably been active concurrently as long, but not as long as the Mokol\u00e8. It's not that hard to parse at all, but you're right that for some reason they're going to &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;streamline&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; for some inane reason if they revisit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T09:53:59-07:00","id":1444670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444633#post1444633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see why the Abyss(es) are being mentioned here in regards to KotE. In the lore behind the Yama Kings within the said line, the August Personage of Jade never punished them, despite them being the cause for the Wan Kuei's corruption and becoming what they became; nor punishing them at all for abusing their offices assigned by the August Personage of Jade for being the Wardens' of Hell. The August Personage of Jade just disappeared one day and they merely continued on with their ambitions.<br /> <br /> <b>This is directly contrary to any of the &quot;Abyss drama&quot; we see in D:TF and the subsequent derailing of who's actually who in the lane of Demons in oWoD and who actually the so-called &quot;creator&quot; is due to how D:TF panned out (especially the awkwardness of how these supposed D:TF &quot;Demons&quot; don't know about the Yama Kings at all; nor any semblance of the other Umbra beside the Low Umbra, even despite claiming to have made the Universe with the help of the &quot;God&quot; from D:TF) .</b><br /> <br /> Regardless of this and to continue on point, the Yama Kings have nothing to do with the Abyss and most of their functions reside in the Middle-Umbra at this point, where most of the 1000 Hells exist (though of course the 1000 Hells itself has periphery overlap with the Low Umbra). They never were trapped rendered helpless to do anything. They've probably been active concurrently as long, but not as long as the Mokol\u00e8. It's not that hard to parse at all, but you're right that for some reason they're going to &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;streamline&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; for some inane reason if they revisit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it feels like a joke, albeit a funny one.<br /> <br /> The Yama Kings and Kuei Jin as well as the Werewolves have objective proof positive their worldview is true.<br /> <br /> And so the Demons that contradict all of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T10:10:54-07:00","id":1444674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444670#post1444670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, it feels like a joke, albeit a funny one.<br /> <br /> The Yama Kings and Kuei Jin as well as the Werewolves have objective proof positive their worldview is true.<br /> <br /> And so the Demons that contradict all of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think oWoD has much more fun with the idea of &quot;Truth.&quot; It's messy as hell, but if you start from the premise &quot;everyone is right, but also very wrong,&quot; then the fun comes in when you start deciding how you want all of that to shake out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T13:29:41-07:00","id":1444707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444580#post1444580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, it is explictly linked to Wraith: The Oblivion because those are the souls that the Demon Lords in the Labyrinth torment and use the dreams of to make a more traditional Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems quite unnecessary. One wonders if it might get retconned. The Thousand Hells of KotE, too, seem like they could just jettison being forged from bits of Wraith and Werewolf and say that it resembles both Middle and Dark Umbra while not actually being a part of either.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's not like there was much heat to either bit of lore. Anything regarding D:tF just popped up about the time that all the books were wrapping up, and any connection that The (Real) Yellow Springs had to other portions of the Umbra doesn't seem like it was exploited, either. Might as well have never made the connections in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-19-2021, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T20:03:17-07:00","id":1444751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it is explictly linked to Wraith: The Oblivion because those are the souls that the Demon Lords in the Labyrinth torment and use the dreams of to make a more traditional Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute, now I just remembered to ask this to begin with; where exactly do you get this idea from? The Abyss in D:TF is merely a prison and nothing else. And what &quot;Demon Lords&quot; are you even talking about? Neverborn, do you mean? They don't have anything to do with the Abyss or the events surrounding its creation as per D:TF. The Neverborn are entities that were created as soon as the conception of Life and Death split apart. <br /> <br /> Not only that the Neverborn were only active for a little while at that, with almost all falling into a deep sleep in the Labyrinth. The dreams they have aren't about making a &quot;traditional Hell&quot; (Wraith explicitly goes on about the nebulosity of the Underworld and how it isn't here nor there, on whether or not its &quot;Hell or Heaven&quot;; <i>Its Just Is As It Is</i>), their dreams have no particular meaning, just pure unadulterated maleficence. <br /> <br /> I also fail to see what &quot;souls&quot; do you mean in particular with the Abyss being discussed, with the added inference toward the Neverborn (or &quot;Demon Lords&quot; as you called them) being related to it. Do you mean the souls of the D:TF Demons/Eloheim? How, when they're trapped in someplace that apparently is under Oblivion itself already? Also the Neverborn are sleeping, why do you think they need souls for? Even if they were active; they wouldn't waste time in souls they can't acquire or are almost fully out of reach from, why do that when you have scores of humanity to harvest from with the aid of their Spectre hordes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T20:04:51-07:00","id":1444752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444751#post1444751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait a minute, now I just remembered to ask this to begin with; where exactly do you get this idea from? The Abyss in D:TF is merely a prison and nothing else. And what &quot;Demon Lords&quot; are you even talking about? Neverborn, do you mean? They don't have anything to do with the Abyss or the events surrounding its creation as per D:TF. The Neverborn are entities that were created as soon as the conception of Life and Death split apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're jumping around a lot.<br /> <br /> You do realize the Demons of Demon: The Fallen all have their true names owned by Demon Lords there that can't get out. Only the smallest and weakest demons escaped from the crack in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn were also revealed to have always been the Demons in Hell-Hell.<br /> <br /> Here's what the Wiki says about it:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abyss_(DTF\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abyss_(DTF</a>)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T20:35:46-07:00","id":1444762,"title":"","content":"The Abyss (D:TF) wiki article claims nothing about the Neverborn being involved with the Abyss at all. All it says that only Fallen inhabit it (which is correct). And there is no information about anything concerning &quot;Demon Lords&quot; at all in the article aswell. I even did the courtesy to search that term up on the wiki and it only brings up a spinoff in-character game from &quot;M:TA: The Fallen Tower: Las Vegas&quot;. (Preemptive Edit: Scratch all that, because I actually misread it. Its &quot;Death Lord Games, not Demon Lords&quot;)<br /> <br /> Also I saw nowhere in the D:TF core book that mentions in the Abyss itself of the more &quot;larger&quot; Demons owning other ones at all. All there is about &quot;size or power differentiation&quot; between the Fallen is merely mentions and facts of what they can possess (whether they can possess a human or an object), or who can escape the Abyss easier (smaller and more moderate powered can escape easier, while larger and more powered have it harder). <br /> <br /> If this were actually true by D:TF, then atleast a big plotpoint in the epilogue section of the book would mention as such; since your future character in that game will supposedly be owned by another Demon/Fallen. But this isn't a thing at all. Also the Neverborn aren't even mentioned once in the D:TF core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T20:37:54-07:00","id":1444763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444762#post1444762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss (D:TF) wiki article claims nothing about the Neverborn being involved with the Abyss at all. All it says that only Fallen inhabit it (which is correct). And there is no information about anything concerning &quot;Demon Lords&quot; at all in the article aswell. I even did the courtesy to search that term up on the wiki and it only brings up a spinoff in-character game from &quot;M:TA: The Fallen Tower: Las Vegas&quot;. (Preemptive Edit: Scratch all that, because I actually misread it. Its &quot;Death Lord Games, not Demon Lords&quot;)<br /> <br /> Also I saw nowhere in the D:TF core book that mentions in the Abyss itself of the more &quot;larger&quot; Demons owning other ones at all. All there is about &quot;size or power differentiation&quot; between the Fallen is merely mentions and facts of what they can possess (whether they can possess a human or an object), or who can escape the Abyss easier (smaller and more moderate powered can escape easier, while larger and more powered have it harder).<br /> <br /> If this were actually true by D:TF, then atleast a big plotpoint in the epilogue section of the book would mention as such; since your future character in that game will supposedly be owned by another Demon/Fallen. But this isn't a thing at all. Also the Neverborn aren't even mentioned once in the D:TF core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured just sharing the Abyss section would be enough but yes, it's three different things you're asking about.<br /> <br /> Here's a thread about the discussion of the D:TF retcons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321285-what-is-your-opinion-of-demon-s-connection-to-wraith\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321285-what-is-your-opinion-of-demon-s-connection-to-wraith\"> What is your opinion of Demon's connection to Wraith? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321285-what-is-your-opinion-of-demon-s-connection-to-wraith\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321285-what-is-your-opinion-of-demon-s-connection-to-wraith </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> For those few who don't know, Demon: The Fallen explored; or perhaps one should say &amp;quot;retconned&amp;quot;; the origins of the Underworld of Wraith. According to it, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T20:52:12-07:00","id":1444767,"title":"","content":"I parsed through that told thread and agreed with Khalessi (is there any point @'ing that account? Seems pretty dead.. no pun intended). Most of D:TF was mishaps and glutterances that had no baring on actual Wraith itself. <br /> <br /> Removing Wraith by itself and just speaking on D:TF alone, you're still not right at all in what you talk about. What Demon Lords did you mean, what plotpoint that all the more stronger Fallen intrinsically own the smaller ones (because this doesn't exist in D:TF), and what do you mean the Neverborn use the souls of Eloheim/Fallen for anything? They do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T22:52:28-07:00","id":1444783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321285-what-is-your-opinion-of-demon-s-connection-to-wraith#post1321285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those few who don't know, Demon: The Fallen explored; or perhaps one should say &quot;retconned&quot;; the origins of the Underworld of Wraith. According to it, the Underworld was the creation of the Alabaster Legion, there was a Slayer named Charon; who may or may have not been the same Charon who would become the Emperor of Stygia; who yielded a demon-made scythe named Siklos; which may or may have not been the same scythe used by the aforementioned emperor;<b> the Neverborn are implied to possibly be the last demons of the Alabaster Legion, the Tempest was created by the sacrifice of a Devil, the Ferrymen are actually the souls of the Nephilim, etc.</b><br /> <br /> I'd like to know what the fans of Wraith think of these developments. Do you like these backgrounds? Do you feel that they are unnecessary and cheapen the setting? Do you completely ignore them?<br /> <br /> Also, have you ever explored these ideas in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that is what he is referring to. I have not read the DtF source material, so I can't speak to the veracity of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T02:57:06-07:00","id":1444808,"title":"","content":"Yes, however all that is bolded isn't &quot;true&quot; (this word gets abused alot, doesn't it?) at all. Especially about the Neverborn being Demons because that would imply Fallen beside the Earthbound and Lucifer residing outside the Abyss be possible (it's not; and this is inferencing pre-Week of Nightmares of course). And not even the Alabaster Legion wiki page even mentions either of these &quot;implications&quot;. The simple answer is that the Neverborn came precisely into existence when Life split from Death. The Tempest also could've not been made by a Devil, because that supposedly was the process of the Slayers.<br /> <br /> Having the Tempest being a cause-effect sacrifice of a Devil doesn't make sense by itself either. And like what Khalessi discussed in that previous very old thread, the Ferrymen's origin and backstory have already been established in W:tO itself. Demon being a line that had far reaching &quot;implications&quot; to &quot;&quot;&quot;branch&quot;&quot;&quot; about into other game lines, but also categorically aswell not caring about the already established lore of other lines is notorious (which is why its not good in my opinion and why I dislike it).<br /> <br /> By itself from what was claimed before still doesn't make sense. Even if the &quot;Alabaster&quot; implication in relation to the Neverborn were actually true; they still would not be able to have any interaction with the Abyss because; A) they'd be in a sleep in the Labyrinth itself, with no possible communication or interaction with any of the Fallen in the &quot;Abyss&quot;; And B), there is no single proof that the Neverborn would need Fallen souls to shape the Low Umbra itself as the previous claim made. They're the Neverborn. That enough being said should come across the fact that as soon as the Neverborn came into existence, they could fabricate around the Low Umbra easily as per Wraith's lore. Even then like I mention time and again as a point, the Abyss is completely locked off and the Neverborn wouldn't be able to utilize souls within the Abyss as resources.<br /> <br /> The Abyss quite frankly has nothing to do with the Neverborn, nor anything truly relevant in Wraith; so no, there is no real &quot;link&quot; and the pseudo-&quot;linkage&quot; there is from the bludgeon-inducement <i>retroactivity</i> that comes from D:TF doesn't even match up on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T08:39:46-07:00","id":1444831,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I do actually agree with you here. I don't generally like takes that reduce one game's canon down to another entirely.<br /> <br /> But having it listed as an option for players who want crossover, but very Demon-centric, it's fine. Having the Demons *believe* it, regardless of the truth of the matter, is even better.<br /> <br /> But we've also started to drift off-topic, maybe another thread for the pros and cons of Demon crossover plot hooks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:34:53-07:00","id":1444837,"title":"","content":"No need for another thread, I think, since this whole sub-discussion had to do and started with KotE itself somehow being related to Abyss (when it definitely isn't). Also KotE itself heavily dealt with aspects of all of the Umbra anyway; also again added that Yama Kings are Demons, but not the Abrahamic based ones seen in D:TF (which is probably why this point was even brought up in the first place).<br /> <br /> And yes, having options for story takes is fine for specific games (because no individual game stays to the notion of &quot;canon&quot;), is fine, I agree with that. However, when out from the context of an individual game and speaking about the lore in general, it generally is helpful be atleast somewhat accurate in claims being made. The crossover points mentioned earlier aren't even correct and the points about base D:TF alone isn't correct either.<br /> <br /> The Fallen are completely unaware of the Neverborn. The Fallen inside the Abyss never had any suzerain-tributary relations in the Abyss; it was a pure pitch-blackness and they were completely were unaware on who-was-who. Neither is any of the stuff about the Fallen being Neverborn. Even if taken at face-value, the original claim/inference that they're descended from the Alabaster Legion and saying that they need &quot;souls from the Abyss&quot; to shape the Low Umbra doesn't make sense; since the Alabaster Legion was literally composed of Slayers and their whole purpose was building/establishing the Low Umbra per D:TF's strewn together lore.<br /> <br /> Why would they need Fallen souls to do what they do? And like I mentioned already, the Abyss was a near-impenetrable prison only slightly cracked post-Week of Nightmares; the Neverborn doesn't didn't interact with the Abyss for resource extraction pertaining toward Fallen/Eloheim souls.<br /> <br /> The Ferrymen also definitely aren't the souls of the &quot;Nephilim&quot; because they were literally founded as the &quot;Boatmen's Society or the Oath-circle of the Oar&quot; after (Wraith) Charon was ennobled his mandate by the Lady of Fate to rule the Underworld. The Ferrymen were just regular Wraiths, nothing to do with the Fallen (atleast for the most part, since the wiki blurb I see mentions that some Nephilim souls worked as Ferrymen, but that's only some and not the whole organization; and the Nephilim's origin lie in the fact that they're offspring of humans and demons (checking the boxes for Abrahamic stuff). They have little thing with most of the Ferrymen beyond some of them going into the Ferrymen. Also the Neph-peeps aren't even Fallen too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:40:50-07:00","id":1444839,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, no crossover.<br /> <br /> Shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:37:19-07:00","id":1444934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444839#post1444839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha, no crossover.<br /> <br /> Shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a radical interpretation of the previous posts unsupported by their contents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:38:24-07:00","id":1444937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444934#post1444934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a radical interpretation of the previous posts unsupported by their contents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:07:52-07:00","id":1445194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444450#post1444450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the answer tends to come down to &quot;the people who actually live in those places that might want to buy the product otherwise aren't interested in having those superficial (if not dangerous: see above post) stereotypes fisted into the textbook description of the part of the world that they would presumably be playing in.&quot; And combined with those of us that think &quot;that's a reasonable thing to want,&quot; the business tries to decide which group will earn them more dollars.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember when complaining about pop culture infecting the &quot;Western&quot; depictions of vampires in Vampire: the Masquerade is that the authors are &quot;Western.&quot; They recycled Western tropes for Western audiences, having some understanding of the context of what they were influenced by and what they were creating. And even that doesn't save them from occasionally fucking up horribly (WoD: G****s). But we are all fallible humans, learning everyday, and hindsight is 20/20.<br /> <br /> To the extent that pop culture &quot;anime-esque&quot; tropes are not necessarily harmful, I don't think that removing them from the Wan Kuei, or removing the Wan Kuei over them, is absolutely necessary. But I think that fans who actually live in those places have as much, if not more, right to have their opinions and feelings considered by the writers as the fans who don't live in those places but have enjoyed the superficial portrayal of those places up to now. Ultimately, the writers themselves have the right to decide how they might want to update their setting, and the business will consider the decision that they think will produce the most profit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am saying I think there is an achievable version of say &quot;Vampire Japan&quot; that leans heavily into anime tropes.. if written by LOCAL voices. It probably looks very different from KOTE but going for an explicitly &quot;Realistic&quot; take of say Japanese myth(much less other cultures in Asia) would perhaps be just as fetishing. It also might be something like &quot;Vampires didn't show up until Admiral Perry&quot; I am not an expert on Japanese Pop culture, though I do part take of it and have theories. <br /> <br /> Generally Vampires are seen as Western Supernatural beings. One could litterally tie the spread of Vamprism with Western Imperialism... the metaphor would be unsubtle. <br /> <br /> The other is vampire aren't &quot;created&quot; They are born that way. This would be an interesting take a local fera holding the Niche until Western imperalism pushed them back.<br /> <br /> Jiang-shi are sort of theirown thing? They aren't any more vampires than Kitsune. Honestly given how they treat sapient Zombies in anime I'd say there was Millage to make WK a universe phenomemon but that's its own thing.<br /> <br /> But I am just an ignorant white man on the internet so I don't really have a deep dive to give.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444453#post1444453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mostly because I ( and most of the people I've played with over the years) think that VtM shouldn't get a pass on unbelievably stupid shit which is why everything you've mentioned there has been reworked by us in our campaigns to be less FUBAR and occasionally thrown out wholesale. Sure, some people love the stupid shit and think it should be sacrosanct but I don't know any of them in real life so they don't really have any impact on MyWoD.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine playing Vampire without any of the clans, the caine myth, generation, 90 percent of the powers... the idea of a Masquerade functioning at all...the Masquerade functioning in a world where Sabbat play Games of Instinct. That there are enough Vampires that exist to have anything resembling a society.... really once you start pulling out &quot;this is dumb&quot; there isn't much left.<br /> <br /> I accept this is a dumb unrealistic setting with certain tropes and concepts. Like I don't go into D&amp;D and start asking about what do the Goblins eat. It just sort of starts falling apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T21:52:49-07:00","id":1445219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445194#post1445194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am saying I think there is an achievable version of say &quot;Vampire Japan&quot; that leans heavily into anime tropes.. if written by LOCAL voices. It probably looks very different from KOTE but going for an explicitly &quot;Realistic&quot; take of say Japanese myth(much less other cultures in Asia) would perhaps be just as fetishing. It also might be something like &quot;Vampires didn't show up until Admiral Perry&quot; I am not an expert on Japanese Pop culture, though I do part take of it and have theories.<br /> <br /> Generally Vampires are seen as Western Supernatural beings. One could litterally tie the spread of Vamprism with Western Imperialism... the metaphor would be unsubtle.<br /> <br /> The other is vampire aren't &quot;created&quot; They are born that way. This would be an interesting take a local fera holding the Niche until Western imperalism pushed them back.<br /> <br /> Jiang-shi are sort of theirown thing? They aren't any more vampires than Kitsune. Honestly given how they treat sapient Zombies in anime I'd say there was Millage to make WK a universe phenomemon but that's its own thing.<br /> <br /> But I am just an ignorant white man on the internet so I don't really have a deep dive to give.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can't imagine playing Vampire without any of the clans, the caine myth, generation, 90 percent of the powers... the idea of a Masquerade functioning at all...the Masquerade functioning in a world where Sabbat play Games of Instinct. That there are enough Vampires that exist to have anything resembling a society.... really once you start pulling out &quot;this is dumb&quot; there isn't much left.<br /> <br /> I accept this is a dumb unrealistic setting with certain tropes and concepts. Like I don't go into D&amp;D and start asking about what do the Goblins eat. It just sort of starts falling apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>As my above point mentioned, I don't have a problem with &quot;anime-style&quot; tropes being included in Asian World of Darkness content (or any, really), but the people who live in those places should be considered when determining the content written for those regions.<br /> <br /> Lots of people here would appreciate a heavily updated game that would be very different from KotE, as posts above have indicated. But just as many seem to hate the notion of those kinds of changes being made, for reasons. It's a decision that is likely to be rather unpopular with a large group of fans, no matter which decision is made. So they skip it for the 20A edition, because that's simple enough. I don't follow V5 closely enough to know if they have settled on &quot;no more Wan Kuei&quot; or not in V5, but that's an edition where they will probably have to decide at some point.<br /> <br /> It wasn't really directed at me, but I want to respond to your comment about the &quot;dumb unrealistic setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> The unfortunate thing is that the World of Darkness is stuck in a bind that many other RPGs avoid. It's not set in some far off other-place with other-people, where even when there are clearly real-world influences the authors usually manage to &quot;file the serial numbers off,&quot; so the people being stereotyped usually have to be looking really hard to catch it. The World of Darkness is set on Earth. Not OUR Earth, but Earth, with all the same countries and ethnicities and religions for the most part. And that means that real people, real history, is getting dragged up and churned out as &quot;content.&quot; And simply being a &quot;darker&quot; version of our world can't work as a blanket pass, because there often isn't some obvious line between what is &quot;grimdarkification&quot; and what is a genuine expression of superficial attitudes and understandings about REAL people.<br /> <br /> In a D&amp;D-esque LARP a player can probably get away with playing as an anti-Elf racist or bigot without anyone's feelings being hurt. But using CTPhipps' example from above, REAL racists can use the FAKE racism in the game at LARPs to cover for their REAL racism against other players. It's just not the same thing, and it can't be treated as the same thing.<br /> <br /> PS Perhaps even more importantly, they cannot control whether or not their readers can properly distinguish between &quot;grimdarkification,&quot; ignorant stereotypes, or &quot;reality.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T21:59:29-07:00","id":1445221,"title":"","content":"Very good points, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a><br /> <br /> One thing also is that a lot of tables have varying degrees of &quot;seriousness&quot; that can't really be entirely accounted for. To use another example, I have run games that are:<br /> <br /> * <b>Gotham City by Night</b> with honest to God actual Batman as a character.<br /> <br /> * <b>Deeply Tragic </b>personal story of horror and nightmarish tragedy.<br /> <br /> * Basically just <b>Hellsing</b>, complete with Nazi vampires for the Camarilla Archons to kill.<br /> <br /> * <b>Epic Romance</b><br /> <br /> All of them are valid interpretations of V:TM. Over the top anime may be fine for some players but others may have been expecting something a great deal more serious.<br /> <br /> If you have the time, there's an excellent Mod for BLOODLINES that's about 30 minutes long that attempts to do a &quot;serious&quot; presentation of the Kuei-Jin as something other than Female Lo Pan and her minions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rlZi5uaUSBs\" data-code=\"rlZi5uaUSBs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/rlZi5uaUSBs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T23:28:35-07:00","id":1445227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445219#post1445219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As my above point mentioned, I don't have a problem with &quot;anime-style&quot; tropes being included in Asian World of Darkness content (or any, really), but the people who live in those places should be considered when determining the content written for those regions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and amazingly for example anime is made.. in Japan. There should be a search for Local voices. There are a lot of good Rpg design elements in Japan(I use Japan because these are ones I actually have experience with). Many of them built around extended one shots with marathon gaming.<br /> <br /> So games I've played that were translated were: Double cross and Kamigakuri both of which extended games... and some that didn't work so well anything but single shots(Maid, Tenro bansho) of those three of those I would consider having mechanics that have things to say about WOD and vampire.<br /> <br /> Double cross, Kamigakuri and TBZ all have... a sort of &quot;wassail&quot; condition. But its not something you are likely to hit in the middle of setting but rather at the end of the Adventure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kami and Dx both have you picking up connections similar to Touchstones but you do so during the game proper by interacting with NPCs rather than declaring them premptively. Then at the end of the Adventure you get a number of dice based on those connections you build and maintained in contrast to your Wassailing conditions.. which have been built up by using your various powers. Essentially you've built all these times risking giving inot the beast for extra power.. or to survive or what have you and now its come to pay. But the friendships you made along the way may keep you from becoming the monster you fear you become.<br /> <br /> Or you fail and become a monster.<br /> <br /> TBZ is.. more complicated than that. If you have more than 108 points(These include powers, connections.. even points in enemies) you become evil at the end of the adventure.. So there's alot of spending points for super attacks at the end... alot of sheading of hatreds etc its.. interesting and worth looking at.<br /> <br /> All Three of these games are DEEPLY Steeped in Anime tropes all have a personal horror/psychological angle.<br /> <br /> So My entire issue is that &quot;de-animefying&quot; the game is a goal in and of itself. That's it. Saying &quot;We improved it by making not anime&quot; doesn't improve anything. Saying &quot;the writer is from...&quot; is an improvement. Being less Shaw brothers is not an innate good. The selling point of an improved KOTE should be &quot;The writer is From....&quot; and what work they have done. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lots of people here would appreciate a heavily updated game that would be very different from KotE, as posts above have indicated. But just as many seem to hate the notion of those kinds of changes being made, for reasons. It's a decision that is likely to be rather unpopular with a large group of fans, no matter which decision is made. So they skip it for the 20A edition, because that's simple enough. I don't follow V5 closely enough to know if they have settled on &quot;no more Wan Kuei&quot; or not in V5, but that's an edition where they will probably have to decide at some point.<br /> <br /> It wasn't really directed at me, but I want to respond to your comment about the &quot;dumb unrealistic setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> The unfortunate thing is that the World of Darkness is stuck in a bind that many other RPGs avoid. It's not set in some far off other-place with other-people, where even when there are clearly real-world influences the authors usually manage to &quot;file the serial numbers off,&quot; so the people being stereotyped usually have to be looking really hard to catch it. The World of Darkness is set on Earth. Not OUR Earth, but Earth, with all the same countries and ethnicities and religions for the most part. And that means that real people, real history, is getting dragged up and churned out as &quot;content.&quot; And simply being a &quot;darker&quot; version of our world can't work as a blanket pass, because there often isn't some obvious line between what is &quot;grimdarkification&quot; and what is a genuine expression of superficial attitudes and understandings about REAL people.<br /> <br /> In a D&amp;D-esque LARP a player can probably get away with playing as an anti-Elf racist or bigot without anyone's feelings being hurt. But using CTPhipps' example from above, REAL racists can use the FAKE racism in the game at LARPs to cover for their REAL racism against other players. It's just not the same thing, and it can't be treated as the same thing.<br /> <br /> PS Perhaps even more importantly, they cannot control whether or not their readers can properly distinguish between &quot;grimdarkification,&quot; ignorant stereotypes, or &quot;reality.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I feel like we are completely talking past eachother here.<br /> <br /> A vampire illuminati is stupid but cool<br /> <br /> Romani vampires are compelled to steal is just racist.(I&quot;m also giving a dirty look to classic Tzim but that's more slavic word salad)<br /> <br /> There is a vampire book of Mormon!-Stupid and not hurting anyone asside from biblical scholars.<br /> <br /> There's a vampire power that lets you throw blasts of energy like a DBz character dumb but cool<br /> <br /> Asian people have different souls. Racist.<br /> <br /> Asian people are more likely to practice martial arts and need a whole separate broken mechanic for it-Racist<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You can pick stuff that is Dumb but cool without it being racist. IT being Dumb but cool is not justification for including bigotted things in your game. That doesn't mean going the other direction too far doesn't sort of lose the point. This after all game with a vampire book of Mormon and a Vampire Illuminati. It included RE HOWARD snake men as a vampire clan and space alien WAMPYRII as another. That one one in Japan might throw dragon ball z blasts isn't particularly dumber than that.<br /> <br /> The only Asian people can rise? that's problematic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T00:24:33-07:00","id":1445235,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help Japan doesn't have a Kuei-Jin myth.<br /> <br /> A couple of points, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampire illuminati is stupid but cool </div> </div> </div>The rich and powerful drink the blood of the working class. As metaphors go, it's hardly a bad one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a vampire book of Mormon!-Stupid and not hurting anyone asside from biblical scholars. </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't objectively supernatural creatures h