is an improvement. Being less Shaw brothers is not an innate good. The selling point of an improved KOTE should be &quot;The writer is From....&quot; and what work they have done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like we are completely talking past eachother here.<br /> <br /> A vampire illuminati is stupid but cool<br /> <br /> Romani vampires are compelled to steal is just racist.(I&quot;m also giving a dirty look to classic Tzim but that's more slavic word salad)<br /> <br /> There is a vampire book of Mormon!-Stupid and not hurting anyone asside from biblical scholars.<br /> <br /> There's a vampire power that lets you throw blasts of energy like a DBz character dumb but cool<br /> <br /> Asian people have different souls. Racist.<br /> <br /> Asian people are more likely to practice martial arts and need a whole separate broken mechanic for it-Racist<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You can pick stuff that is Dumb but cool without it being racist. IT being Dumb but cool is not justification for including bigotted things in your game. That doesn't mean going the other direction too far doesn't sort of lose the point. This after all game with a vampire book of Mormon and a Vampire Illuminati. It included RE HOWARD snake men as a vampire clan and space alien WAMPYRII as another. That one one in Japan might throw dragon ball z blasts isn't particularly dumber than that.<br /> <br /> The only Asian people can rise? that's problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right.<br /> <br /> We ARE talking past each other.<br /> <br /> There is literally nowhere that I have called for &quot;de-animification for de-animification's sake.&quot; I've been arguing for &quot;de-animification if the people living there want things de-animificated.&quot; Maybe I'm getting hooked into your disagreement with Damian May there, but that hasn't been my position. Ever.<br /> <br /> MY point is that CTPhipps has provided examples above of fans who DON'T want &quot;Kindred of the East&quot; to be a bunch of kung-fu Orientalism. Whether or not that includes Anime Tropes is beyond my ability to answer, because I'm making a second-hand reference to someone else's conversation. The most likely answer is that there are groups in both camps, and figuring out exactly where the lines will be drawn is going to be hard when part of the fanbase goes off every time you discuss making any kind of meaningful change.<br /> <br /> MY disagreement is with the people arguing that there's no reason to change the original KotE. That does not seem to be your position, so we are not in disagreement as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> PS Yes, Anime is made in Japan. And there is a lot of Asia that is *not* Japan. I have not studied pop culture trends in Asia especially closely, so I don't know if maybe anime is huge everywhere in Asia, but it kind of seems reductive to assume that because anime is Japanese that it will be welcome in World of Darkness content covering *all* of Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-22-2021, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T09:07:03-07:00","id":1445277,"title":"","content":"*most Japanese anime seems to be animated by Korean studios these days. <br /> <br /> But, eh, yeah nah let's not make rulebooks in accordance to 'anime'. First off, Otakus are shunned in Japan; Anime isn't as mainstream as you think it is. Nor is tabletop gaming of course, but I'd like to pretend we're cool kids, not a bunch of weaboos who put japan ahead of the rest of asia because we like the cartoons they started pouring out post wwII so you'd think they were a harmless nation who'd never done anything wrong. <br /> Just be try to be neutral. Nothing's wrong with neutral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T09:59:50-07:00","id":1445282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445244#post1445244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the biggest problem is still thus;<br /> Asians hate eachother. I had a longwinded post describing the specifics of the problem, but the short of it is, nationalism is uglier in asia than it is in europe or the Americas, particularly with some more... imperialist countries. If you fetishize one nation, you alienate others.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's not make generalizations like this, longstanding political and cultural differences or not.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:09:00-07:00","id":1445285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445271#post1445271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right.<br /> <br /> We ARE talking past each other.<br /> <br /> There is literally nowhere that I have called for &quot;de-animification for de-animification's sake.&quot; I've been arguing for &quot;de-animification if the people living there want things de-animificated.&quot; Maybe I'm getting hooked into your disagreement with Damian May there, but that hasn't been my position. Ever.<br /> <br /> MY point is that CTPhipps has provided examples above of fans who DON'T want &quot;Kindred of the East&quot; to be a bunch of kung-fu Orientalism. Whether or not that includes Anime Tropes is beyond my ability to answer, because I'm making a second-hand reference to someone else's conversation. The most likely answer is that there are groups in both camps, and figuring out exactly where the lines will be drawn is going to be hard when part of the fanbase goes off every time you discuss making any kind of meaningful change.<br /> <br /> MY disagreement is with the people arguing that there's no reason to change the original KotE. That does not seem to be your position, so we are not in disagreement as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> PS Yes, Anime is made in Japan. And there is a lot of Asia that is *not* Japan. I have not studied pop culture trends in Asia especially closely, so I don't know if maybe anime is huge everywhere in Asia, but it kind of seems reductive to assume that because anime is Japanese that it will be welcome in World of Darkness content covering *all* of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At least for me, I just care about them being a clearly different supernatural blood drinker, clearly not cainites, and from a totally different mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:23:59-07:00","id":1445289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445285#post1445285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least for me, I just care about them being a clearly different supernatural blood drinker, clearly not cainites, and from a totally different mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely 100% justified.<br /> <br /> Which the obvious answer should be that they should have absolutely no interaction with Cainites whatsoever and that Cainite courts should exist in the East with their own Clans and rules and origin stories. Because, by and large, World of Darkness fans in Asia want to play Vampire: The Masquerade as written. Not be segregated into playing their &quot;separate but equal&quot; mythology.<br /> <br /> Divorced of all the racial context, which is impressive, it would still be told that they had to play Hunter: The Reckoning or Mummy: The Cursed instead of Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Which is what they want to play.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Mind you, Taggie, I think we've run into this before. Is the thing you hate the rules or the fact you utterly hate the Judaeo-Christian origins of vampires? If they ever confirmed Caine didn't exist and was a nondenominational magical ritual in Africa gone wrong, would it change things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:24:27-07:00","id":1445290,"title":"","content":"I wonder if anyone even really read Kindred of the East beside me and few minority others to begin with. The most prevalent themes within KotE has been things from China and India respectively mostly; with more influence stemming from the former. The only real central &quot;point&quot; Japan has had in the forming of the KotE as a line, has obviously been its apparently less liked other name among the fanbase; &quot;Kuei-Jin&quot;, with the &quot;Jin&quot; part atleast being a word within the Japanese language.<br /> <br /> Beyond that and some aesthetic found in how the art was drawn in the various books, most of it wasn't really about &quot;anime&quot; nor did it have such a focus as people are claiming. Ironically Japan on its own in KotE has always been a periphery at best. Everything in it was always like I mentioned before, heavily centered around the framing of China and had more influences from certain tales from Chinese folklore than &quot;anime&quot;; and also like I mentioned again before, India, with a huuuuge amount of core concepts gleaning interesting things from Hinduism (with the Dharma mechanic being the most obvious and important one).<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong however, I won't deny that at some places there were certainly some anime inspirations in the brew too, but that was just some atmospheric cheesiness. So really, if anything is to be tackled about &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;fixing&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; (and I put that in heavy quotations because I feel like nu-Wolf hasn't even done VTM oWoD good so far, and I don't even know they'll revisit Werewolf and in a very distant future, much less Mage), spruce out the weird parts that some find trouble with, but try and keep the game intact for what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:30:39-07:00","id":1445291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445290#post1445290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if anyone even really read Kindred of the East beside me and few minority others to begin with. The most prevalent themes within KotE has been things from China and India respectively mostly; with more influence stemming from the former. The only real central &quot;point&quot; Japan has had in the forming of the KotE as a line, has obviously been its apparently less liked other name among the fanbase; &quot;Kuei-Jin&quot;, with the &quot;Jin&quot; part atleast being a word within the Japanese language.<br /> <br /> Beyond that and some aesthetic found in how the art was drawn in the various books, most of it wasn't really about &quot;anime&quot; nor did it have such a focus as people are claiming. Ironically Japan on its own in KotE has always been a periphery at best. Everything in it was always like I mentioned before, heavily centered around the framing of China and had more influences from certain tales from Chinese folklore than &quot;anime&quot;; and also like I mentioned again before, India, with a huuuuge amount of core concepts gleaning interesting things from Hinduism (with the Dharma mechanic being the most obvious and important one).<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong however, I won't deny that at some places there were certainly some anime inspirations in the brew too, but that was just some atmospheric cheesiness. So really, if anything is to be tackled about &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;fixing&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; (and I put that in heavy quotations because I feel like nu-Wolf hasn't even done VTM oWoD good so far, and I don't even know they'll revisit Werewolf and in a very distant future, much less Mage), spruce out the weird parts that some find trouble with, but try and keep the game intact for what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think of the Kuei Jin (or Wan Kuei as they tried to fix it) as particularly anime. I think they tried to tackle a lot of interesting and complicated moral as well as religious issues.<br /> <br /> However, the heavy focus on the Spirit World while Revised was trying to make it more grounded across its lines contrasted extra-heavily.<br /> <br /> I also believe the &quot;Kuei Jin are Asian people only&quot; was meant with the idea of good intentions. They wanted people to play locals and not American Ninjas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:33:29-07:00","id":1445292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445285#post1445285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least for me, I just care about them being a clearly different supernatural blood drinker, clearly not cainites, and from a totally different mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have absolutely no issue with that in principle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In practice, it becomes a bit more complicated, but by no means impossible. You just need to leave enough room for the presence of Cainites that local players who want to play Cainites a) *can*, and b) don't feel like their local metaplot is being drowned out by the non-Cainites.<br /> <br /> North American audiences don't have a right to tell Asian audiences what their home settings should be like just because they have an attachment to previous canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445291#post1445291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think of the Kuei Jin (or Wan Kuei as they tried to fix it) as particularly anime. I think they tried to tackle a lot of interesting and complicated moral as well as religious issues.<br /> <br /> However, the heavy focus on the Spirit World while Revised was trying to make it more grounded across its lines contrasted extra-heavily.<br /> <br /> I also believe the &quot;Kuei Jin are Asian people only&quot; was meant with the idea of good intentions. They wanted people to play locals and not American Ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this post makes a good point, that people criticizing KotE aren't accusing the authors of bad intentions. But there are reasons coming up now for considering significant changes, regardless of how good the original intentions were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:51:11-07:00","id":1445295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445289#post1445289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Entirely 100% justified.<br /> <br /> Which the obvious answer should be that they should have absolutely no interaction with Cainites whatsoever and that Cainite courts should exist in the East with their own Clans and rules and origin stories. Because, by and large, World of Darkness fans in Asia want to play Vampire: The Masquerade as written. Not be segregated into playing their &quot;separate but equal&quot; mythology.<br /> <br /> Divorced of all the racial context, which is impressive, it would still be told that they had to play Hunter: The Reckoning or Mummy: The Cursed instead of Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Which is what they want to play.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> 2)Mind you, Taggie, I think we've run into this before. Is the thing you hate the rules or the fact you utterly hate the Judaeo-Christian origins of vampires? If they ever confirmed Caine didn't exist and was a nondenominational magical ritual in Africa gone wrong, would it change things?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I would hope for competition at least, but I am not wed to the total genocidal war they had previously, basically them as a 4th, regional sect, strong some places, weak to absent in others.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes probably, or it was something the Wyrm did, basically take it out of human religious focus and make it caused by something in the WoD, (like they are some kinds of Fomori and the Beast is a specific type of Bane) could work for me. I actually didn't have to much of a problem with the Caine myth when it could be regarded as a myth, but Gehenna and DtF drop kicked it to hard in universe fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:59:27-07:00","id":1445296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445295#post1445295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) I would hope for competition at least, but I am not wed to the total genocidal war they had previously, basically them as a 4th, regional sect, strong some places, weak to absent in others.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes probably, or it was something the Wyrm did, basically take it out of human religious focus and make it caused by something in the WoD, (like they are some kinds of Fomori and the Beast is a specific type of Bane) could work for me. I actually didn't have to much of a problem with the Caine myth when it could be regarded as a myth, but Gehenna and DtF drop kicked it to hard in universe fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. That puts things into a better perspective. I think Matthew Dawkins shares the view as in his Inconnu thread he talks about how weird it is for Caine to be taken at face value when Cainites older than Judaism are a fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:13:16-07:00","id":1445324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445296#post1445296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotcha. That puts things into a better perspective. I think Matthew Dawkins shares the view as in his Inconnu thread he talks about how weird it is for Caine to be taken at face value when Cainites older than Judaism are a fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Judaism didn\u2019t just appear out of a vacuum and the Torah was written down from a transmitted oral tradition that pre-dated it by at least centuries (based on structure the oldest section of the Torah is believed to be the wording of the song the Israelites sang after they escaped Egypt - \u201cI will sing to the Lord who is gloriously triumphant. Horse and chariot He has cast into the sea.\u201d).<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Flood story seems to be based on a shared oral tradition related to the 100+ meter rise in global sea levels at the end of the last Ice Age c. 14,000 years ago (not coincidentally this is the same time frame as the supposed destruction of Atlantis and the inundation of the inhabited Dogerland and Sundaland regions).<br /> <br /> The track of humanity in the form of expulsion from the Garden to the east, then Caine\u2019s exile further east yet and a return to the Levant region after the Flood also tracks the migration pattern of early humans out of Africa to the Middle East then to Asia with a post Ice Age migration back west by the ancestors of the present natives in the Levant.<br /> <br /> The point is that the notion that the biblical stories recorded in the Torah didn\u2019t just spring up and though aspects of it are wrapped up in the specific religious interpretations of the time it was written down, there is enough of the early stories that aligns with prehistoric migration patterns to believe that the broadest strokes are actually recounting real history as filtered through oral tradition.<br /> <br /> Thus, while the events involving Cain might not have happened exactly as written in Genesis (the story is being related by those claiming Seth as their ancestor), but it could be a recounting of a prehistoric conflict that drove \u201cCain\u201d (an individual or group associated with farming) out of the region after \u201cAbel\u201d (a subset of the people \u201cAdam\u201d associated with herding) was destroyed and the rise of \u201cSeth\u201d from the people \u201cAdam\u201d to replace those losses.<br /> <br /> In a World of Darkness context this outcast or outcast group could be the first vampire(s) and thus, it makes as much sense as any to call the first of that group \u201cCaine\u201d in the same way we refer to our earliest identified common female ancestor as \u201cMitochondrial Eve.\u201d<br /> <br /> In other words, even if their name wasn\u2019t actually Caine (and they could have been a woman), a term for the First Vampire would be needed to discuss the concept and, at least in Western civilization, that name for them may as well be \u201cCaine.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:15:56-07:00","id":1445325,"title":"","content":"You don't have to convince me. I think in an urban fantasy setting like this that the Creation Mythology of vampires doesn't have to be linked to the history of RL religions. I feel the questions of cultural imperialism is undermined by the fact Caine is a figure in defiance of God and the Book of Nod version is dramatically different from the Biblical.<br /> <br /> Like Gaiman or Netflix's Lucifer being taken for the Catholic one.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Caine Myth&quot; of the Bible being in-universe based on the RL events. For those who feel that it validates one worldview, though, like Taggie then it is not something you can &quot;fix&quot;, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:38:10-07:00","id":1445327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the questions of cultural imperialism is undermined by the fact Caine is a figure in defiance of God and the Book of Nod version is dramatically different from the Biblical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people implicate it as such due to the fact that other regions had nothing to do with Abrahamic fiats or conventions; so to then to shove it and pretend like the group inflicted with the; &quot;Vampires that have been set up to be almost explicitly judeo-christian is the right way, and by that proxy alone all the beliefs of this place has been wrong&quot; is awkward and dumb. This is the samething that happened with D:tF when they pulled the stupid &quot;all Pagan religions are false, actually all ruled by Demon Earthbound (yep, checking that Christian trope dogma boxes) and the religion founded by Lucifer to combat is Christianity! xDDDDD&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Wan Kuei atleast were White Wolf's attempt at something fresh and actually interesting, despite how dodgy some aspects of it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:47:27-07:00","id":1445328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445327#post1445327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some people implicate it as such due to the fact that other regions had nothing to do with Abrahamic fiats or conventions; so to then to shove it and pretend like the group inflicted with the; &quot;Vampires that have been set up to be almost explicitly judeo-christian is the right way, and by that proxy alone all the beliefs of this place has been wrong&quot; is awkward and dumb. This is the samething that happened <b>with D:tF when they pulled the stupid &quot;all Pagan religions are false, actually all ruled by Demon Earthbound </b>(yep, checking that Christian trope dogma boxes) and the religion founded by Lucifer to combat is Christianity! xDDDDD&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Wan Kuei atleast were White Wolf's attempt at something fresh and actually interesting, despite how dodgy some aspects of it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh, the problem with that argument is that Werewolf already seemed to establish the exact opposite and nobody complained then. Werewolf, Mage, and Changeling all seemed to be pagan theologies.<br /> <br /> It also does fall into the weird idea that a game starring demons as the protagonists is Pro-Christian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:11:54-07:00","id":1445334,"title":"","content":"Werewolf was its own theology altogether. Mage was about Consensual reality altogether too, and Changeling was similar to Mage in this regard aswell; humans and/or strong concentrated thought-lulls in general formed reality through collective thought for the most part. Wraith since the get-go was always nebulous in a good way and kept things open. Then by KotE White Wolf was getting together and was making its own original IC cosmology onto itself, taking some elements, but not making real world religions or &quot;one central truth&quot; to the game. Then Hunter: Reckoning came along. It had heavy Christian themes on the surface level, but in the same breadth was heavily connected to KotE through a few major characters in the lore of that game via the Messengers.<br /> <br /> Then D:tF came and sledged all of that like I already discussed in many other threads in the past before. And yes, D:tF is very &quot;pro-Christian&quot;; they literally made certain through Lucifer that Christianity was made by him from the shadows to fight against the Earthbound; who for some reason all have inhabited &quot;key objects&quot; in certain places and certain times, to ostensibly become the puppet-masters of every single non-Abrahamic religion. The D:tF books say that what Lucifer made-up for the books in oWoD-verse Christianity were basically recountings of the Fallens' war against the Host, with a few modifications. So basically from an IC-meta standpoint, Christianity is truest religion in the franchise apparently; because remember, the Fallen were apparently the &quot;creators of the entirety of the oWoD universe&quot;:<br /> <br /> (despite the fact they know nothing of the Fera (ESPECIALLY about knowing nothing of the Mokol\u00e8, the oldest splat that were presumably active during the Triassic Era), haven't heard of any of the ephemeral Umbras (Middle &amp; High Umbrae specifically), they don't know anything about any Mage factions, nothing about knowing the Yama Kings who also apparently worked for god, but were never sent to the &quot;Abyss&quot;, etc.).<br /> <br /> D:tF is an example of what NOT to do when regards to honing only one explicit narrative. Same point carrying over to why its nonsensical to just full implant Cainite vampires wholesale and just retcon out the Wan Kuei, which by itself would hemorrhage a huge amount of oWoD connected cosmology and lore. It's also not as if there ISN'T any Cainite Vampires in Asia to begin with, there is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-22-2021, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:20:20-07:00","id":1445336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445334#post1445334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then D:tF came and sledged all of that like I already discussed in many other threads in the past before. And yes, D:tF is very &quot;pro-Christian&quot;; they literally made certain through Lucifer that Christianity was made by him from the shadows to fight against the Earthbound; who for some reason all have inhabited &quot;key objects&quot; in certain places and certain times, to ostensibly become the puppet-masters of every single non-Abrahamic religion. The D:tF books say that what Lucifer made-up for the books in oWoD-verse Christianity were basically recountings of the Fallens' war against the Host, with a few modifications. So basically from an IC-meta standpoint, Christianity is truest religion in the franchise apparently; because remember, the Fallen were apparently the &quot;creators of the entirety of the oWoD universe&quot;:</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, sometimes I do wonder if we gamers live in their own world because we're discussing the Pro-Christianity message that Christianity was created by Satan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not disputing your post but just noting the irony.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> In my homebrew D:TF games, I flat out ignored that and had the Abrahamic religions created by the &quot;missing&quot; Archangel, Gabriel, with the implications that Jesus was that particular Elohim in human form or his son. I also threw some shade on the whole thing in a crossover game by having a Changeling character argue with a Demon character (both longtime PCs from different Chronicles) that the Demons might well be Changelings themselves. Its just that due to Christianity still have an existing faith that they don't realize that they're products of the Dreaming. It was a fun little AMERICAN GODS-esque conversation. I understand C20 actually DOES have Angel and Demon Kith now too.<br /> <br /> In my current V:TM/W:TA game, I also had a werewolf discover in Mokole mnesis that the Garou created the vampire race with a ritual as a closely guarded secret.<br /> <br /> The vampires just flat out don't believe it.<br /> <br /> For me, the mystery is more important than the answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:28:28-07:00","id":1445338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, sometimes I do wonder if we gamers live in their own world because we're discussing the Pro-Christianity message that Christianity was created by Satan.</div> </div> </div> </div>...........lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:28:30-07:00","id":1445339,"title":"","content":"All I was passing on was that my Indonesian, Polynesian and Indigenous players didn't like the anime aestetic and &quot; chop-sockey&quot; feel and wanted a more folkloric feel to the core. I'm not sure how that became a disagreement with anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:32:23-07:00","id":1445340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445334#post1445334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Hunter: Reckoning came along. It had heavy Christian themes on the surface level, but in the same breadth was heavily connected to KotE through a few major characters in the lore of that game via the Messengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What were the links to KotE in Hunter: The Reckoning? I know when the gameline ended with Time of Judgement they started to explicitly make callouts to KotE with things like Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen (who incidentally were also called out as Angels from DtF cosmology) but I wasn't aware of anything popping up before the final book in the gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:35:56-07:00","id":1445341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445340#post1445340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What were the links to KotE in Hunter: The Reckoning? I know when the gameline ended with Time of Judgement they started to explicitly make callouts to KotE with things like Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen (who incidentally were also called out as Angels from DtF cosmology) but I wasn't aware of anything popping up before the final book in the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there were. It didn't quite go over well because KOTE's reception was controversial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:40:30-07:00","id":1445342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445340#post1445340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What were the links to KotE in Hunter: The Reckoning? I know when the gameline ended with Time of Judgement they started to explicitly make callouts to KotE with things like Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen (who incidentally were also called out as Angels from DtF cosmology) but I wasn't aware of anything popping up before the final book in the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was in one of the Wayward supplements or the one supplement where a central scholar-character (who was kinda, maybe, inspired off of Beckett?) tries to gain a deeper understanding of the condition of the Imbued. Now I have to check the very old threads where we all discussed this a long time ago...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:50:01-07:00","id":1445344,"title":"","content":"I know I've typed this same thing out like 100x now but we are all aware that throughout canon there are thousands of Cainites all throughout South, South-East and East Asia? There have been Cainites in some of those places for thousands of years and in other places for hundreds of years. There is literally nothing preventing anyone from running a stock VtM game in Hong Kong, Taipei, Kuala Lumpur, Kyoto, Ulaanbaatar, Chiang Mai or hundreds of other cities and there never has been.<br /> <br /> The only Caveat added to this is perhaps central mainland China would be very rough ground because its the centre of Quincunx power and some of those Ancestors are whackjobs.<br /> <br /> Hungry Ghosts are going to come into conflict with Cainites because they're both predators on the same flock with similar needs ( for the less advanced HG at least) and because some Blood Magic has a funky effect on the surroundings but theres no reason that conflict has to be anything but political. <br /> <br /> Of course HG will be wary of Cainites as they can grow in population exponentially compared to HGs but they are unlikely to do so as that leads to Masquerade violations so agreements can be made and adhered to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:57:45-07:00","id":1445345,"title":"","content":"What if.... Demon: the Fallen is wrong?<br /> <br /> What if.... all of the core books are wrong?<br /> <br /> It's almost like the entire schtick of the World of Darkness has been &quot;Here are some of our favourite options for plot threads, but go crazy kids.&quot;<br /> <br /> So Demon: the Fallen being set up very pro-Christian doesn't really matter if huge parts of its &quot;canon&quot; are wrong in a World of Darkness setting you create where gamelines other than Demon: the Fallen exist. My personal head-canon basically lets some broad strokes of the Demon canon be true...ish, while also explicitly rebuking some of the most absolute claims of the Abrahamic mythology; they did not create the Universe, it existed well before the Elohim came along. And while plenty of Earthbound might have hijacked plenty of ancient religions, plenty of others were still focused on Umbral entities, vampiric pretenders, Magical Traditions, etc.<br /> <br /> And given how every gameline past Vampire eased off of the Abrahamic narrative significantly, having one last series that featured it heavily again makes a fair amount of sense, book-ends as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:01:25-07:00","id":1445347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445345#post1445345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Demon: the Fallen being set up very pro-Christian doesn't really matter if huge parts of its &quot;canon&quot; are wrong in a World of Darkness setting you create where gamelines other than Demon: the Fallen exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big irony is that its not remotely pro-Christian as the setting basis is God is evil. That's like saying Shin Megami Tensei is pro-Christian.<br /> <br /> However, the objection seems not to be that God is Good or God is Evil, it is that God is real.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:04:54-07:00","id":1445350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445347#post1445347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The big irony is that its not remotely pro-Christian as the setting basis is God is evil. That's like saying Shin Megami Tensei is pro-Christian.<br /> <br /> However, the objection seems not to be that God is Good or God is Evil, it is that God is real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I read the core rulebook once, don't think I finished it. I can't claim to be an expert. But I think it is more complicated than &quot;God is Evil,&quot; and there is something of a pro-Christian slant to the extent that Christianity is presented as having been built up to fight against horrible fiends that seek our enslavement and worship. Again, it's complicated. But I'm more conceding that point while arguing that it still doesn't matter even if you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:08:26-07:00","id":1445351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're both predators on the same flock with similar needs ( for the less advanced HG at least)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Wan Kuei are much more advanced in regards to feeding, considering they can gain sustenance from &quot;stealing&quot; Chi just by inhaling the breaths of mortals by Dharma 4 (correlating to Jina status/rank; which only takes IC in-universe wise 5 years to assume into); and the other fact that by Dharma 6 and above, all they need to is to just then absorb ambient energies only, which more often than not stem from Nodes/Caerns/Freeholds/Dragon Nests. Getting to Dharma 6, which is Mandarin status/rank only takes IC 100 in-universe years. I'd think the competition centering for blood would be far <i>less</i> and more be about sheer political balances as you mention. <br /> <br /> Actually I think the more central conflicts in KotE than worrying about Kindred would be from the Awakened (Mage) and the Fera, since the higher echelons of Wan Kuei power would be more interested in acquiring sources of latent power than Herd scrounging like the Kindred do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:17:37-07:00","id":1445354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445351#post1445351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say the Wan Kuei are much more advanced in regards to feeding, considering they can gain sustenance from &quot;stealing&quot; Chi just by inhaling the breaths of mortals by Dharma 4 (correlating to Jina status/rank; which only takes IC in-universe wise 5 years to assume into); and the other fact that by Dharma 6 and above, all they need to is to just then absorb ambient energies only, which more often than not stem from Nodes/Caerns/Freeholds/Dragon Nests. Getting to Dharma 6, which is Mandarin status/rank only takes IC 100 in-universe years. I'd think the competition centering for blood would be far <i>less</i> and more be about sheer political balances as you mention.<br /> <br /> Actually I think the more central conflicts in KotE than worrying about Kindred would be from the Awakened (Mage) and the Fera, since the higher echelons of Wan Kuei power would be more interested in acquiring sources of latent power than Herd scrounging like the Kindred do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somewhat true, but remember the vast majority of HG that are roaming the streets and likely to accidentally/intentionally run into Cainites are Dharma 2-3. I'd say your correct but the perception may be somewhat skewed by which HG Cainites mostly run into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:25:21-07:00","id":1445355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445350#post1445350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I read the core rulebook once, don't think I finished it. I can't claim to be an expert. But I think it is more complicated than &quot;God is Evil,&quot; and there is something of a pro-Christian slant to the extent that Christianity is presented as having been built up to fight against horrible fiends that seek our enslavement and worship. Again, it's complicated. But I'm more conceding that point while arguing that it still doesn't matter even if you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's just built on a pack of lies by the enemy of the Christian religion. I can't even think of a better example than, &quot;And the Devil actually created the Christian religion. He's also the hero of the setting while God sentenced all of the good guy demons to be driven insane and turned into monsters.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's certainly something that would please neither Christian or atheist in presentation. At least IMHO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:09:58-07:00","id":1445360,"title":"","content":"The conflict in D:tF wasn't about good or bad, it was about ideology; with the crux on how reality was to be managed (again with everything seeming almost copy-by-copy gleaning facets from the IRL Book of Genesis). Lucifer wanted to enlightened humans, while the Abrahamic based God (with the makers of the D:tF OOCly putting in their original own twist by making the Abrahamic God a She, instead of a He) wanted humans to remain as is, for some arcane reason. When the proto-Fallen (Lucifer, his Archdukes, and the rest of the gang) began teaching Adam and Eve, they still were on the &quot;side&quot; of God.<br /> <br /> Even after with Caine doing the apparent &quot;first murder&quot; and that by itself unlocked for the Fallen and the Host to actually begin killing eachother (because pre-Cain murder of Abel, skirmishers were basically just; &quot;So since we fight on 'multiple realities at once' (funny, since like I always trump on about, they can't even parse other Umbrae than the Low one), any strike made, we can see on multiple planes &amp; axises at once. So we can't actually and/or will not hit eachother because we already &quot;precogged&quot;/know who would win the outcome beforehand.&quot; Basically it was cosmic LARP fighting), the Fallen didn't &quot;hate&quot; God or saw her as the &quot;bad&quot;. They ACTUALLY felt that they were in the wrong, since they were directly disobeying it; but still, it's very gray in overall how D:tF was plotted out.<br /> <br /> During the Fallen-Host war, the Fallen did numerous atrocities and the Host did some too. At the end, D:tF's entire story schema was adapting/gafting Book of Genesis in oWoD; with of course putting in the twists typical to how oWoD adapts central story archetypes for the other lines aswell (Vampires, but make them heavily tied to Judeo-Abrahamic mythos; Werewolves, but instead of making them 1 dimensional killers that only changes at a full moon, lets make them 3 dimensional fun killers that wage a cosmic war against an entity that wants to destroy all life; Mage, but instead of going down an all Merlin style route or DnD cheese, lets me a complex central metaphysical game centering around reality change. And let's have the main quasi-antagonists-but-not-really-antagonists(?) of that game be essentially the authoritarian MIB, but for Wizards instead of Ayyliums)<br /> <br /> Lucifer wasn't the hero (because he betrayed everyone, due to it being suggested that he maybe took somesort of back-end deal not to be sent into the Abyss with God) and many Fallen pre-Abyss were horrendous Beings after being unchained to finally go into their darkest desires, after Caine killed Abel to shattered the safeguards they were &quot;metaphysically&quot; bound to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-22-2021, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:15:42-07:00","id":1445364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445347#post1445347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The big irony is that its not remotely pro-Christian as the setting basis is God is evil. That's like saying Shin Megami Tensei is pro-Christian.<br /> <br /> However, the objection seems not to be that God is Good or God is Evil, it is that God is real.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's about it, that the Christian mythos story is real, and therefore the mythos of other splats, as well as other cultures (Indian, African, etc) are all fake, and that this is the basis for the entirety of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Like, Demon: the Fallen is fine on its own, but when it begins to subsume the rest of the World of Darkness into its cosmology, which means that all other cosmologies and religions are wrong, false or fake, that's where the problem is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:16:08-07:00","id":1445365,"title":"","content":"This wasn't in the books but the fiction but Lucifer had no idea why he was locked out of Hell and was portrayed as a John Constantine-esque exorcist and antihero in LUCIFER'S SHADOW and the Trilogy of the Fallen. I always felt that took away a lot of the mystery, making Lucifer a hero. The Demon: The Fallen apocalypse scenario didn't help either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Shadow-Tales-Fallen-Angels/dp/1588468240/ref=sr_1_11?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Demon%3A+The+Fallen+White+Wolf&amp;qid=1619133162&amp;sr=8-11\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Shadow-Tales-Fallen-Angels/dp/1588468240/ref=sr_1_11?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Demon%3A+The+Fallen+White+Wolf&amp;qid=1619133162&amp;sr=8-11\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Shadow-Tales-Fallen-Angels/dp/1588468240/ref=sr_1_11?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Demon%3A+The+Fallen+White+Wolf&amp;qid=1619133162&amp;sr=8-11\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Shadow-Tales-Fallen-Angels/dp/1588468240/ref=sr_1_11?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Demon%3A+The+Fallen+White+Wolf&amp;qid=1619133162&amp;sr=8-11 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:22:55-07:00","id":1445370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445365#post1445365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This wasn't in the books but the fiction but Lucifer had no idea why he was locked out of Hell and was portrayed as a John Constantine-esque exorcist and antihero in LUCIFER'S SHADOW and the Trilogy of the Fallen. I always felt that took away a lot of the mystery, making Lucifer a hero. The Demon: The Fallen apocalypse scenario didn't help either.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Shadow-Tales-Fallen-Angels/dp/1588468240/ref=sr_1_11?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Demon%3A+The+Fallen+White+Wolf&amp;qid=1619133162&amp;sr=8-11\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Shad...133162&amp;sr=8-11</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh. I didn't even know these books existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:17:02-07:00","id":1445381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445235#post1445235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shouldn't objectively supernatural creatures have a written religion?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason I compare the book of Nod to the book of Mormon and not say the book of Enoch or the book of Jubilees. Its... clearly not written by someone who has done research to make it even look like its particularly old. But I accept it and stories of the first and second city as somewhat based on something that actually happened even though it makes no sense.<br /> <br /> Though I always liked the Ancient aliens interpretation I[ve seen on fanfic sites... it would explain some of the anachronistically high level of social development needed for the first and second city and why a flood was needed..<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445271#post1445271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right.<br /> <br /> We ARE talking past each other.<br /> <br /> There is literally nowhere that I have called for &quot;de-animification for de-animification's sake.&quot; I've been arguing for &quot;de-animification if the people living there want things de-animificated.&quot; Maybe I'm getting hooked into your disagreement with Damian May there, but that hasn't been my position. Ever.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am laying out my point. You are the one responding to something that is not there. I've laid out my opinions. We need local voices. We should use the very good and developed gaming culture of the local area. I haven't even been saying we should use anime tropes for every damned asian vampire concept. I have entirely been saying &quot;We should do this with Just Japan&quot; because.. Asia is bigger and more diverse than every place else? I have been specifically narrow focused on one culture. The culture I know the most about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445277#post1445277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*most Japanese anime seems to be animated by Korean studios these days.<br /> <br /> But, eh, yeah nah let's not make rulebooks in accordance to 'anime'. First off, Otakus are shunned in Japan; Anime isn't as mainstream as you think it is. Nor is tabletop gaming of course, but I'd like to pretend we're cool kids, not a bunch of weaboos who put japan ahead of the rest of asia because we like the cartoons they started pouring out post wwII so you'd think they were a harmless nation who'd never done anything wrong.<br /> Just be try to be neutral. Nothing's wrong with neutral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most table top rpers and even more extremly larpers are shunned in the US we shouldn't use them as writers for future vampire games. Sounds reasonable.. no wait..<br /> <br /> The nerd culture interconnectedness is a thing in Japan. They have a tabletop industry. They make interesting things. They should be the people who are courted for a Japanese focused game about vampires. People trying to to remove &quot;Weebness&quot; are being silly.<br /> <br /> We also maybe should use.. I don't know.. different people to write about China than Japan rather htan trying to develop some sort of &quot;Neutral&quot; Look at Asia. China has more people and more land than all of Europe. It could easily support a creature type by itself before we get to Korea, Myanmar, Japan. etc. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:51:37-07:00","id":1445389,"title":"","content":"Thing is simply that myths, mythology and all that is mystic should follow the same rule: be kept that way. If a myth is proven or some opposing be proven instead, than it is no longer myth, and all that aura and profundity is lost. That is sort of why I pretty much dislike WtA myth, because it's so driven as &quot;complete unadulterated truth&quot; in text and mechanics so many times. Vampire makes its own myths always come in question, even if its only a misunderstanding of it. At least from all i've read, and from what I interpret. The Wan Kuei seem also too much engulfed and made from their own (for some reason) homogenous myth, in a way that its very difficult to have a different or unique interpretation, from what the texts says, it's all real, so it can't be myth. Of course, a bad tendency that was had here is to make Asia always more mystic and mythical than the rest of the world even in modern times, if not for some other weird reason than to make it more exotic and different. <br /> The world of darkness legends and myths should remain as such, even when one speck of it is shown it should still remain unconfirmed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T18:25:31-07:00","id":1445390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445381#post1445381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am laying out my point. You are the one responding to something that is not there. I've laid out my opinions. We need local voices. We should use the very good and developed gaming culture of the local area. I haven't even been saying we should use anime tropes for every damned asian vampire concept. I have entirely been saying &quot;We should do this with Just Japan&quot; because.. Asia is bigger and more diverse than every place else? I have been specifically narrow focused on one culture. The culture I know the most about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, apologies for misunderstanding you. I kept getting quoted, so my assumption was that there was something you agreed or disagreed with that merited response.<br /> <br /> To stick on the point that you are laying out: if I remember the posts above correctly, finding local writers is somewhat difficult. I believe that CTPhipps has mentioned that many local writers would rather not touch Kindred of the East with a ten-foot-pole, because they can't change the product in ways that they would be satisfied with that would not outrage a large portion of the KotE fanbase. Meanwhile, I think the sources that Damian May cited were by local authors, but I must admit I haven't checked those out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T19:10:55-07:00","id":1445395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445390#post1445390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, apologies for misunderstanding you. I kept getting quoted, so my assumption was that there was something you agreed or disagreed with that merited response.<br /> <br /> To stick on the point that you are laying out: if I remember the posts above correctly, finding local writers is somewhat difficult. I believe that CTPhipps has mentioned that many local writers would rather not touch Kindred of the East with a ten-foot-pole, because they can't change the product in ways that they would be satisfied with that would not outrage a large portion of the KotE fanbase. Meanwhile, I think the sources that Damian May cited were by local authors, but I must admit I haven't checked those out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the big issues seem to be the fact that the Kuei-Jin CAN be fixed but if its fixed, it won't necessarily be recognizable as the same product.<br /> <br /> If you want to do a modern street level Asian vampire game without a big focus on the Spirit World or Daoist mythology, well, that's not the Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> They are very much kung-fu demon fighters powered by their religious enlightenment.<br /> <br /> It's not like trying to adjust VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE, its more like trying to adjust IN NOMINE.<br /> <br /> A lot of the objections are for the same reason people don't like Christian mythology in their games, despite it being &quot;local&quot; for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:13:28-07:00","id":1445403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is sort of why I pretty much dislike WtA myth, because it's so driven as &quot;complete unadulterated truth&quot; in text and mechanics so many times.</div> </div> </div> </div>WtA had a staunch mythos within itself, but it's mythos wasn't an unadulterated single truth at all. What was found in the line had pieces to many other things, while alone at times questioned things the Garou categorically though was &quot;<i>right</i>&quot;, but was actually systemically was wrong due to how they dealt with things in the past (and the reason why the Wyrm has been chipping away at them; and the roundabount away they chipped at the collective effort of fighting the Wyrm too, by being the primary initiators of the War of Rage against the other Fera).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire makes its own myths always come in question, even if its only a misunderstanding of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it barely ever does. Numerous supplements and since 1st edition core in VTM have all but confirmed that Caine has been the first Vampire, despite main claims that VTM has &quot;kept it nebulous&quot;. It hasn't for the most part. The only time it has questioned itself at a great length, from my moderate memory alone; was with the Lasombra clanbook; the Followers of Set on its own entirely (but lets be real, Set's sire and grandsire before were descended from Caine); and some other miscellaneous tidbits. Overall it is Caine though as the central confirmed myth. They admittedly have, in the past, tried to make an &quot;alternate Caine&quot;-figure with the Laibon with the whole &quot;Cagn&quot; thing... yeah, doesn't really work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wan Kuei seem also too much engulfed and made from their own <b>(for some reason)</b> homogenous myth,</div> </div> </div> </div>Because at that point as I observed from reading KotE, White Wolf took full hospice to finally settle into its own tailor-made original cosmology, lore, myth, meta, etc. With that reasoning, KotE was unique in that it WASN'T a &quot;homogeneous&quot; myth whatsoever. If you read KotE, you'd see very often they make clear connections to other plot-points or lore from other games, but not in a way where its damaging or overarches another gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:21:20-07:00","id":1445404,"title":"","content":"I suspect a lot of fans would love for Ancient Greek equivalents of the Book of Nod with Kronos being the first Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:33:26-07:00","id":1445405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445403#post1445403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtA had a staunch mythos within itself, but it's mythos wasn't an unadulterated single truth at all. What was found in the line had pieces to many other things, while alone at times questioned things the Garou categorically though was &quot;<i>right</i>&quot;, but was actually systemically was wrong due to how they dealt with things in the past (and the reason why the Wyrm has been chipping away at them; and the roundabount away they chipped at the collective effort of fighting the Wyrm too, by being the primary initiators of the War of Rage against the other Fera).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be more accurate to say that the Garou were wrong, but what they believed in largely was not. Being chosen as Gaia's warriors to take down corruption? True. Being above the Fera and given license to kill them? So utterly fucking wrong that it helped wreck the world. Gaia above the Triat? Generally supported by the books in most cases except for a very few, generally being comparable to the Caine treatment that you outlined.<br /> <br /> (Note: Fera is the Garou word for werecreatures that aren't them. They do not number among the Fera, and are not &quot;other Fera&quot;.) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, it barely ever does. Numerous supplements and since 1st edition core in VTM have all but confirmed that Caine has been the first Vampire, despite main claims that VTM has &quot;kept it nebulous&quot;. It hasn't for the most part. The only time it has questioned itself at a great length, from my moderate memory alone; was with the Lasombra clanbook; the Followers of Set on its own entirely (but lets be real, Set's sire and grandsire before were descended from Caine); and some other miscellaneous tidbits. Overall it is Caine though as the central confirmed myth. They admittedly have, in the past, tried to make an &quot;alternate Caine&quot;-figure with the Laibon with the whole &quot;Cagn&quot; thing... yeah, doesn't really work. </div> </div> </div>Well, it hasn't yet. There could be something that sticks, so long as the ultimate direction of the line doesn't stop trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because at that point as I observed from reading KotE, White Wolf took full hospice to finally settle into its own tailor-made original cosmology, lore, myth, meta, etc. With that reasoning, KotE was unique in that it WASN'T a &quot;homogeneous&quot; myth whatsoever. If you read KotE, you'd see very often they make clear connections to other plot-points or lore from other games, but not in a way where its damaging or overarches another gameline. </div> </div> </div>I'd consider its attempts to &quot;sync&quot; with Werewolf fairly damaging; Blood and Silk stands out as a particular stinker where the changers are concerned. There was also the presentation of their spiritual patrons as some variety of Celestial Bureaucracy (only with Gaia and Luna at the top instead of a Heavenly Emperor), which Changers are, on the whole, rather unsuited for in affiliation and mood, as it would lead straight into exactly the sort of issue that Banu_Saulot mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:40:11-07:00","id":1445407,"title":"","content":"If we went back to the Drawing Board, I would have delinked the Kuei Jin from the Spirit World to begin with and instead made them linked to Wraith: The Oblivion instead.<br /> <br /> It makes a great deal more sense and would have left them with a darker more ambiguous tone.<br /> <br /> As much as giving the Yama Kings as a threat an obvious enemy, it might have been interesting to just have them rise from the dead for no understandable reason and deal with the search for meaning this entails.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:58:09-07:00","id":1445410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood and Silk stands out as a particular stinker where the changers are concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never read Blood and Silk before. Can you explain what was done wrong in there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also the presentation of their spiritual patrons as some variety of Celestial Bureaucracy</div> </div> </div> </div>This by itself doesn't really step on any toes much or hard at all and really was just left out there. And the with the how Garou and the others interact with Spirits, and how bureaucratic-esque Spirits are (all the chiminages that need to done, keeping the pacts right, the local Caern Spirit has to be the one to accept cubs, etc.); its not hard to see the tenuality in that. But again, atleast some linkage, but not a very damaging one was made there. The Celestial Bureaucracy as per accounts from the Hsien and Wan Kuei attest that such an institution had existed, but depleted as soon as the August Personage of Jade mysteriously disappeared. So its really just a low-level hanging question on what specific Spirits were actually functionaries in the Celestial Bureaucracy when it was active, not some far-reaching generalized &quot;variety&quot; as to mean ALL of them were in on it.<br /> <br /> This can be contrasted with D:tF (a line that like KotE tried to &quot;sync&quot; things, but did it horribly) that didn't even bother to mention anything of Gaia or the Triat, much less Spirits at all. They of course only mentioned Wraiths, but Wraiths are entropic entoplasmia; while Spirits are more estoric living ephemera (and I make this distinction in the first place to show the silliness of it. How can beings of intrinsic creation cannot or has no recognition of the Spirit World, but only the part of entropic Underworld? Wut?). And Wraiths even when presented in D:tF were mere backdrops and with no importance, and no real interaction; and the interactions that did happen really fibbed with Wraith in a bad way. The irony isn't lost on me either, that one line being ignored is damaging in D:tF since heavily deals with creation, but no mention of W:tA anywhere (basically invalidating the Triat and Gaia in relation to oWoD); but one line getting piecemeal undetailed attention also made some awkward fibs aswell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as giving the Yama Kings as a threat an obvious enemy, it might have been interesting to just have them rise from the dead for no understandable reason and deal with the search for meaning this entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing interesting in that. KotE's main theme is about people who had done some karmic bads in their living life, must now atone for it in undeath after facing the worst sufferings of their existence in the 1000 Hells. From the get-go it already has a &quot;dark tone&quot;. And decoupling them from the Middle-Umbra is ludicrous given the entire backdrop of the lore surrounding it. The Wan Kuei KNOW what they need todo with their unlife, but the actual road to achieve it seems arduously impossible; like climbing a never ending tower you try to scale from the outside. Some fall, while others clamber on. Erasing their ultimate causation for rising just to raise... just shows the lack of understanding toward KotE.<br /> <br /> Not even the Risen from Wraith: The Oblivion rise for no reason; which pinpoints some minor, but understandable ignorance toward W:TO (which isn't surprising, considering how a miniscule amount of have actually read it) aswell. Every single Risen raises for a reason, even trying is extremely hazardous internally due how powered the Shadow can become. It's an ultimate gambit struggle to balance trying not to succumb to the Shadow, not tow the line or get caught by the Hierarchy, and trying to resolve *why* you raised in the first place.<br /> <br /> And the Wan Kuei are connected to the Low Umbra through Yin aspected Wan Kuei specifically. And the same breadth aswell, more Yang aspected Wan Kuei are more connected with the Spirit World. That's the beauty of KotE, with how dynamic it can be to traverse cosmologies.. stagnating it down to only one piece is nonsensical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-23-2021, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:00:16-07:00","id":1445411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445407#post1445407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we went back to the Drawing Board, I would have delinked the Kuei Jin from the Spirit World to begin with and instead made them linked to Wraith: The Oblivion instead.<br /> <br /> It makes a great deal more sense and would have left them with a darker more ambiguous tone.<br /> <br /> As much as giving the Yama Kings as a threat an obvious enemy, it might have been interesting to just have them rise from the dead for no understandable reason and deal with the search for meaning this entails.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IF we are going back to the drawing board I'd probably also change lots of aspects of wraith too.. Like legitimately tie the whole far shores to the High umbra and more readily make the cycle of Ghost to Spirit a thing. The many paths out functioning a bit like Dharmas currently and then you could just combine risen and Wan Kuei.... the fact that Transcendence is the only &quot;Option&quot; for wraith undercuts alot of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:01:06-07:00","id":1445414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445411#post1445411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF we are going back to the drawing board I'd probably also change lots of aspects of wraith too.. Like legitimately tie the whole far shores to the High umbra and more readily make the cycle of Ghost to Spirit a thing. The many paths out functioning a bit like Dharmas currently and then you could just combine risen and Wan Kuei.... the fact that Transcendence is the only &quot;Option&quot; for wraith undercuts alot of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>How ironic our suggestions end up canceling each other out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:30:23-07:00","id":1445418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445414#post1445414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How ironic our suggestions end up canceling each other out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It annoys me that there are all these &quot;OBVIOUSLY FAKE&quot; heavens and hells(asside from the Yomi) I'd rather a greater level of ambiguity. That Transcendence is the only ending for a Wraith rather than say &quot;become a god&quot; in the umbra bothers me.. the only way you can get there is by going through a Wan Kuei &quot;heresy&quot;. One of the major defining works of Japanese Urban fantasy/Horror involved a series of novels dealt with in part the transition of &quot;ghost&quot; into a the god of Tokyo.<br /> <br /> That you can't even do that with standard Wan Kuei was something I never liked. The transition from venerated ancestor to divinity is a pretty common universe concept.. and yet its impossible. Its probably something I'd incorporate if I rebuilt wraith a bunch of &quot;Wraith becomes an...&quot; options. Risen/Wk would be one option. Kermet another and so on. There would just be more options and plenty of heavens and hells to visit.. are there a bunch of mages calling them parts of the &quot;High umbra&quot; absolutely... are they right? That I would make ambiguous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:31:49-07:00","id":1445419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the fact that Transcendence is the only &quot;Option&quot; for wraith undercuts alot of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trascendence was far from the only &quot;&quot;option&quot;&quot; that could be done with Wraith. In Wraith you could just merely want to stay as Wraith as much as you want, just trying to survive. You could become part of the Hierarchy full on, instead of nominally, and try to rise through the ranks of it. You could also try to be an opposition toward it and make your unlife about fighting it, while competing against or allying with other Renegades. You could join one of the various &quot;Heretic&quot; Cults, gaining in on the intrigues of influencing society from the shadows and likewise fighting against other Cults that don't share your specific line of dogma. You could become a Warlord in the Underworld, cruising along the Tempest to raid other Isles. You could be someone who specifically hunts down Spectres, a Doomslayer. You could focus solely on increasing your signature and favored Arcanoi, to then maybe go on and join one of the Guilds. The possibilities are endless.<br /> <br /> Or you could as referenced, attempt Transcendence. All Transcendence is however, is basically Golconda, but with actual workable mechanics unlike what went on with VTM. It's not even meant to be as defined however once you actually reach it, that's up to the players and ST playing it generally; Wraith never was supposed to give you certain answers about Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Hell, you could forgo all notions of Transcendence to begin with and become a Spectre; be a full being of malignant entropy, violence, dreariness, and darkness. And with how W:tO mechanics worked (and has actually rules for), you could even redeem yourself out of being a Spectre entirely (but with a permanent unremovable scarification to alert that you were once a Spectre. You'll be hated by both ends of the Spectrum, Wraith or Spectre, after that). The type of stuff you can do with Wraith is huge, and not just about Transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-23-2021, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:35:23-07:00","id":1445420,"title":"","content":"Random Aside:<br /> <br /> I had Cappadocias become THE GRIM REAPER and ruler of this Far Shore.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Paradise_of_the_Fishers\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pa...of_the_Fishers</a><br /> <br /> He could take over the entirety of the Underworld if he wanted to but feels no need as the Dark Lord. He thinks he successfully diablerized God after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:47:47-07:00","id":1445423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445418#post1445418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It annoys me that there are all these &quot;OBVIOUSLY FAKE&quot; heavens and hells(asside from the Yomi) I'd rather a greater level of ambiguity. That Transcendence is the only ending for a Wraith rather than say &quot;become a god&quot; in the umbra bothers me.. the only way you can get there is by going through a Wan Kuei &quot;heresy&quot;. One of the major defining works of Japanese Urban fantasy/Horror involved a series of novels dealt with in part the transition of &quot;ghost&quot; into a the god of Tokyo.<br /> <br /> That you can't even do that with standard Wan Kuei was something I never liked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Simply have the Hungry Ghost enter the Middle Umbra and remain there for long enough to become a spirit it doesn't happen as quickly as it does for a normal human but Hungry Ghosts like Changing Breeds will become pure spirit if they spend long enough in the spirit world. Its not as direct a path as following the teachings of the Celestial Tribe becuse you will need to climb the spiritual ladder the long way, but it can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T22:00:21-07:00","id":1445427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445419#post1445419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trascendence was far from the only &quot;&quot;option&quot;&quot; that could be done with Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>IN the long term there is, Trancend or Oblivion. There are a lot of really good interesting plots to be had in the Shadowlands, in Stygia. I would just like to give some legitimacy to The Far shores. Some weight if you would. There is a profound missed opportunity by having every heaven and hell objectively fake except the Yomi which is real and for Asians in Asia only. They are the only demons who don't come off as chumps since they objectively get souls.. for something.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T22:10:25-07:00","id":1445428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445423#post1445423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? Simply have the Hungry Ghost enter the Middle Umbra and remain there for long enough to become a spirit it doesn't happen as quickly as it does for a normal human but Hungry Ghosts like Changing Breeds will become pure spirit if they spend long enough in the spirit world. Its not as direct a path as following the teachings of the Celestial Tribe becuse you will need to climb the spiritual ladder the long way, but it can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 the most obvious way to get there explicitly say that doesn't work.(Yang prana says you can spend infinite time in that state..)<br /> <br /> 2. Given it is litterally never brought up while there are descriptions of how Thousand whispers might spend hundreds of years trawling the spirit world.. there is more argument this isn't an option.<br /> <br /> 3. Given that The transition from Goryo to kami is pretty major concept it probably should have explicit mechanical support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T22:32:16-07:00","id":1445430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a profound missed opportunity by having every heaven and hell objectively fake</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the point, in Wraith there is no abject &quot;heaven or hell&quot;. That was not the goal of the gameline at all; it had a deep theme of existential nihilism, where it didn't absconded to one particular one view of a &quot;heaven or hell&quot;. All that was viewed and known was that everything in the Low Umbra was dead and you had to deal with that, or get so caught up in being overwhelmed you perished to be destroyed forever. No opportunity was really missed there, it executed its thematic beautifully. <br /> <br /> And to remark on the &quot;fakeness&quot; of the &quot;Heaven&quot; and &quot;Hells&quot;, such-called places at some specific Isles in the Far Shores region; calling them &quot;objectively&quot; fake is surely a subjective-relativity. The Wraiths that find themselves in a Heaven definitely feel that are in as such and fully believe their afterlife has found a homing point. It's very real for those specific Wraiths that it's a paradise for them. The Wraiths that find or were forced in common cases a Hell definitely more than anything feel they've reached a point of horrific damnation of a sort. It's a VERY real experience of pure bleakness for those Wraiths. So the Heavens and Hells are whether are not they're fake is subjective, but not a resolute notion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are the only demons who don't come off as chumps since they objectively get souls.. for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are aware that major part of Wraith's grimdark reputation is that literally almost all the commodities and resources in the game are other Wraiths, right? Where they're literally and horrifically soulforged down for usability? Its not even known if soulforged Wraiths-turned-objects don't fully lose sentience; that maybe (and has been clued-in/teased multiple times before) they're fully aware still and are stuck like that for eternity. Imagine you were soulforged to become a golf ball for the elites of Stygia; only to then get made, but fall out of the wagon during transport on the streets of Stygia. You roll into a alley at a nook that'll almost certainly be never checked at. Now you're stuck for eternity in a random spot unable to see anymore, speak, or even move at all....<br /> <br /> Nothing about how souls were done in Wraith were chumpy at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T22:53:09-07:00","id":1445433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445428#post1445428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 the most obvious way to get there explicitly say that doesn't work.(Yang prana says you can spend infinite time in that state..)<br /> <br /> 2. Given it is litterally never brought up while there are descriptions of how Thousand whispers might spend hundreds of years trawling the spirit world.. there is more argument this isn't an option.<br /> <br /> 3. Given that The transition from Goryo to kami is pretty major concept it probably should have explicit mechanical support.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, I always read Yang prana as specifically protecting the HG against the change to spirit allowing them to remain HG despite prolonged time in the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> It does seem strange to me that of all the supernatural beings in the WoD HGs would be specifically protected against the change but we have been playing fairly focused chronicles so its been a while since I've read widely on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T23:35:43-07:00","id":1445437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445403#post1445403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtA had a staunch mythos within itself, but it's mythos wasn't an unadulterated single truth at all. What was found in the line had pieces to many other things, while alone at times questioned things the Garou categorically though was &quot;<i>right</i>&quot;, but was actually systemically was wrong due to how they dealt with things in the past (and the reason why the Wyrm has been chipping away at them; and the roundabount away they chipped at the collective effort of fighting the Wyrm too, by being the primary initiators of the War of Rage against the other Fera).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Garou are absolutely positive that they're right, and their books reflect that. But then you go and look through the Mokole book, or the Ananasi book, or the book on the Emerald Courts and it quickly becomes apparent that the Garou don't know nearly as much as they think they do (none of the shifters do) and the Garou are largely responsible for many of the problems that they're facing today. And to be fair, some of the tribes acknowledge their failings and their limited knowledge and spend time trying to get in contact with the Fera to learn more and to do what they can to make up for their past mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T23:42:54-07:00","id":1445439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445418#post1445418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you can't even do that with standard Wan Kuei was something I never liked. The transition from venerated ancestor to divinity is a pretty common universe concept.. and yet its impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't there an entire wan kuei dharma devoted to becoming a god? I think though that it never really god mechanics, just as many &quot;ascensions&quot; for various splats in the WoD rarely, or barely, got mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T00:14:30-07:00","id":1445442,"title":"","content":"To be honest, when I was starting to get into World of Darkness proper after Vampire (which is pretty gritty streets and bloody alleyways, keeping away from worldwide schemes, magic, other worlds and etc. if one wants it) I was very much confused about Umbra and all it's depths and &quot;vertical&quot; layers (high, medium, low), and I'm still kind of am, especially when its about transitioning between each of them and the visual of each. But something else that made me scratch ma' brain was the fact that there is spirits and things that could be called souls of dead things, that exist or go to the &quot;Spiritual&quot; Umbra while there is a Underworld. It all mostly came from the breaming Werewolf that made it seem like millions of worlds that are and could be, with no limits and very different rules and depths for each. So when I got that Underworld (Low Umbra) is the place where dead mortals go thing got a bit clearer, putting the rest of the medium Umbra and high one aside (considering it was hard to separate Dreaming from the high umbra), things got a bit clearer. <br /> It got complicated when family spirits and things like that seemed more spiritual than wraithly, and I still think Wraiths should be able to become hosts (groupings) of guardian spirits of some sort, even if it means to slumber most of the time, serve a family, group, or something else for centuries, and not be much of Playable mode of character. And if they can, which I assume there is some way, then okay, but I haven't seen it shown clearly. I'm not talking about ghosts helping their loved ones and such, cuz thats simply Wraith the Oblivion as it is.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I kind of think Wan Kuei should be more Wraith than Werewolf, at least base/vanilla, or cosmologically. Although for them to have ample access to spiritual powers and magic should be considered novelty or strange by other supernatural races. Maybe their whole fall from Wan Xian to Wan Kuei would make them less spirit and more wraith. I don't mind not knowing why they are a different (although not ruling or homogenous) supernatural being from either wraiths or vampires, it could be an ancient Spell like the Mummy games for all I care. And I don't think it should be purely Asian either, even if its only mentioning occurrences elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to know more about this Cappadocius idea CTPhipps, if there is more to tell.<br /> <br /> At last, I think it got already out of discussion, but when it comes to Demon the Fallen, I always interpreted - by all the accounts of the de demons saying that the world used to be every truth being real at the same time - that each demon that would wake in different part of the world would have it deeply marked in them exactly the myths of demons and devils from that culture (remember that they would feel, eat and torment some souls that would pass through their hell, so there was some contact, even if mostly blind). So much so that they would think that's their identity, and they would shape their story from that, with Torment breaking that illusion until de demon forgot everything and was nothing more than anger and frustration. So it wasn't just the memories from the mortal host that they take that are &quot;not theirs&quot;, but the whole &quot;I'm an elohim that fought alongside Lucifer&quot; too is a construct. <br /> Well, thats a big freaking headcanon if you can still call it that, but it makes it possible for the setting to be plural and devils to be even more mysterious; like they are eidolons of the demons their hosting cultures, forgetful of what they really are in fact (which may be unknowable).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T00:32:54-07:00","id":1445443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445439#post1445439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't there an entire wan kuei dharma devoted to becoming a god? I think though that it never really god mechanics, just as many &quot;ascensions&quot; for various splats in the WoD rarely, or barely, got mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it's the Faces Of The Gods dharma. to be honest, I actually like the Heretical Dharmas more than the Orthodox ones since I feel that their writing is better, although they need to be revised as well since &quot;if it isn't from Arhat Xue, it's wrong&quot; kind of stuff and forced demonization<br /> <br /> some of the members of those dharmas will likely even work with kindred. like a Rising Phoenix and Golconda seeker wanting to be human again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T00:50:54-07:00","id":1445445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445443#post1445443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> it's the Faces Of The Gods dharma. to be honest, I actually like the Heretical Dharmas more than the Orthodox ones since I feel that their writing is better, although they need to be revised as well since &quot;if it isn't from Arhat Xue, it's wrong&quot; kind of stuff and forced demonization<br /> <br /> some of the members of those dharmas will likely even work with kindred. like a Rising Phoenix and Golconda seeker wanting to be human again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, Faces of the Gods ( previously Celestial Tribe ) and Spirit of Living Earth derivatives get most of the play in my SE Asia/Oceania games, closely followed by local variants of the Bone Flowers and Thrashing Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T00:52:43-07:00","id":1445446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445442#post1445442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wanted to know more about this Cappadocius idea CTPhipps, if there is more to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The idea was that Cappadocias just becoming another mad Specter that was deranged about being God, he actually had at least some small inkling of the truth of the cosmos. In this case, Cappadocias devoured a being that he assumed to be God and merged with it that gave him unimaginable powers regarding the Underworld as well as molding it to his wishes. WHAT he devoured, be it Neverborn or Demon Lord or Yama King or just a powerful wraith.<br /> <br /> 2. Cappadocias proceeded to mold a giant chunk of the afterlife into a New Garden of Eden where he lured massive numbers of souls to live in a paradise of his own devising. He also molded Specters into his servants and &quot;angels&quot; that obeyed him. Unfortunately, being an Antediluvian means that his morality was warped and he also created a version of Hell and Puragtory that equally punished the &quot;unworthy&quot; with as much arbitrary capriciousness as God as always been accused of.<br /> <br /> 3. Cappadocias is also denied what he truly wanted as the ritual has left him permanently in the image of a ghastly skeleton with black wings and robes. Cappadocias perhaps knows that he is not God and instead has decided that he is the avatar of Death instead. He thus still continues to seek a way to find out where God is and overthrow him. The fact he rules &quot;Heaven&quot; and yet plots this from &quot;Hell&quot; is double think that he holds simultaneously.<br /> <br /> 4. Augustus Giovanni bringing down the Shroud may actually have been inspired by &quot;Death&quot; as it would have definitely benefited the Antediluvian to be ruler of both Heaven and Earth.<br /> <br /> 5. I was inspired for this by Death in Castlevania and the idea certain Kindred have been advised by this spirit since 1666.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","