er Weaver) to control humanity and created misogyny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love using the Patriach in my games, but then I have a few players who are Ex-JW and Ex-Mormon so they could relate to that take a lot better.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T16:34:54-07:00","id":1445570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445569#post1445569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love using the Patriach in my games, but then I have a few players who are Ex-JW and Ex-Mormon so they could relate to that take a lot better.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>good for you. Glad someone got something out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:58:52-07:00","id":1445587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445410#post1445410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never read Blood and Silk before. Can you explain what was done wrong in there?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the battle between Huangdi and Chiyou? It was recast as corrupt Wan Xian versus the Beast Courts, respectively. And for some reason, Chiyou, who is associated with the appearance of a metallic bull, was cast as a Hakken werewolf. Hakken, who as you might know, are from Japan and wouldn't likely have called themselves Hakken then for a variety of reasons (such as nebulous formation of Confucian-identified virtues thousands of years before they would have been codified, and the likelihood that tribes proper might not have split off by then). Heaven intercedes, the Wan Xian get smacked into being Wan Gui, but because the Changers did a bad thing in heavenly authority's eyes by attacking the Wan Xian, Chiyou has to accept imprisonment in hell along with the souls that now become Wan Gui.<br /> <br /> Note that most traditions place that confrontation as far closer to the present than the fall of the Wan Xian in the WoD, by roughly thousands of years. Also, it kind of seems like it's insulting everyone and everything in how it was handled. To top that off, the book undoes the diversity of Garou tribes found in the Beast Courts; Hengeyokai, for all its faults, included the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, and CoGs in addition to the Stargazers and Hakken. Blood and Silk pared that down, reinforcing the stereotype of the Stargazers as &quot;The Asian Tribe&quot;, which is somehow the least populous in spite of being from some of the most populous regions on Earth. And W20 didn't change much of this in Shattered Dreams, otherwise a choice place for addressing this issue (such as by making Chiyou into an Apis, at the very least).<br /> <br /> When we add the atrocious botch that was its attempt to inform readers of various styles of Chinese Romanization, you get a book that needed some substantial rewrites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This by itself doesn't really step on any toes much or hard at all and really was just left out there. And the with the how Garou and the others interact with Spirits, and how bureaucratic-esque Spirits are (all the chiminages that need to done, keeping the pacts right, the local Caern Spirit has to be the one to accept cubs, etc.); its not hard to see the tenuality in that. But again, atleast some linkage, but not a very damaging one was made there. The Celestial Bureaucracy as per accounts from the Hsien and Wan Kuei attest that such an institution had existed, but depleted as soon as the August Personage of Jade mysteriously disappeared. So its really just a low-level hanging question on what specific Spirits were actually functionaries in the Celestial Bureaucracy when it was active, not some far-reaching generalized &quot;variety&quot; as to mean ALL of them were in on it.<br /> <br /> This can be contrasted with D:tF (a line that like KotE tried to &quot;sync&quot; things, but did it horribly) that didn't even bother to mention anything of Gaia or the Triat, much less Spirits at all. They of course only mentioned Wraiths, but Wraiths are entropic entoplasmia; while Spirits are more estoric living ephemera (and I make this distinction in the first place to show the silliness of it. How can beings of intrinsic creation cannot or has no recognition of the Spirit World, but only the part of entropic Underworld? Wut?). And Wraiths even when presented in D:tF were mere backdrops and with no importance, and no real interaction; and the interactions that did happen really fibbed with Wraith in a bad way. The irony isn't lost on me either, that one line being ignored is damaging in D:tF since heavily deals with creation, but no mention of W:tA anywhere (basically invalidating the Triat and Gaia in relation to oWoD); but one line getting piecemeal undetailed attention also made some awkward fibs aswell. </div> </div> </div>Getting something from a spirit requires chiminage, but if it were an agency like a Spiritual Bureaucracy, there would be petitions required instead, and the chiminage would be an illegal bribe instead of a recognized and official part of the process. A number of spirits are also part of larger spirits. Basically, there's a place for that structure, but it's something that would characterize the Astral Umbra way more than the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's nothing interesting in that. KotE's main theme is about people who had done some karmic bads in their living life, must now atone for it in undeath after facing the worst sufferings of their existence in the 1000 Hells. From the get-go it already has a &quot;dark tone&quot;. And decoupling them from the Middle-Umbra is ludicrous given the entire backdrop of the lore surrounding it. The Wan Kuei KNOW what they need todo with their unlife, but the actual road to achieve it seems arduously impossible; like climbing a never ending tower you try to scale from the outside. Some fall, while others clamber on. Erasing their ultimate causation for rising just to raise... just shows the lack of understanding toward KotE.<br /> <br /> Not even the Risen from Wraith: The Oblivion rise for no reason; which pinpoints some minor, but understandable ignorance toward W:TO (which isn't surprising, considering how a miniscule amount of have actually read it) aswell. Every single Risen raises for a reason, even trying is extremely hazardous internally due how powered the Shadow can become. It's an ultimate gambit struggle to balance trying not to succumb to the Shadow, not tow the line or get caught by the Hierarchy, and trying to resolve *why* you raised in the first place.<br /> <br /> And the Wan Kuei are connected to the Low Umbra through Yin aspected Wan Kuei specifically. And the same breadth aswell, more Yang aspected Wan Kuei are more connected with the Spirit World. That's the beauty of KotE, with how dynamic it can be to traverse cosmologies.. stagnating it down to only one piece is nonsensical. </div> </div> </div>You could easily plug yang into the Astral instead of the Middle Umbra and have the Hungry Dead go to a High Umbral hell instead. The High Umbra even has elements of the underworld and living umbras already, with unpleasant reactions based on Rage. Seems like it would be custom made for holding that part of the setting as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T20:55:42-07:00","id":1445594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445519#post1445519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm too into Settites but yeah, in WoD (and I'm strictly speaking about WoD here, that needs to be emphasized, I'm not discussing RW christianity, now at least) , if the stories we're given can be believed, the god of judaism's is a massive prick who might as well be a Wyrm Incarnae. The Creator of the world's very mean.<br /> I'm surprised i've never read any setting that tries to drag Jesus down (apart from the obvious &quot;Jesus was one of us!&quot; nonsense that everyone wants to pull) (but of course there's that RW Gnotic belief that Jesus is a son of The One Above All and the guy in the old Testiment is just the Demiurge, or maybe folks just messed up big time with the concept of the trinity..)<br /> <br /> Honestly I've always imagined that a good chunk of what Garou consider Wyrm or not is subjective. Tribes are very opinionated after all. Red Talons probably think most human spirits are either Banes or the weaver equivolent (mechanical arthropods? Uh, should we call them bugs?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course its all an elaborate social experiment by the Pooka. I mean they said it and their book has to be true right? I mean.. there is a certain logic there plus nearly every god has some sort of animal symbolism... most blatantly among the Egyptians.<br /> <br /> I've honestly taken and run with that with Pooka Lore. Go all in as satire for the &quot;We were the real cause&quot; of history you get from vampire/mage/etc...<br /> <br /> I think i had the pooka history of vampires being &quot;once there were two brothers that One of us decided to mess with.. calling their glamour they appears to the two brothers &quot;I an the creator of the Universe... MAKE SACRIFICES TO ME.... BRING ME YOUR BEST SHIT OR SMITING!&quot;<br /> <br /> The elder brother brought the best of his crops... but as we all know you don't win friends with Salad.<br /> <br /> The Second brother slew his finest lamb and this pleased our carnivorous kin.<br /> <br /> The first brother seeing this got an idea and sometime later would approach the pooka with bloody meat &quot;I can do better this is the best I have..&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;is this people flesh?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well there's only like 4 people... 3 ;people...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No there's a whole bunch of other people did you think there was only just you and your parents and your brother?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah Kind of....&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait did you kill your brother?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He is the best I have..&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;NO WHAT THE FUCk IS WRONG WITH YOU CURSE CURSE CuRSE!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:02:18-07:00","id":1445603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1445508#post1445508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Patriarch\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Patriarch</a><br /> <br /> The Black Furies: 1st Edition Tribe Book gave the mythology of their tribe that the world of Gaia was once one of great peace, order, and women worship with humanity at peace among the sexes. Howeber, the Wyrm in the form of the Patriarch taught men to be jealous of women and crave their secret power to life as well as control wolves (it makes sense in context). The Patriarch eventually became the God of Western Mankind with it being the Wyrm Totem of Jealousy and Misogyny. It is behind why people worship it and the Wyrm rather than Gaia. It is, in Werewolf, the God of Abrahamic religion vs. other deities that are totems of Gaia or powerful spirits in the setting.<br /> <br /> Later, it got retconned into a Weaver Totem in The Book of the Weaver with the idea that religious faith is one of the pillars of how the Weaver controls mankind alongside science but a lot of people, particularly those who might be of a religious liberality, really hate the concept as a whole. I'm pretty flexible about how White Wolf treats my religion but this one just pisses me off for some reason, possibly because its so goddamn stupid.<br /> <br /> It gets discussed in 25 Years of Vampire: The Masquerade: <a href=\"https://www.buzzsprout.com/1171889/8129593-tribebook-black-furies-1st-edition-episode-19\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.buzzsprout.com/1171889/8...ion-episode-19</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Where it appears in the Book of the Weaver, it was a nearly never-seen Incarna (not a totem spirit; Weaver-Incarnae don't seem to sponsor many packs) folded under the Weaver's purview of Dogma. It seems to care more about conformity than anything else, as the book has a lengthy discussion of normalite fomori to underline Dogma not needing religion to function. Critically, it's also important to note that W:tA doesn't really have spirits that cap off entire human religions, though there might be a surprising array of spirits of all variaties that take turns trying to reach and nudge various religions' adherents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've always imagined that a good chunk of what Garou consider Wyrm or not is subjective. Tribes are very opinionated after all. Red Talons probably think most human spirits are either Banes or the weaver equivolent (mechanical arthropods? Uh, should we call them bugs?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not, in fact, subjective, but what resonates more deeply with any given member of the Triat can be misleading. Taint can be had as readily as in Shinto, and some Garou might use that as an excuse to kill first and cleanse later when it would have been perfectly possible (if difficult; you have to conceal the nature of a rite of cleansing to do it, which can be trying if someone doesn't like or doesn't respect the religion you're using as a cover) to scrub the target and send them on their way, with an expectation that they might never get tainted again. Red Talons belief, for instance, is well noted as having extremely low expectations for human activity and potential, viewing it as inevitable that they're going to do something execution-worthy, which might not even strictly be Wyrmish but more along the lines of an existential threat on par with compromising a caern or the Veil (such as killing or driving off wolves, which Garou cannot survive without; they will literally cease to exist the moment that wolves die off entirely). Yet, a number of branches have been surprised from time to time and stayed some variety of Red Talons while dialing down their willingness to kill humans on sight, such as the Kucha Ekundu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}